alted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T17:46:17-08:00","id":1287357,"title":"","content":"So like, in a non-aggressive way because I'm curious, who is Rei exactly? Someone's backer character?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T18:07:07-08:00","id":1287362,"title":"","content":"Hi, folks, Just here to explain the Rei thing. I'm in the Exalted Discord and in the lead-up hype for Lunars a lot of people were joking about #MakeReiCanon, as the backer intended to back at a level to canonize their character in the art. I thought it was a cute, funny, harmless meme (and still do) so I mentioned it to James Bell as a &quot;don't be surprised if this pops up in the comments&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> He decided to jokingly put it in the hashtags, and no harm was meant, no lifting up one person more than others, etc. Just having some silly fun with our fans. It could have been anyone who got the hashtag, and if there's any history/bad blood, I was unaware. Sorry it caused some weirdness in here, as I generally find the community to be super positive and fun, and don't want to take away from that. &lt;3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>In-House Developer for <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> and <b>Exalted </b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":22}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23832-dixiecyanide","name":"DixieCyanide","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T18:10:17-08:00","id":1287365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DixieCyanide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1287362#post1287362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi, folks, Just here to explain the Rei thing. I'm in the Exalted Discord and in the lead-up hype for Lunars a lot of people were joking about #MakeReiCanon, as the backer intended to back at a level to canonize their character in the art. I thought it was a cute, funny, harmless meme (and still do) so I mentioned it to James Bell as a &quot;don't be surprised if this pops up in the comments&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> He decided to jokingly put it in the hashtags, and no harm was meant, no lifting up one person more than others, etc. Just having some silly fun with our fans. It could have been anyone who got the hashtag, and if there's any history/bad blood, I was unaware. Sorry it caused some weirdness in here, as I generally find the community to be super positive and fun, and don't want to take away from that. &lt;3</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That sounds like something silly and harmless, and if the person is already planning on throwing enough money at things to make their character show up in the art, why are people getting all twisted up over it? *sigh*<br /> <br /> On a positive note, all the teasers before now did a great job actually making me excited for Lunars (They're my least favorite of the core splats) and goddamn, even just the fluff does NOT disappoint!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T18:14:41-08:00","id":1287368,"title":"","content":"Yeah that all sounds innocuous. A bit sad it turned into whatever that was.<br /> <br /> #MakeReiCanon","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T18:49:26-08:00","id":1287381,"title":"","content":"I winced a bit when the first Lunar elder description included the all-too-familiar phrase &quot;at the cost of several Sidereal lives&quot;, but was pleasantly surprised thereafter at how many of the Lunar-<br /> Sidereal engagements thereafter ended in mutual destruction rather than a slaughter in favor of Lunars, which I had feared would be the case. Thus far in general, the writing is living up to my high expectations of the 3E line, if not exceeding them.<br /> <br /> I am a bit concerned that the book is glossing over the costs of the Lunar vendetta against the Realm in favor of trying to portray them in a sympathetic light, but I'll reserve judgement on that until I see more of the previews. Other than that, I have nothing but good things to say. It just goes to show that even my least favorite splat can intrigue and delight me this edition, and I'm not sure what praise I can give that's higher than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/39-ysadrel","name":"ysadrel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T18:58:08-08:00","id":1287385,"title":"","content":"For the person who gets the cover art image. Please request a duck-billed platypus lunar in warform.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/977-major","name":"Major","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar977_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T19:16:44-08:00","id":1287387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ysadrel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1287381#post1287381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am a bit concerned that the book is glossing over the costs of the Lunar vendetta against the Realm in favor of trying to portray them in a sympathetic light, but I'll reserve judgement on that until I see more of the previews.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually that's interesting, because I think it's there, but it's a lot more subtle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T22:56:55-08:00","id":1287433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ysadrel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1287381#post1287381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I winced a bit when the first Lunar elder description included the all-too-familiar phrase &quot;at the cost of several Sidereal lives&quot;, but was pleasantly surprised thereafter at how many of the Lunar-<br /> Sidereal engagements thereafter ended in mutual destruction rather than a slaughter in favor of Lunars, which I had feared would be the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's not clear that the deaths of Radhika and her allies was as costly to the Lunars as to the Sidereals, then I'll need to revise that section post-editing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T23:31:36-08:00","id":1287438,"title":"","content":"I would say it needs more clarity, yeah. It reads to me like they had to zerg rush her down and the loss ratio was well in her favor.<br /> <br /> To be fair, I'd also advise seeking other opinions than mine; I got really tired of Sidereal death and incompetence by late 2E (my other least favorite Exalted phrase is &quot;...catching the Sidereals by surprise&quot;) so I may be overly sensitive to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/39-ysadrel","name":"ysadrel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T02:10:31-08:00","id":1287459,"title":"","content":"Given that Lunars are supposed to be the number 1 cause of sidereal mortality I expect to see more of it in here than anywhere else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T05:18:31-08:00","id":1287486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ysadrel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1287381#post1287381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I winced a bit when the first Lunar elder description included the all-too-familiar phrase &quot;at the cost of several Sidereal lives&quot;, but was pleasantly surprised thereafter at how many of the Lunar-<br /> Sidereal engagements thereafter ended in mutual destruction rather than a slaughter in favor of Lunars, which I had feared would be the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Too bad the same can't be said for Lunar-Dynast engagements. For a superpower, the Realm doesn't really seem to successfully do much of anything.<br /> <br /> Maybe The Realm will be the first book to portray the Realm as something other than Snidely-Whiplash-evil, baby-eating, murder machine of ineffectual incompetence... but I don't hold out much hope for that.<br /> <br /> I'm glad that the Lunar book hypes Lunars; I just wish that any book did the same for Dynasts and the Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","name":"Equitable Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T05:43:07-08:00","id":1287497,"title":"","content":"I think <i>being the only superpower in the world</i> is a bit of an achievement in and of itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T07:31:01-08:00","id":1287525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ysadrel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1287438#post1287438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say it needs more clarity, yeah. It reads to me like they had to zerg rush her down and the loss ratio was well in her favor.<br /> <br /> To be fair, I'd also advise seeking other opinions than mine; I got really tired of Sidereal death and incompetence by late 2E (my other least favorite Exalted phrase is &quot;...catching the Sidereals by surprise&quot;) so I may be overly sensitive to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it needs any clarification, I think that would be minor. After all, it says that several Sidereals took down Radhika <i>and her senior disciples</i>, also implied to be experienced Lunar disciples. And, as dev mentions, this sole act crystallized the Lunar's choice to pursue asymmetrical warfare.<br /> <br /> I personally like Sidereals over Lunars, but I don't think that there is any real bias here. The other major Lunar-Sidereal interaction described has a Lunar lasting all of <i>9 days</i>, using her bailiwick of shapestealshifting, against a Sidereals bailiwick of 'knowing how stuff is supposed to go'.<br /> <br /> I got the impression that the initial response to these was fairly pro-Lunar, perhaps exaggerated a bit for their viewpoint, but the honors between Lunars and Sidereals were just about even in a straight-up fight. The problem is that the Sidereals have this proxy army that tips the balance towards them while they can keep it focused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T13:40:45-08:00","id":1287655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1287486#post1287486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Too bad the same can't be said for Lunar-Dynast engagements. For a superpower, the Realm doesn't really seem to successfully do much of anything.<br /> <br /> Maybe The Realm will be the first book to portray the Realm as something other than Snidely-Whiplash-evil, baby-eating, murder machine of ineffectual incompetence... but I don't hold out much hope for that.<br /> <br /> I'm glad that the Lunar book hypes Lunars; I just wish that any book did the same for Dynasts and the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't get that sense myself. I mean, Ma-Ha-Suchi's entire character arc in teh book right now is &quot;We did all this fucking work <i>and it's still there</i>.&quot; And the geenral ability for the Realm to basically put a boot on the neck of Lunars for nearly eight centuries is a big motivating aspect to the entire Lunar like, thing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T14:16:22-08:00","id":1287668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1287486#post1287486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Too bad the same can't be said for Lunar-Dynast engagements. For a superpower, the Realm doesn't really seem to successfully do much of anything.<br /> <br /> Maybe The Realm will be the first book to portray the Realm as something other than Snidely-Whiplash-evil, baby-eating, murder machine of ineffectual incompetence... but I don't hold out much hope for that.<br /> <br /> I'm glad that the Lunar book hypes Lunars; I just wish that any book did the same for Dynasts and the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair the Realm is still to come, and <i>could </i>remedy this. <br /> <br /> That said seconded, for the moment. The Realm's portrayed as incompetent, underpowered and tearing itself apart rather than anything to be seriously feared. Lunars is hyping the elders and doing so really well, but it kinda drew into sharp relief for me how little WFHW really did to make the Dragon Blooded feel similarly badass. That was setting out facts, this is more the sales pitch. I'm absolutely a biased source on this, 'X vs the Realm' is a plothook I've never been sold on as a fun one, but... well, I haven't exactly had my mind changed yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T14:39:18-08:00","id":1287677,"title":"","content":"I admit that one line in the overall thing there made it feel a bit like the DBs are stuck as &quot;inevitably&quot; losing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> These strategies also played on the Empress\u2019 conservatism and obsession with perpetuating her rule. Knowing that overreach would play into Lunar hands, she slowed the Realm\u2019s expansion to a crawl, tolerated greater independence in troublesome satrapies, and grew more reluctant to embark upon grand endeavors \u2014 subjugating the Scavenger Lands, reclaiming Prasad,<br /> expanding Westward. </div> </div> </div>Now, the situation presented here isn't wrong. It's the keystone of how the Lunar strategy works. But the wording basically presents the Empress' overall response as holing up in the Realm's existing territories and not doing much of <i>anything</i> for fear that Lunar bogeymen will jump out of the shadows and wreck shit the minute she makes a risky play. Which is absolutely the attitude that some members of the Realm likely have, given the psychological warfare going on, but attributing the same to the Empress (versus, say &quot;biding her time until she could find a way to effectively engage them&quot; or something more active and befitting the kind of person that founded something like the Realm in the first place) makes it seem less like a contest between equal players rather than the current situation that doesn't seem to give the Realm any scenario in which their being able to substantially threaten the Pact is even an option.<br /> <br /> Now, the Realm is <i>the Realm</i>. We don't WANT them to win under current circumstances, obviously. But it does make it kinda painfully obvious that Raksi and Ma Ha Suchi did more to damage the Pact via in-fighting than the Realm seems likely to ever do even on a good century.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1817,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1817-opmegs","user":"OpMegs","date":". 02-13-2019, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1817-opmegs","name":"OpMegs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1817_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T14:56:22-08:00","id":1287686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OpMegs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1287677#post1287677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit that one line in the overall thing there made it feel a bit like the DBs are stuck as &quot;inevitably&quot; losing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, the situation presented here isn't wrong. It's the keystone of how the Lunar strategy works. But the wording basically presents the Empress' overall response as holing up in the Realm's existing territories and not doing much of <i>anything</i> for fear that Lunar bogeymen will jump out of the shadows and wreck shit the minute she makes a risky play. Which is absolutely the attitude that some members of the Realm likely have, given the psychological warfare going on, but attributing the same to the Empress (versus, say &quot;biding her time until she could find a way to effectively engage them&quot; or something more active and befitting the kind of person that founded something like the Realm in the first place) makes it seem less like a contest between equal players rather than the current situation that doesn't seem to give the Realm any scenario in which their being able to substantially threaten the Pact is even an option.<br /> <br /> Now, the Realm is <i>the Realm</i>. We don't WANT them to win under current circumstances, obviously. But it does make it kinda painfully obvious that Raksi and Ma Ha Suchi did more to damage the Pact via in-fighting than the Realm seems likely to ever do even on a good century.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prior material has painted the fall of Dragon-Blooded hegemony as somewhat inevitable - all of the wonders they use to maintain their empire will fail, the empire will crumble, and there isn't much, if anything, that can stem the tide, because they're squatting on stuff that Solars built for Solar use and persistent only by Solar maintenance. Short of forcing captured Solars to labor to maintain it, which is dangerous for a number of reasons, they're headed on a downward trajectory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T15:09:56-08:00","id":1287692,"title":"","content":"Before I read anything : Oh my gods they have a Nautilus totem Lunar. This is all I never knew I wanted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T15:30:14-08:00","id":1287708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LeTipex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1287692#post1287692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before I read anything : Oh my gods they have a Nautilus totem Lunar. This is all I never knew I wanted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their name is apparently Silent Pearl, as per the fiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T15:41:23-08:00","id":1287715,"title":"","content":"135K broken, hooray for 7 more animals in the bestiary!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T16:12:21-08:00","id":1287730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OpMegs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1287677#post1287677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, the situation presented here isn't wrong. It's the keystone of how the Lunar strategy works. But the wording basically presents the Empress' overall response as holing up in the Realm's existing territories and not doing much of <i>anything</i> for fear that Lunar bogeymen will jump out of the shadows and wreck shit the minute she makes a risky play. Which is absolutely the attitude that some members of the Realm likely have, given the psychological warfare going on, but attributing the same to the Empress (versus, say &quot;biding her time until she could find a way to effectively engage them&quot; or something more active and befitting the kind of person that founded something like the Realm in the first place) makes it seem less like a contest between equal players rather than the current situation that doesn't seem to give the Realm any scenario in which their being able to substantially threaten the Pact is even an option.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that probably without outside intervention, the Realm likely can't win against the Silver Pact. It's like fighting the Viet Cong or the Taliban, when they have the perfect hiding spots of their underground networks to retreat to. Except it's even worse than either of those cases because the Lunars are so crazy smart, powerful and adaptable. Make no mistake, the Lunars are winning this war, slowly. On the other hand the Viet Cong never really had a chance in hell of invading the US either.<br /> <br /> The Lunar book actually does a really good job of showing that, I think. Every time somebody decides that they're going to take on the Empire and finish it off once and for all, they get smashed by it's armies. What a relief it is, I imagine, for the Realm generals to finally have a pitched battle to fight when that does happen.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T16:43:16-08:00","id":1287753,"title":"","content":"Hmm... At root, someone has to be winning. It's not so bad for the status quo implied by the books for it to be the Lunars (esp. through imperfect knowledge, authorial slant, etc.).<br /> <br /> Now, within that it <i>is </i>bad if this is implied that the Lunars are predestined to win because, well, they're superior Celestial Exalted, and / or there's really nothing the mere Dragonblooded of the Realm can do to reform or adapt to counter their flawless super strategy while remaining recognizably an empire. That really sucks.<br /> <br /> But &quot;The Lunars will, eventually, win, *if* and only if the Realm remains as sclerotically structurally flawed as it currently is (and they don't make any changes on the Lunar side that messes anything up, and no third party factors intrude!)&quot; is less a setting problem than a positive feature providing incentive for PC Realm Dragonblooded to rise to the challenge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T17:01:14-08:00","id":1287759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1287753#post1287753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... At root, someone has to be winning. It's not so bad for the status quo implied by the books for it to be the Lunars (esp. through imperfect knowledge, authorial slant, etc.).<br /> <br /> Now, within that it <i>is </i>bad if this is implied that the Lunars are predestined to win because, well, they're superior Celestial Exalted, and / or there's really nothing the mere Dragonblooded of the Realm can do to reform or adapt to counter their flawless super strategy while remaining recognizably an empire. That really sucks.<br /> <br /> But &quot;The Lunars will, eventually, win, *if* and only if the Realm remains as sclerotically structurally flawed as it currently is (and they don't make any changes on the Lunar side that messes anything up, and no third party factors intrude!)&quot; is less a setting problem than a positive feature providing incentive for PC Realm Dragonblooded to rise to the challenge.</div> </div> </div> </div>The certainty and inevitability of Lunar victory is meant to be presented as a subjective belief on the part of the Lunars rather than an objective statement about the future of the setting. Please point out any examples of the latter so we can address them in post-editing development. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T17:22:47-08:00","id":1287768,"title":"","content":"Wow, big jump and we have gone through 145K. Welcome to the book Leviathan, Aum-Ashatra; Aqadar; and Smiling Zamisha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T19:13:42-08:00","id":1287799,"title":"","content":"The $175,000 stretch goal are four new animal MA styles for the Companion!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T23:26:45-08:00","id":1287871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LeTipex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1287692#post1287692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before I read anything : Oh my gods they have a Nautilus totem Lunar. This is all I never knew I wanted.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're the No Moon signature character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T06:08:44-08:00","id":1287916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1287730#post1287730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that probably without outside intervention, the Realm likely can't win against the Silver Pact. It's like fighting the Viet Cong or the Taliban, when they have the perfect hiding spots of their underground networks to retreat to. Except it's even worse than either of those cases because the Lunars are so crazy smart, powerful and adaptable. Make no mistake, the Lunars are winning this war, slowly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, retraction in this. I thought since there was no way for the Realm to actually win the war, that eventually the Lunars must win it. I didn\u2019t really consider that the Realm might have a win condition in that they just deal with the Silver Pact basically forever. <br /> <br /> Right now with the crazy amount of infighting and civil war and stuff going on in the Realm, plus the fact that they\u2019ve got a lot more than just Lunars to deal with, opens up the possibility that the Pact may have to change tactics. There\u2019s a good chance that a unified Empire might just be able to keep them at bay, which can add an urgency to the current climate. Before the civil war starts and ends, and the Realm possibly reunifies is the perfect time to strike while the iron is hot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T06:37:47-08:00","id":1287919,"title":"","content":"I think that the books portray very clearly (and <i>well</i>) that all of Creation balances on a razor's edge. The Lunars' asymmetrical warfare policy <i>will</i> win... against the Realm's current fragmented state. The reason the current age is referred to as the Time of Tumult (which I've always thought of <i>post hoc</i> naming) is that there are no longer any 'safe' options... for anyone.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded: They are currently a nuclear reactor going into meltdown because the control rod (the Scarlet Empress) has been removed from the equation. The Dynasty realizes that internal (internecine?) squabbling can only serve the Realm's enemies, but they can't agree on the right action to take, and the system the Scarlet Empress set up deliberately has this problem. So there is a Tragedy-of-the-Commons situation in the Dynasty. Every House would <i>prefer</i> to deal with external threats to Realm power first and their power second, because if the Realm doesn't survive, neither does their power. However, doing this risks another House taking over and destroying others' power bases, and so they all squabble over power.<br /> <br /> Lunars: The basic question facing the Silver Pact: do they push, or not push? Each has their risks, and the Lunars are too smart to naively believe one way is 'safe'. It could be that pushing will work, because if they do not push then the Realm will have time to reestablish central authority and turn all of their attention back to the<i> status quo ante</i>. But it's possible that pushing will not work, because it will give the Realm the external threat without which they will tear themselves to pieces. So what do the Lunars do?<br /> <br /> Sidereals: There are huge upheavals in the Five-Score Fellowship. Their <i>princeps senatus</i> is about to die. Their chief proxy in Creation (the Realm) is dulling themselves fighting each other, which lowers their effectiveness. Their breaking of the Mask basically prevents direct rule, so they must have a proxy, and the best proxy in terms of power after the DB are the Lunars, and that's basically an impossible position without Sauron-level manipulation. To make matters worse, the return of the Solars is causing a resurgence of the Gold Faction, and real dissension in the Fellowship is starting to come back because of this. Speaking of...<br /> <br /> Solars: This is the huge wild card. Exalts of unsurpassed power with, effectively, <i>no direct stake</i> in the current power structure and nowhere to fit in said structure. The finely-tuned yet precarious equilibrium of the Empress's reign over Creation has just been shattered. I'm not going to say that the Solars are the sole protagonists in the story of the Time of Tumult, but none of the other Exalts can really afford to overlook them, and their power does lend them to tipping the balance in any given direction.<br /> <br /> This is the reality of the Time of Tumult. Decisions are going to be made, for better or worse, and nearly every decision can be defended rationally. The Silver Pact could decide to do their best to exterminate the Solars themselves, no matter how personally painful that might be. After all, a couple more Bulls of the North, and the Dynasty might actually start paying more attention to something more than the mirror palace of the Realm. And so on...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T08:42:00-08:00","id":1287951,"title":"","content":"The Scarlet Dynasty COULD have defeated the Lunar Exalted by now (or at least done far better at fighting them), if the Scarlet Empress hadn't been so obsessed with making sure she was never replaced. The first priority of the Scarlet Empire was keeping the Scarlet Empress in power. Conquering the world and killing Anathema were only methods to achieve that goal, rather than the primary goals themselves, and so were not pursued as efficiently as possible.<br /> <br /> Had she built a system where the Dragon-Blooded could more effectively rule themselves even without her, she likely wouldn't have remained in power as long as she did, because she could be replaced without a major hiccup.<br /> <br /> Of course, that does open up the question of what happens with the next person to gain control of the Imperial Palace and the Sword of Creation. Was the Scarlet Empress' obsession with remaining in control ultimately about herself, or some desire to protect Creation from something she feared they could not control? That's the sort of question the books leave deliberately open-ended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 02-14-2019, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T08:55:56-08:00","id":1287958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1287951#post1287951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Scarlet Dynasty COULD have defeated the Lunar Exalted by now (or at least done far better at fighting them), if the Scarlet Empress hadn't been so obsessed with making sure she was never replaced. The first priority of the Scarlet Empire was keeping the Scarlet Empress in power. Conquering the world and killing Anathema were only methods to achieve that goal, rather than the primary goals themselves, and so were not pursued as efficiently as possible.<br /> <br /> Had she built a system where the Dragon-Blooded could more effectively rule themselves even without her, she likely wouldn't have remained in power as long as she did, because she could be replaced without a major hiccup.<br /> <br /> Of course, that does open up the question of what happens with the next person to gain control of the Imperial Palace and the Sword of Creation. Was the Scarlet Empress' obsession with remaining in control ultimately about herself, or some desire to protect Creation from something she feared they could not control? That's the sort of question the books leave deliberately open-ended.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is a bit unfair to Her Redness. (I almost can't believe I said that.) It is certainly possible that the Scarlet Empress is more focused on maintaining her control than the Realm as a whole for selfish reasons. But consider her history.<br /> <br /> How did she become the Scarlet Empress? Because she was able to deal with the problems that no one else could. In a world literally teetering on annihilation, she who would become the Scarlet Empress--and <i>only</i> her--successfully stabilized Creation. She has <i>prima facie</i> evidence that she knows best. She, unlike so many others, is not a puppet of the Sidereals but their equal. Or, if a puppet, a puppet who <i>knows</i> her value and can treat with them as someone with intrinsic value, and that is very rare for a Terrestrial Exalt to be able to do with elder Celestial Exalts.<br /> <br /> I don't think the Scarlet Empress is scared of any successor gaining control of the nuclear football. I am very much of the opinion that the nuclear football is more or less permanently offline, or that the Scarlet Empress will have arranged that to occur if anything happened to her. But it is very arguable that she is not self-absorbed so much as she is utterly convinced--for the reasons given above--that she <i>is</i> that critical to Creation's survival. Her machinations to make the Realm fall apart if anything happened to her was not a manifestation of megalomania, but an insurance policy that the Dynasty--who did not carry the burdens she did--would not try to overthrow her.<br /> <br /> I do agree with your original premise, though. I don't think any group of Celestial Exalts would survive against a united Dragon-Blooded attack. <i>Maybe</i> if the Solars and Lunars banded together, as the Usurpation implies that the DB Host required the assistance of the Sidereals to overcome their might. But then recall that (presumably similarly to earlier editions) roughly half of the Solars have been corrupted in various ways. But yeah, if I had to bet on any Exalt type vs. any other Exalt type, as they are in the Time of Tumult, I would have to bet on the DBs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T14:01:48-08:00","id":1288064,"title":"","content":"In an OC brawl where every exalt of each type banded together to fight other OC bands I'd bet on the Dragon Blooded to. There are roughly 25,000 of them, after all. Hell, I'd probably bet on them even if the Lunars, Sidereal, and Solars/abyssals/infernals banded together because that would still mean each individual celestial exalt had to on average take out 25 dragon blooded to win. So long as they don't send out newly hatched eggs that exalted yesterday I'd wager even a first age elder celestial is going to have a bad day if they need to fight 25 dragon blooded by themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 02-15-2019, 02:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T20:55:00-08:00","id":1288161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1287486#post1287486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Too bad the same can't be said for Lunar-Dynast engagements. For a superpower, the Realm doesn't really seem to successfully do much of anything.<br /> <br /> Maybe The Realm will be the first book to portray the Realm as something other than Snidely-Whiplash-evil, baby-eating, murder machine of ineffectual incompetence... but I don't hold out much hope for that.<br /> <br /> I'm glad that the Lunar book hypes Lunars; I just wish that any book did the same for Dynasts and the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem here is twofold. First, Empires are baby eating murder machines and the Realm is only different in that the boot on the neck of the world has an elemental demigod\u2019s foot in it.<br /> <br /> Second, due to the vanishing of the Scarlet Empress, the Realm is losing cohesion and competence by the day.<br /> <br /> So, if that\u2019s your takeway, well... yes, that\u2019s the current state of affairs. Thirty years ago, the Realm was an amazing juggernaut, using the horrifying things it did to fund great (but usually not good) things and allow a class of demigods to live in luxury undreamt of by most of the world. And it kept its bottom line safe by arranging for some degree or order to be maintained in those areas where it held sway.<br /> <br /> Now, it still does that first part, but the order has fallen by the wayside in favor of more taxes to fund bigger armies that will be used on internal targets.<br /> <br /> I do think the Realm book will have some amazing and great (possibly even some good) things in it, but I don\u2019t think they\u2019ll stop pointing out all the terrible stuff the Realm does along the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T05:23:52-08:00","id":1288226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288161#post1288161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem here is twofold. First, Empires are baby eating murder machines and the Realm is only different in that the boot on the neck of the world has an elemental demigod\u2019s foot in it.<br /> <br /> Second, due to the vanishing of the Scarlet Empress, the Realm is losing cohesion and competence by the day.<br /> <br /> So, if that\u2019s your takeway, well... yes, that\u2019s the current state of affairs. Thirty years ago, the Realm was an amazing juggernaut, using the horrifying things it did to fund great (but usually not good) things and allow a class of demigods to live in luxury undreamt of by most of the world. And it kept its bottom line safe by arranging for some degree or order to be maintained in those areas where it held sway.<br /> <br /> Now, it still does that first part, but the order has fallen by the wayside in favor of more taxes to fund bigger armies that will be used on internal targets.<br /> <br /> I do think the Realm book will have some amazing and great (possibly even some good) things in it, but I don\u2019t think they\u2019ll stop pointing out all the terrible stuff the Realm does along the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>With respect, while you are articulating the forum orthodoxy on the subject, and doing so quite well, the answer begs the question.<br /> <br /> In the first instance, empires (or Empires, as they're often called on the forum) in Exalted are whatever the writers say they are; there is nothing inevitable about them or their nature in the fiction. The point that I would make is that the Realm <i>could</i> have been written in such a way that there would be interesting moral and pragmatic questions about Solars/Lunars destroying it or Dynasts restoring/reforming it; not doing so in favor of baby-eating murder machine of evil incompetence was a choice. I don't write RPGs for a living, so maybe evil-empire Realm is the best for the game line; I just don't think much of it personally.<br /> <br /> I recognize that I'm very much in the minority on the forums, and I'm not trying to convince anyone to see it the way I do. The Realm just strikes me as a missed opportunity in the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","name":"Equitable Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T06:01:32-08:00","id":1288233,"title":"","content":"If an empire wasn\u2019t a baby eating machine, then it wouldn\u2019t be an empire.<br /> <br /> You\u2019re effectively complaining that we\u2019re calling a system of hereditary rulership with just one ruler at a time a \u201cmonarchy\u201d. That is what the word means. Words mean things.<br /> <br /> Grass is grass; it is a plant that consumes light and water to grow. That is how plants work, and Creation is not meant to be so fantastic that plants work any differently.<br /> <br /> So too empires. An empire which does not operate or behave like an empire would need to be called something else, appropriate to how it operates and behaves.<br /> <br /> Imperialism is all about conquering one\u2019s neighbors to serve oneself. Nazism was imperial.<br /> <br /> There is no particular word, so far as I know, for \u201cleave your neighbors to manage their own affairs so that you could each concentrate on building up your own assets and then seek trade with each other.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPeacefulness\u201d, I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T06:06:42-08:00","id":1288234,"title":"","content":"Well, if we\u2019re talking about literal baby eating, the Realm is never said to do that while Raksi does it all the time. Maybe not herself but still. I think the Lunar book is doing a pretty great job so far of making you go \u201cYeah that sounds pretty-wait, hold up. That\u2019s kind of horrible too isn\u2019t it?\u201d But it\u2019s doing it in a way that shows there are still a lot of really well meaning idealists, and a lot of the really bad stuff that the older rebels do is half justified and half driven by several lifetimes of murder and pain. The Lunars also can\u2019t be the bad guys of their own book, because that would suck, so you\u2019ve gotta read between the lines a little.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T06:12:36-08:00","id":1288235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288233#post1288233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no particular word, so far as I know, for \u201cleave your neighbors to manage their own affairs so that you could each concentrate on building up your own assets and then seek trade with each other.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPeacefulness\u201d, I suppose.</div> </div> </div> </div>The treaty of Westphalia?<br /> <br /> (Of course, that only applies to your neighbours and other areas ruled by governments you recognise.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T06:23:32-08:00","id":1288238,"title":"","content":"Um, why are empires <i>essentially</i> 'baby eating machines'? This is asserted without any discussion. I won't dispute that many if not most empires have been so; is that an essential part of them? This is quite a poor argument.<br /> <br /> As far as the larger concern, the Realm is full of moral dilemmas. Of all the Exalt types, Dragon-Bloods are the ones least affected by the Great Curse, and <i>likely</i> if the Great Curse deals with the Exalts as type, the larger the number of DBs, the less impact the Curse has on any given member. This translates to the Dragon-Bloods being the Exalt who can, actually, create the most <i>stable</i> Creation-spanning government. It is very likely the case that the ideal state structure for Creation as it stands in the wake of the Great Curse would invert the First Age's structure: the Dragon-Bloods are <i>on top</i>, and the Lunars/Solars/Sidereals/others are all troubleshooters for issues too large for local DBs to deal with.<br /> <br /> That is the true glory of the Host. The problem with the DBs is that it requires unity of a much larger group than the other Exalts. The Scarlet Empress's Realm IS an evil empire; that is basically uncontested. It is very possibly a pragmatic 'this is what I had to do' evil, but its excesses are unnecessary and surrender the moral high ground.<br /> <br /> But the Empress is gone, and the Realm is going to implode without extraordinary measures. What part of this limits meaningful decisions on the part of the DBs? If anything, the Empress's control was what limited true discussions of moral character.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T06:38:11-08:00","id":1288241,"title":"","content":"Empires are nations that use armies to take over other nations. They might rationalize this, claiming it\u2019s \u201cfor that other nations own good\u201d or whatever, but the reason is usually because the other nation has something the empire wants: more land, food, natural resources, slaves, etc. <br /> <br /> Invading other sovereign nations and taking them over is usually seen as evil by most people, so...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T07:00:59-08:00","id":1288247,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure that a hierarchy based on noble blood (even if it really does make you superior to the common man) is the most ideal state structure for Creation.<br /> I'm not sure a world-spanning Empire is the most ideal state structure for an entire world.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Which doesn't, of course, mean Dragonblood have to be evil, or that a society that prominently features Dragonblood amongst its upper levels has to be evil.<br /> <br /> Lookshy isn't wonderful, it, like most states with a strong military, takes dubious actions, but it's not the invader and oppressor that the Realm is. Obviously the Realm doesn't have to go around invading places, it's a choice the Dynasty has made.<br /> <br /> But to be an <i>Empire</i> (as opposed to a federation, coalition, trading bloc, or nation-state) does involve taking over other countries, which involves violence or other dubious means, because nations don't generally let themselves get taken over. And that involves killing babies (I don't know why people keep focusing on the babies, it's not okay to kill adults either).<br /> <br /> That's why the British Empire was, well, an Empire, whereas the USA is a federation.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, that doesn't mean you can't have stories of the Realm defending territories from rampaging beastmen or Fair Folk or anathema. But... is that not mentioned in WFHW?<br /> Either way, I kind of feel that WFHW isn't the one to judge it on, but rather The Realm.<br /> <br /> That'll have examples of a number of Satrapies, so that's the one to look at to see if they present it as &quot;The Realm conquered this satrapy, and many people would like to be independent again due to the taxes and religious oppression, but the Immaculate Monastery did at least turf out the volcano god who demanded human sacrifice,&quot; or as &quot;100% of people in this Satrapy hates the Realm because Realm soldiers murdered their babies.&quot;<br /> <br /> I very much doubt it'll be a case of &quot;everyone loves the Realm in this satrapy,&quot; but that would be unrealistic.*<br /> <br /> *There are of course, many places that, generally not initially but eventually, quite liked being part of an Empire. Britain, for example, ended up as one of Rome's most loyal and best-assimilated far provinces.<br /> But these are places that are either colonies (Canada, New Zealand, etc) or which are integrated and assimilated, so the people see themselves as part of the Empire, unlike their barbarian ancestors.<br /> The Realm doesn't colonise much, and nor does it really try and integrate foreign lands into it. The people in Satrapies are not taught to be Realm citizens, and they do not gain the rights of Realm citizens. They are forever second-class, and that's the kind of thing that makes conquered lands unhappy. And unhappy lands rebel, and so can only be controlled via violence.<br /> And thus we get back to killing people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T07:25:03-08:00","id":1288253,"title":"","content":"What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar226_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"226\" data-vbnamecard=\"226\">BrilliantRain</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2402_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2402\" data-vbnamecard=\"2402\">The Wizard of Oz</a> said.<br /> <br /> Imperialism is slavery. It is one man breaking into his neighbor's house and taking anything he wants, and the neighbor can't stop him because the thief is better at violence. &quot;You work, and I eat,&quot; as Abraham Lincoln defined slavery and tyranny.<br /> <br /> The Scarlet Dynasty doesn't have to be an empire. Instead of devoting resources to building and maintaining a war machine for conquering and occupying its neighbors, it could focus those resources on building its own assets, and then trading those assets to its neighbors in return for assets that they are better at producing.<br /> <br /> But the Dynasty wants to take more than it produces. It wants to gain more than it gives. It is a thief and a vampire. That's what it means to be an empire rather than just a kingdom or a nation or a state, or a voluntary federation of states.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T07:31:41-08:00","id":1288254,"title":"","content":"On the other hand of course, that doesn't mean that every individual within the Realm has to be presented as evil. There's a reason Empires use propaganda to justify their conquests, even on their own people; the citizens of the Empire can be fooled into thinking that their glorious Empire is helping the benighted savages.<br /> <br /> Plus, monolithically evil bad guys are dullllll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T07:45:03-08:00","id":1288258,"title":"","content":"Ehhhhh the native peoples of Canada are still pretty sour about the whole invasion-genocide thing. Suicide is up, crime is up, police distrust is high, even now. We\u2019re trying to fix it but it\u2019s not easy. <br /> <br /> There are also some really hard problems like a massive energy sector project, a few of them, that are set to run through native territory that didn\u2019t get proper approval. The projects aren\u2019t well received by many of the First Nations they go through, either because the natives want fair compensation or because oil extraction and transport harms the environment in a myriad of ways. Or both. This is all made even worse by the fact that yes we need alternative energy sources, but the fastest way to get them is to drive towards it with a strong economy, so just stopping as fast as possible isn\u2019t an option. Not to mention the quality of life hit that everyone would take. But you can\u2019t fall into the trap of using that as an excuse to just not deal with the problem and keep harvesting/burning oil either. It\u2019s a bloody mess. Now we have federal police clashing with native protestors too so that\u2019s great.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway enough about Canadian politics, although that actually sounds like it COULD be inspiration for a plot in exalted, couldn\u2019t it? Replace oil pipeline with jade caravans or some such, and pretty bloodless police clashes with bloody Lunar assaults and brutal Realm crackdowns. You could even keep some of the diplomacy in there as I\u2019m sure as ready and willing as the Realm is to commit a legion to surprising a rebellion the best option is just to not have one in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T08:07:49-08:00","id":1288261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288258#post1288258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ehhhhh the native peoples of Canada are still pretty sour about the whole invasion-genocide thing. Suicide is up, crime is up, police distrust is high, even now. We\u2019re trying to fix it but it\u2019s not easy.<br /> <br /> There are also some really hard problems like a massive energy sector project, a few of them, that are set to run through native territory that didn\u2019t get proper approval. The projects aren\u2019t well received by many of the First Nations they go through, either because the natives want fair compensation or because oil extraction and transport harms the environment in a myriad of ways. Or both. This is all made even worse by the fact that yes we need alternative energy sources, but the fastest way to get them is to drive towards it with a strong economy, so just stopping as fast as possible isn\u2019t an option. Not to mention the quality of life hit that everyone would take. But you can\u2019t fall into the trap of using that as an excuse to just not deal with the problem and keep harvesting/burning oil either. It\u2019s a bloody mess. Now we have federal police clashing with native protestors too so that\u2019s great.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway enough about Canadian politics, although that actually sounds like it COULD be inspiration for a plot in exalted, couldn\u2019t it? Replace oil pipeline with jade caravans or some such, and pretty bloodless police clashes with bloody Lunar assaults and brutal Realm crackdowns. You could even keep some of the diplomacy in there as I\u2019m sure as ready and willing as the Realm is to commit a legion to surprising a rebellion the best option is just to not have one in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>SOMETIMES the best option is to not have a rebellion. If you can give away some minor things as a sop to the people who might rebel without having to change anything important, ok, fine. On the other hand, if you can get all the revolutionaries to do something horrible that you can use as a pretext to have them all executed/jailed and the remaining people are &quot;pacified,&quot; also fine.<br /> <br /> And some Lunars might prefer the second option too, so they have some Martyrs that they can use to rally the people around and kick out the Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T08:13:07-08:00","id":1288263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288258#post1288258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ehhhhh the native peoples of Canada are still pretty sour about the whole invasion-genocide thing. Suicide is up, crime is up, police distrust is high, even now. We\u2019re trying to fix it but it\u2019s not easy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I know. Same with Australian aborigines, Maori, etc.<br /> <br /> I meant the colonists. My point was that most, say, Australians have an okayish view of the British Empire (not perfect, but good enough that they've still got the Queen), because most of them are not descended from the victims of the Empire, they're descended from the colonists. Similarly, if you go to Northern Ireland, there are large areas (not as much of it as 100 years ago, but still very large portions) where many people are way more overt in British patriotism than Britain is (to an extent that seems, frankly, a bit weird to us), because they are descended from English and Scottish settlers, not Irish people.<br /> <br /> My point was that you can't go to, say, the Canadian parliament and use the fact there's no great move to ditch the Queen as proof that Empires are popular, since most Canadian MPs are descended from British people anyway.<br /> <br /> I probably could have been more precise in my description, sorry.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T08:18:12-08:00","id":1288264,"title":"","content":"I might point out that all of the definitions of 'empire' given in this thread are <i>military</i> empires. There are other kinds of empires: economic and cultural are two others. Are those also inherently evil to the point of evoking 'baby eating' imagery?<br /> <br /> I will also point out that the idea of invading other people (for limited purposes), otherwise known as how people mainly warred before the 20th century, was not the 'ultimate expression of evil' that people today view it to be. IOW, 'war as inherently evil' is a <i>very</i> modern view of war, and digging into this is likely to create a huge discussion about all kinds of topics people generally avoid in forums not devoted to those subjects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'm not sure that a hierarchy based on noble blood (even if it really does make you superior to the common man) is the most ideal state structure for Creation.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'm not sure a world-spanning Empire is the most ideal state structure for an entire world.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div> <div align=\"left\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'd like to address this point a little more specifically. I'm not claiming that the <i>current</i> DB power structure, as the Realm or indeed of an aristocratic state in general, is the most ideal state structure for Creation. I'm just pointing out that due to setting conceits (specifically the Great Curse) the Exalt type that is most likely to create a stable order is the one that suffers from the Great Curse the least. AFAIK, that is the DBs.<br /> <br /> I can make RL comparisons to a very well-known metaphysical doctrine, but again, don't want to derail the thread.<br /> <br /> Edit: </span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Similarly, if you go to Northern Ireland, there are large areas (not as much of it as 100 years ago, but still very large portions) where many people are way more overt in British patriotism than Britain is (to an extent that seems, frankly, a bit weird to us), because they are descended from English and Scottish settlers, not Irish people</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Converts are nearly always more zealous than those raised to a belief system.</span></span></span></div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T08:19:50-08:00","id":1288265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288254#post1288254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand of course, that doesn't mean that every individual within the Realm has to be presented as evil. There's a reason Empires use propaganda to justify their conquests, even on their own people; the citizens of the Empire can be fooled into thinking that their glorious Empire is helping the benighted savages.<br /> <br /> Plus, monolithically evil bad guys are dullllll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though that said, very good people can buy into pretty evil propoganda. Just read stuff on African Colonialism or Amerinidan relocaiton or the Stain and things get pretty nasty really. The US was brought-up as a non-empire but seeing its treatment of Latin America since the Monroe Doctrine and the forced relocation of native peoples, it kind of does fit the bill. It just happens to also be a colonizing one wihtin its own borders.<br /> <br /> And a lot of it was done with an idea of bettering the lands or people. Or just the land, by getting rid of the people there already as often teh case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T08:21:49-08:00","id":1288267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288261#post1288261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> SOMETIMES the best option is to not have a rebellion. If you can give away some minor things as a sop to the people who might rebel without having to change anything important, ok, fine. On the other hand, if you can get all the revolutionaries to do something horrible that you can use as a pretext to have them all executed/jailed and the remaining people are &quot;pacified,&quot; also fine.<br /> <br /> And some Lunars might prefer the second option too, so they have some Martyrs that they can use to rally the people around and kick out the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, or the empire could even pick sides in a local conflict or using local power structures. The Lunar book says a much when it talks about how her Redness had to slow her expansion and allow boarder territories more autonomy and stuff. Your local tyrant might actually be a Realm proxy, backed by imperial power but you\u2019re not going to see a legion necessarily. <br /> <br /> If for no other reason than it\u2019s really boring to have Dynasts who weave an unparalleled web of lies, loyalties, passions, and favours at home to suddenly turn into exclusively the brute squad abroad. Totally use the brute squad, but also be a charming snake about it sometimes too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288263#post1288263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point was that you can't go to, say, the Canadian parliament and use the fact there's no great move to ditch the Queen as proof that Empires are popular, since most Canadian MPs are descended from British people anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Queen is a damned treasure and you better believe it. For Queen and country we\u2019ll show \u2018em the might of the commonwealth in no uncertain terms","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T08:30:28-08:00","id":1288269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288264#post1288264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might point out that all of the definitions of 'empire' given in this thread are <i>military</i> empires. There are other kinds of empires: economic and cultural are two others. Are those also inherently evil to the point of evoking 'baby eating' imagery?</div> </div> </div> </div>The US treatment of the Americas in the 19th and 20th Century, as well as some of the ways that imposed land distribution was implemented to native lands, kind of push me to say...yes actually. Economic empires are often built on ecnomic exploitationa nd dependence. Cultural empire is often done with a large chunk of cultural eradication in the process, especially when done purposefully as was done by the Spanish, British, and the United States.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288264#post1288264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will also point out that the idea of invading other people (for limited purposes), otherwise known as how people mainly warred before the 20th century, was not the 'ultimate expression of evil' that people today view it to be. IOW, 'war as inherently evil' is a <i>very</i> modern view of war, and digging into this is likely to create a huge discussion about all kinds of topics people generally avoid in forums not devoted to those subjects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, depends here. There's a reason cultural relativism is kind of something brought up in the first couple weeks of any ethics course ever. Naively saying &quot;Well it was fine in the past&quot; is a non-starter for most things. And there folks in variosu parts of the world and history who viewed war differently, and total war and genocide very differently. Just because war was common, war for utter dominaiton, conquest, or displacement of other peoples was not how or why ever war was fought.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288264#post1288264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[COLOR=#252c2f][FONT=Helvetica][SIZE=13px]I'd like to address this point a little more specifically. I'm not claiming that the <i>current</i> DB power structure, as the Realm or indeed of an aristocratic state in general, is the most ideal state structure for Creation. I'm just pointing out that due to setting conceits (specifically the Great Curse) the Exalt type that is most likely to create a stable order is the one that suffers from the Great Curse the least. AFAIK, that is the DBs.</div> </div> </div> </div>This kind of seems then like everyone's screwed since the Shogunate was a failure and the Realm operats through tyranical territorial empire. But I think that while the Great Curse is there, it exasperates the problems of the human condition, not replaces them. And that they have a elss indivdiually mechancially extreme Great Cruse, there are more of them, it's still there, and it's still people being able to be assholes by being people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T08:38:26-08:00","id":1288270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288263#post1288263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Australians have an okayish view of the British Empire (not perfect, but good enough that they've still got the Queen), because most of them are not descended from the victims of the Empire, they're descended from the colonists</div> </div> </div> </div>Meanwhile, you have Americans, who are also descended from British colonists, and so have a different opinion on European colonization of the New World than the Native Americans do, even though the American colonists came to hate the British empire enough to fight a war for independence. Then the United States of America later ignored its founding principles and became an imperial colonizing force against the remaining Native Americans, and probably also the people living around what would become the Panama Canal.<br /> <br /> Every country that could behave imperially HAS committed the sins of imperialism at some point, for some time, to some degree. That's just the nature of human evil. Even when a country isn't being an outright empire with the threat of force, still they will use their greater economic power to tip the scales of negotiation in their favor.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T09:05:43-08:00","id":1288280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288264#post1288264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are other kinds of empires: economic and cultural are two others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are there? Because I think we use those metaphorically.<br /> I could say that the USA is a &quot;cultural Empire&quot; and you'll understand what I mean... but it isn't really. America might exert cultural influence over Britain, but that doesn't lead to political control of Britain.<br /> Similarly, some people say the EU is just Germany's economic empire, but this is hyperbole.<br /> Unless you're thinking of something different?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I will also point out that the idea of invading other people (for limited purposes), otherwise known as how people mainly warred before the 20th century, was not the 'ultimate expression of evil' that people today view it to be. </div> </div> </div>I don't consider it be the <i>ultimate</i> expression of evil. And I don't think most people today actually do. (If they did, no democratic nation would ever declare war on other countries. Yet they sometimes do.) Like, genocide is worse, for example.<br /> <br /> But even in, say, the middle ages (which obviously was full of war), most ordinary people thought that invading another country just to conquer them was, not, actually, cool.<br /> That's why the French Church spent 100 years trying to get knights to swear to keep the peace, before giving up because it simply didn't work. (So instead they came up with Just War, Chivalry, and the Crusades.)<br /> It's also why most wars actually had some kind of &quot;justification&quot;. Maybe the King just wanted to grab more land, but he'd tell everyone that he had a claim, or that the other side started it, or the enemy were heretics, or whatever. Take the Albeginsian Crusade; yes, probably the King and some nobles just wanted to seize land in southern France. But they didn't say &quot;we're going to do some conquering because invading is totally cool&quot;, they said &quot;the poor people of Southern France are being corrupted by monstrous heretics who hate our Holy Mother Church! We have to save southern France, and force is our only option!&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course, I'm not sure this is actually relevant. People were complaining that, in their view, WFHW depicts the Realm as an Empire that loves invading stuff, and they think this makes it eeevvvilll in a boring way. Saying that people in the setting may not find it so objectionable* doesn't mean players don't find it as objectionable.<br /> <br /> *In general, people being invaded find it much more objectionable than the people doing the invading, in any era.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd like to address this point a little more specifically. I'm not claiming that the <i>current</i> DB power structure, as the Realm or indeed of an aristocratic state in general, is the most ideal state structure for Creation. I'm just pointing out that due to setting conceits (specifically the Great Curse) the Exalt type that is most likely to create a stable order is the one that suffers from the Great Curse the least. AFAIK, that is the DBs. </div> </div> </div>Ah, okay, that makes more sense.<br /> <br /> But they are still, inherently, an Exalt type based on hereditary, and that's likely to produce an aristocratic state.<br /> <br /> It can of course be stable... but the inherent randomness of Dragonblood Exaltation makes it less so (plus, I guess, Essence Fever?).<br /> <br /> To be honest, I think any system based on the idea that one type of Exalt should rule (as opposed to, say, good and wise people of any Exalt type, but not evil and foolish people of a particular type) is doomed to failure. Diversity is strength, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can make RL comparisons to a very well-known metaphysical doctrine, but again, don't want to derail the thread. </div> </div> </div>You don't have to, if you think it will derail things, but I'm a bit curious what you're referring to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Converts are nearly always more zealous than those raised to a belief system. </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I'm afraid I don't understand your point?<br /> <br /> (I'm a bit hungover from a friend's wedding yesterday, so I'm not the most on the ball today.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>&quot;Blaque</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Though that said, very good people can buy into pretty evil propoganda.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. So I think it's fine to have, say, a Dragonblood character who likes to educate children because he just, you know, is nice like that, but will cripple you if you dare claim Exaltation is From the Dragons, when it is clearly Of the Dragons. And whose greatest desire is to kill the Anathema.<br /> <br /> Oh Pelleps Delled. Never change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-15-2019, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T09:11:38-08:00","id":1288284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288267#post1288267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Queen is a damned treasure and you better believe it. For Queen and country we\u2019ll show \u2018em the might of the commonwealth in no uncertain terms</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, yes... the Queen is wonderful, Britain is your friend, you can trust Britain. We value and respect you.<br /> Not like America. America doesn't like you. They mock your politeness. We British value politeness highly. Don't be friends with America, be friends with Britain. Britain is Mother, Britain is Father.<br /> <br /> You know what else is great about Canada? Your language. You're so clever and well-spoken. You should keep using that language, and producing TV programmes to spread that language to the world. <i>Your</i> language.<br /> <br /> Also, you know that trade deal you're making with the EU? Why not make it with your good chum Britain? Come on, aren't we friends? Give us some of that sweet, sweet trade. Think of all that awesome stuff you can buy from Britain! Much better than crappy European stuff!<br /> <br /> If you don't, what will happen to poor Queenie? Think of how sad she'll be. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-15-2019, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T09:44:09-08:00","id":1288298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288269#post1288269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The US treatment of the Americas in the 19th and 20th Century, as well as some of the ways that imposed land distribution was implemented to native lands, kind of push me to say...yes actually. Economic empires are often built on ecnomic exploitationa nd dependence. Cultural empire is often done with a large chunk of cultural eradication in the process, especially when done purposefully as was done by the Spanish, British, and the United States.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no issue with these views, and believe that they can be held without contradiction. I just wanted to highlight the fact that hegemony can be imposed/accepted/whatever on more than just a military basis, and wanted to avoid sloppy shortcuts in thinking for this thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, depends here. There's a reason cultural relativism is kind of something brought up in the first couple weeks of any ethics course ever. Naively saying &quot;Well it was fine in the past&quot; is a non-starter for most things. And there folks in variosu parts of the world and history who viewed war differently, and total war and genocide very differently. Just because war was common, war for utter dominaiton, conquest, or displacement of other peoples was not how or why ever war was fought. </div> </div> </div>Since I am not an ethical relativist, I have no issue with anything you've said here. Some of my replies to others (below) may interest you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This kind of seems then like everyone's screwed since the Shogunate was a failure and the Realm operats through tyranical territorial empire. But I think that while the Great Curse is there, it exasperates the problems of the human condition, not replaces them. And that they have a elss indivdiually mechancially extreme Great Cruse, there are more of them, it's still there, and it's still people being able to be assholes by being people. </div> </div> </div>Well, I discuss at least my view of the human condition below, so stay tuned. However, I will point out that all becauseall current example of DB rule are obviously failures from the standpoint of this thread does not really bear on the argument that they are the best Exalt type to give rule to, if you had to pick an Exalt type. (Note: this argument also holds against <i>an</i>yExalt type ruling.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Are there? Because I think we use those metaphorically.</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I could say that the USA is a &quot;cultural Empire&quot; and you'll understand what I mean... but it isn't really. America might exert cultural influence over Britain, but that doesn't lead to political control of Britain.</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Similarly, some people say the EU is just Germany's economic empire, but this is hyperbole.</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Unless you're thinking of something different?</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> I know of at least one current state (Japan) that decided that after military conquest failed in WWII to switch to an economic form of 'conquest', and after <i>that</i> failed has switched to a cultural form of conquest. As stated above, I am not saying that these aren't inherently evil, but just to remember these ideas and not simply short-circuit 'empire' or 'imperial' to 'expansion through military conquest', even though that is by far the most common form of empire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't consider it be the </div> </div> </div></span></span></span></div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>ultimate</i><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> expression of evil. And I don't think most people today actually do. (If they did, no democratic nation would ever declare war on other countries. Yet they sometimes do.) Like, genocide is worse, for example.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> We certainly agree on that, yes. But it seemed clear that 'empire' was equated with 'baby eating factory' and also 'military conquest'. I mean, there are very very few things I would call more evil than eating babies.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But even in, say, the middle ages (which obviously was full of war), most ordinary people thought that invading another country just to conquer them was, not, actually, cool. </div> </div> </div>But the point there was that they didn't. People didn't fight wars (generally) to invade another country, at least in the modern sense, because 'country' (or 'nation') in the modern sense as a concept didn't exist. People did fight wars to change the leadership of other states (which would be the essence of the Hundred Years' War) but it would be very difficult to argue, historically, that France was trying to conquer England or vice versa.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's why the French Church spent 100 years trying to get knights to swear to keep the peace, before giving up because it simply didn't work. (So instead they came up with Just War, Chivalry, and the Crusades.) </div> </div> </div>That's one view of it, yes. I'm not sure I would characterize Chivalry as an outgrowth of the French Church specifically, but rather a cultural outgrowth of the Christian cultural hegemony in the time. (Just War, as an ethical principle, would certainly be a better example.) If you have any evidence of this, though, I would be very happy to read it.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's also why most wars actually had some kind of &quot;justification&quot;. Maybe the King just wanted to grab more land, but he'd tell everyone that he had a claim, or that the other side started it, or the enemy were heretics, or whatever. Take the Albeginsian Crusade; yes, probably the King and some nobles just wanted to seize land in southern France. But they didn't say &quot;we're going to do some conquering because invading is totally cool&quot;, they said &quot;the poor people of Southern France are being corrupted by monstrous heretics who hate our Holy Mother Church! We have to save southern France, and force is our only option!&quot; </div> </div> </div>This is a fairly reductionist argument. Personally, I would reverse the primary and secondary considerations here. Presumably, they wanted to fight the heresy--though IMO the Dominican Order was doing a find job without secular involvement--and getting the land was a nice bonus.<br /> <br /> The larger point I would like to make here, though, is that in these times a justification was given and also accepted. In this day and age, there are so few accepted <i>casus belli</i> that justifying going to war is almost impossible. (Cf. the last 70 years of world history)</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course, I'm not sure this is actually relevant. People were complaining that, in their view, WFHW depicts the Realm as an Empire that loves invading stuff, and they think this makes it eeevvvilll in a boring way. Saying that people in the setting may not find it so objectionable* doesn't mean players don't find it as objectionable. </div> </div> </div>Systemic slavery also exists in Creation, which IMO is outright worse than most wars. However, I felt it important to ensure that people understood that modern attitudes to war are quite new and about as much a change as the modern vs. premodern views of slavery, but the two subjects are not equally understood in that light. IOW, people are more likely to be able to RP premodern views of slavery--which the ST should be able to do even if the players do not--but not necessarily be able to RP premodern views of war, given the relative differences among them.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *In general, people being invaded find it much more objectionable than the people doing the invading, in any era. </div> </div> </div>That I felt was self-evident.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Ah, okay, that makes more sense.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">But they are still, inherently, an Exalt type based on hereditary, and that's likely to produce an aristocratic state.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It can of course be stable... but the inherent randomness of Dragonblood Exaltation makes it less so (plus, I guess, Essence Fever?).</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">To be honest, I think any system based on the idea that one type of Exalt should rule (as opposed to, say, good and wise people of any Exalt type, but not evil and foolish people of a particular type) is doomed to failure. Diversity is strength, etc.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Oh, certainly. Just saying that if I had to choose one type of Exalt...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You don't have to, if you think it will derail things, but I'm a bit curious what you're referring to. </div> </div> </div>The Fall, or Original Sin. At the very least, the narrative/practical aspects of the similarities between it and the Great Curse are striking. Blaque above appeals to 'human nature', which properly understood from my ethical tradition is another way of saying 'Original Sin'. Essentially, my stance on allowing the DB to rule was formed from the idea that if different sectors of humanity suffered to greater or lesser degree from the Fall (which, BTW, is not orthodox thought on the matter), those who suffered least would make the best rulers.<br /> <br /> Put in a more widely-acceptable (if IMO more diluted) form, if you had different sectors of humanity where some were more inclined towards egoism and some were more inclined to altruism, I think most would prefer the more altruistic to be in control.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sorry, I'm afraid I don't understand your point? </div> </div> </div>Perhaps this is my lack of understanding, but I was arguing that it is no surprise to me that the Northern Irish are more nationalistically British than the British themselves because they were basically 'converted' to the idea of being British while the British obtain their concept of 'Britishness' organically.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T09:51:32-08:00","id":1288302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288284#post1288284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don't, what will happen to poor Queenie? Think of how sad she'll be. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Vraiment! Et Fran\u00e7ais aussi! Nous devons remercions le Front du Lib\u00e9ration du Qu\u00e9bec pour notre deux langues officielles!<br /> <br /> For those anglophones in the audience that\u2019s \u201cTruely! And French also! We must thank the Quebec liberation front for our two official languages!\u201d<br /> <br /> And for reference the Quebec Liberation Front were French-Canadian terrorists. They killed a bunch of people. Please don\u2019t actually thank them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T09:58:10-08:00","id":1288306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288280#post1288280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Exactly. So I think it's fine to have, say, a Dragonblood character who likes to educate children because he just, you know, is nice like that, but will cripple you if you dare claim Exaltation is From the Dragons, when it is clearly Of the Dragons. And whose greatest desire is to kill the Anathema.<br /> <br /> Oh Pelleps Delled. Never change.</div> </div> </div> </div>The example more to my mind is the sort of situation like Fredrick Douglas talked about a couple times in his autobiography. Where he often met people who did honestly think they were good people, were kind, and treated him well and he noted as such. But then he also points out, <i>they owned people</i> still. He wasn't a child or a worker, he was property.<br /> <br /> I can see this with some Dynasts really. They open a school in a satrapy because well, there are so many orphans there. Not really even thinking that maybe there are a lot of orphans because a lot of parents get conscripted into the jannissary army or die in the mines or just died from a famine because fo how much food got sent somewhere else. This happened in India and Africa quite a bit to my understanding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T10:14:15-08:00","id":1288319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288298#post1288298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... The Fall, or Original Sin. At the very least, the narrative/practical aspects of the similarities between it and the Great Curse are striking. Blaque above appeals to 'human nature', which properly understood from my ethical tradition is another way of saying 'Original Sin'. Essentially, my stance on allowing the DB to rule was formed from the idea that if different sectors of humanity suffered to greater or lesser degree from the Fall (which, BTW, is not orthodox thought on the matter), those who suffered least would make the best rulers.<br /> <br /> Put in a more widely-acceptable (if IMO more diluted) form, if you had different sectors of humanity where some were more inclined towards egoism and some were more inclined to altruism, I think most would prefer the more altruistic to be in control. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>So this is a bit where I still don't buy into things, actually. This is mostly since I have a couple main views of things that I also tend to translate to how I view Creaiton as well.<br /> <br /> First, that while there is a distirbution of altruistic to selfish motivations in a population, they are not something that's heritable to a level that matters. Humnas, as a species, has been &quot;altruistic enough&quot; to get by most of our existance. Kind of like any other organism. Us being multi-cellular organisms geenrally is pretty good altruism, until some cells go rogue and you get cancer. Cancer isn't common enough to sabotage multicellular life in general, but it is common enough to kill indivdiuals now and again.<br /> <br /> So in context of the Great Curse, this means it's about severity fo damage. The Great Curse is still a curse, but a lot of what seems to have made societies in Creation break is not <i>just</i> the curse. It's the general trend observed in both Creation and oru own history of the behavior of selfish or ruthless indivdiuals taking power and imposing that power with few checks. The Great Curse to me exasperates what's already there just into thematically appropriate fashion for the Exalt. The Solar Great Cruse doesn't make them less qualified than Dragon-Blooded to rule due to its strenght. It just flavors the way they go and become bad rulers in a way that's theamtically well, Solary versus Terrestrially. The Curse is simply something <i>on top of</i> general trends of human history.<br /> <br /> Note I don't say like, paths or targets. A big thing to remember too is I follow a fairly striclty non-teleological view of things, including human nature or socities. Things kind fo stumble around into the future, more or less. It's just that some routes are more likely than others in the grand scheme fo things. Just like while sometimes you get a pair of headphones or a cable out of a drawer it's straight, most of the time the fucker will be knotted-up. Because in the end, there are more ways it can be in a knot than straight, given enough time.<br /> <br /> The societies of the Dragon-Blooded Shogunate and its successors aren't good socieites by dint that Dragon-Blooded founded them. Nor are they bad scoities wholy because fo the curse. They're just societies, whcih due to the goals fo the people leading them (which are attitudes people through most time and space hold in our world and in Creation) have often led to assholes in charge and rather exploitative.<br /> <br /> I think in context of this thread which is Lunars, it's notable too that the book never really says that what the Lunar Exalted bring will be any different or better for the world. Just for the Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T11:01:46-08:00","id":1288329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I know of at least one current state (Japan) that decided that after military conquest failed in WWII to switch to an economic form of 'conquest', and after <i>that</i> failed has switched to a cultural form of conquest. As stated above, I am not saying that these aren't inherently evil, but just to remember these ideas and not simply short-circuit 'empire' or 'imperial' to 'expansion through military conquest', even though that is by far the most common form of empire.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point is that's not actually an Empire.<br /> <br /> I mean, even if China, the Phillipines, Korea and Taiwan were full of Japanese-owned factories producing goods for Japanese companies, and everyone watched Japanese TV shows and listened to J-Pop, they wouldn't actually be part of the Japanese Empire, because their governments would still be independent, even if they were constrained by Japan's economic influence.<br /> <br /> So, I don't think that claiming that Empires require military conquest is disproved by the fact that S.Korea has a deliberate strategy to dominate Pop Culture, or that Germany supports the EU so it cannot be invaded by its neighbours.<br /> <br /> I mean, obviously we're running into post-structuralism here; this is purely a matter of semantics.<br /> <br /> But when people were saying &quot;Empires are evil because they conquer stuff&quot;* they are talking about a specific type of political polity, whereby a nation-state/city-state/distinct group dominates larger and larger areas to its own benefit. The Roman Empire, the British Empire, the Japanese Empire, the Spanish Empire, the Mongol Empire, the Timurid Empire, the Ottoman Empire, etc. And this requires force.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But it seemed clear that 'empire' was equated with 'baby eating factory' and also 'military conquest'. </div> </div> </div>*The baby-eating thing is ridiculous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the point there was that they didn't. People didn't fight wars (generally) to invade another country, at least in the modern sense, because 'country' (or 'nation') in the modern sense as a concept didn't exist. People did fight wars to change the leadership of other states (which would be the essence of the Hundred Years' War) but it would be very difficult to argue, historically, that France was trying to conquer England or vice versa. </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> Okay, that's a very valid point.<br /> <br /> I'll rephrase it then; ordinary peasants did not inherently think it was okay for knights to go and kill a bunch of other peasants somewhere else and take their land (and peasants definitely did not think it was okay for knights to come and take their lands), and even some pillars of establishment (like the Church) weren't cool with it. That's why knights and lords had to come up with justifications to tell their followers (and themselves). Henry V told his soldiers he was fighting to take his rightful crown, not that he just wanted to get more money and power.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's one view of it, yes. I'm not sure I would characterize Chivalry as an outgrowth of the French Church specifically, but rather a cultural outgrowth of the Christian cultural hegemony in the time. (Just War, as an ethical principle, would certainly be a better example.) If you have any evidence of this, though, I would be very happy to read it. </div> </div> </div>Nah, I was jumping from the French Church to the more general western Church (and I don't mean they thought of the whole thing by themselves, but that they were a major factor in promoting it, as a way to reign in the robber knights that plagued western Europe).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is a fairly reductionist argument. Personally, I would reverse the primary and secondary considerations here. Presumably, they wanted to fight the heresy--though IMO the Dominican Order was doing a find job without secular involvement--and getting the land was a nice bonus. </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> A lot of modern historians are not sure there actually was any heresy at all. The Cathars may not have existed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In this day and age, there are so few accepted <i>casus belli</i> that justifying going to war is almost impossible. (Cf. the last 70 years of world history) </div> </div> </div>I don't know about your country, but in my lifetime my nation has gone to war in Iraq, the Balkans, the Balkans again, Afghanistan and Iraq again. Not to mention all the times when we've sent troops or warplanes to attack enemies, but just not called it a war, like in Libya, Sierra Leone, etc. Currently we're assisting the Iraqi and Afghan governments against rebels. That doesn't involve a Declaration of War, but let's be honest, it's war.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Systemic slavery also exists in Creation, which IMO is outright worse than most wars. However, I felt it important to ensure that people understood that modern attitudes to war are quite new and about as much a change as the modern vs. premodern views of slavery, but the two subjects are not equally understood in that light. IOW, people are more likely to be able to RP premodern views of slavery--which the ST should be able to do even if the players do not--but not necessarily be able to RP premodern views of war, given the relative differences among them.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Hmmm... I don't agree with everything there (for one thing, pre-modern attitudes to war covers a vast number of different cultural-political theatres of war), but I do see your point.<br /> <br /> I still think the point stands though, that many cultures who are not the Realm are going to see the Realm invading places as evil. This may at times by hypocritical (they may invade other cultures or groups too), but that's still how they'll see it.<br /> I mean, not always, sure. There may well be places that admire the Realm for it. Until they're the ones who get invaded, of course.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Fall, or Original Sin. At the very least, the narrative/practical aspects of the similarities between it and the Great Curse are striking. </div> </div> </div>Ah, sure, but then since Original Sin doesn't affect different groups differently I didn't understand the connection you were making.*<br /> <br /> *Though CS Lewis wrote a rather interesting sci-fi book with pre-Fall aliens on Venus. It wasn't as good a read as the other two books in the trilogy, but I did find it interesting. It was more original than the first in the series, the one on Mars.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Perhaps this is my lack of understanding, but I was arguing that it is no surprise to me that the Northern Irish are more nationalistically British than the British themselves because they were basically 'converted' to the idea of being British while the British obtain their concept of 'Britishness' organically.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Oh no. We didn't convert many Irish.<br /> We just filled the north-east with British settlers (mostly Presbyterians, who were much more anti-Catholic than Anglicans were).<br /> They outnumber the descendants of the native Irish, and so comprise a slight majority (it used to be a bigger majority) of Northern Ireland.<br /> We also didn't let most of the natives vote.<br /> (It wasn't racist, honest! We just didn't let poor people vote. Only people who owned property. It was a complete coincidence that most Protestants were rich and most Catholics were poor.)<br /> <br /> The descendants of the native Irish </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">mostly are pretty anti-UK (hence the IRA; it's more peaceful now, but not because the Irish like being part of the UK, they just think it's better than living in a warzone of IRA vs UVF). Because colonised peoples very rarely like their colonisers.<br /> <br /> So when you look at Northern Ireland and think &quot;oh, there's all these patriots who love Britain, clearly the Empire was popular&quot; it's quite misleading. We just kicked out the natives (because they rebelled against Elizabeth I) and sent a bunch of Brits over there.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-15-2019, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T11:04:51-08:00","id":1288332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288319#post1288319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think in context of this thread which is Lunars, it's notable too that the book never really says that what the Lunar Exalted bring will be any different or better for the world. Just for the Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's so much that the book doesn't say, but rather that it says the Lunars can't agree, and last time they had a big discussion about it two Elders went to war, so now they avoid discussing it.<br /> <br /> And, as Iraq shows us, not making post-victory plans for after you've defeated the tyrants always goes <i>brilliantly</i>.<br /> <br /> (My PCs generally got on fine when they were fighting bad guys. It's when they started running countries, in different ways with different motives, that they turned on each other.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T14:11:46-08:00","id":1288391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288298#post1288298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know of at least one current state (Japan) that decided that after military conquest failed in WWII to switch to an economic form of 'conquest', and after <i>that</i> failed has switched to a cultural form of conquest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Total tangent but.... Hmmm? &quot;No can who is a foreigner can move to Japan and take part in our culture there. We will now make movies, TV and music almost purely for our own consumption (Galpagos Syndrome yay!) with no significant cultural exports other than games and anime, and even then, that's more by luck than design. Occasionally foreigners will buy our cultural products despite failing to market it to them, and we will <i>not encourage this in any way</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> ... is kind of a weird way to approach cultural conquest.<br /> <br /> (I mean, the only country in East Asia that seems halfway decent at cultural conquest (which if anyone is good at, its the US) is... <a href=\"https://qz.com/21468/why-it-was-so-easy-for-korea-to-take-over-japan-in-the-pop-culture-wars/\" target=\"_blank\">South Korea?</a>)<br /> (Hopefully this is not being &quot;Defend Glorious Nihon!&quot; guy here!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T14:40:28-08:00","id":1288396,"title":"","content":"There seem to be a lot of Apperance charms that have a Clause of 'This influence can not be resisted'.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how to feel about that and wonder if some of those are going to be cut down. Sidestepping the social system like that seems kind of surprising.<br /> <br /> Lunars are also way better at leading troops from the front then Solars are and it makes me sad that Solars probably won't ever get those charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T14:49:14-08:00","id":1288398,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure they are way better in terms of raw power, but they do have slightly more options.<br /> <br /> Their training charm is a lot weaker though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288396#post1288396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There seem to be a lot of Apperance charms that have a Clause of 'This influence can not be resisted'.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's not loads, but there are some. They looked to me like mostly quite weak or temporary effects though.<br /> But obviously, it's one you've got to be careful of.<br /> <br /> Were there any particular ones you were thinking of? I've read through the charms once, and there's a lot, so it's difficult to remember everything after one pass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-15-2019, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T14:59:01-08:00","id":1288400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288398#post1288398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's not loads, but there are some. They looked to me like mostly quite weak or temporary effects though.<br /> But obviously, it's one you've got to be careful of.<br /> <br /> Were there any particular ones you were thinking of? I've read through the charms once, and there's a lot, so it's difficult to remember everything after one pass.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a few of the stealth charms which aren't very clear whether you can contest it with powers other than Eye of the Unconquered Sun or if it's just that one charm or bust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T15:00:54-08:00","id":1288401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288398#post1288398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure they are way better in terms of raw power, but they do have slightly more options.<br /> <br /> Their training charm is a lot weaker though.<br /> <br /> <br /> There's not loads, but there are some. They looked to me like mostly quite weak or temporary effects though.<br /> But obviously, it's one you've got to be careful of.<br /> <br /> Were there any particular ones you were thinking of? I've read through the charms once, and there's a lot, so it's difficult to remember everything after one pass.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually went back to look at it and you're right. The charms that can't be resisted are because you're using the charms to change how people perceive you on others; those charms aren't listed as being resistable either in the DB or Solar versions of them in addition to the Lunar one, so it makes sense that a Lunar giving those charm's effects to someone else should also be unresistable. It's just weird because Lunars have two of them and can give them to others, so it looks like there's more unresistable stuff","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T09:49:58-08:00","id":1288628,"title":"","content":"So we have Appearance charms, and I'm disappointed. I don't see Meerkat-Steals-the-Spotlight Prana anywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T10:13:19-08:00","id":1288634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288401#post1288401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually went back to look at it and you're right. The charms that can't be resisted are because you're using the charms to change how people perceive you on others; those charms aren't listed as being resistable either in the DB or Solar versions of them in addition to the Lunar one, so it makes sense that a Lunar giving those charm's effects to someone else should also be unresistable. It's just weird because Lunars have two of them and can give them to others, so it looks like there's more unresistable stuff</div> </div> </div> </div>Which ones do it without counting as a Psyche effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T10:33:29-08:00","id":1288637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288628#post1288628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So we have Appearance charms, and I'm disappointed. I don't see Meerkat-Steals-the-Spotlight Prana anywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Attention-Demanding Presence and at least two other Charms that may build off of it. Argent Muse Approach, at a stretch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T12:19:41-08:00","id":1288675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288634#post1288634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which ones do it without counting as a Psyche effect?</div> </div> </div> </div>Both Solar Larceny's Seasoned Criminal Method and Dragonblood Sail's Dragon Mariner lack Psyche. These charms are perfectly within the already established spectrum with a twist appropriate for Iconoclasts and Outsiders who manipulate the fabric of society due to their stance outside of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T13:01:45-08:00","id":1288701,"title":"","content":"Where are these new Charms listed? I haven't seen them yet.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Never mind, found them. Am a dummy after all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2176,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","user":"SpectacularTentacular","date":". 02-16-2019, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T13:11:32-08:00","id":1288706,"title":"","content":"They're in the updates page on the kickstarter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T14:07:00-08:00","id":1288728,"title":"","content":"On a more constructive note: Will the animals section have some helpful &quot;mythic themes&quot; attached to said animals? Snakes mean <i>this</i> in this part of Creation, but over here they mean <i>this</i>, etc.? It will probably help in adding some depth to the Lunars loking for the meaning behind what they are, as well as for the Charms that depend on said meaning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T14:14:33-08:00","id":1288733,"title":"","content":"Just stopping by to say I am loving the updates so far! Also, I was curious about the moderately numerous references that have been made to Lunar necromancy so far. Does anyone now if we are going to get any mechanics for necromancy in the sorcery chapter of this book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T14:57:54-08:00","id":1288747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288733#post1288733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just stopping by to say I am loving the updates so far! Also, I was curious about the moderately numerous references that have been made to Lunar necromancy so far. Does anyone now if we are going to get any mechanics for necromancy in the sorcery chapter of this book?</div> </div> </div> </div>The last I remember is that necromancy will be introduced in the abyssals book or if there is enough popular demand I could see it being introduced in a book on general sorcery. But ya, as things stand now it will be at least 3 years before we see necromancy at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T15:55:51-08:00","id":1288766,"title":"","content":"Yes. Lunars are being promised to be proficient at necromancy, so the appropriate aesthetics is being established now, rather than leaving it to a recon whenever the actual rules drop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T16:32:11-08:00","id":1288775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288329#post1288329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">]My point is that's not actually an Empire.<br /> <br /> I mean, even if China, the Phillipines, Korea and Taiwan were full of Japanese-owned factories producing goods for Japanese companies, and everyone watched Japanese TV shows and listened to J-Pop, they wouldn't actually be part of the Japanese Empire, because their governments would still be independent, even if they were constrained by Japan's economic influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a very narrow view of influence. If one state cannot make useful policy without the consent of another state, no matter the reason, the second is imperially dominating the first. The fact that no one has yet successfully achieved a cultural hegemony (except, perhaps in some areas, France through some history) does not make it any less a theoretical possibility.<br /> <br /> Another point is that while Rome <i>obtained</i> its empire through military means, its cultural hegemony was far more important in retaining its Empire than its military.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, I don't think that claiming that Empires require military conquest is disproved by the fact that S.Korea has a deliberate strategy to dominate Pop Culture, or that Germany supports the EU so it cannot be invaded by its neighbours.<br /> <br /> I mean, obviously we're running into post-structuralism here; this is purely a matter of semantics. </div> </div> </div>I guess. I think that as the use of military force becomes more and more disliked, the competition is increasingly likely to occur in other spheres.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But when people were saying &quot;Empires are evil because they conquer stuff&quot;* they are talking about a specific type of political polity, whereby a nation-state/city-state/distinct group dominates larger and larger areas to its own benefit. The Roman Empire, the British Empire, the Japanese Empire, the Spanish Empire, the Mongol Empire, the Timurid Empire, the Ottoman Empire, etc. And this requires force. </div> </div> </div>Historically, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *The baby-eating thing is ridiculous. </div> </div> </div>Well, it is very difficult for me at least to understand at times when hyperbole is being used for rhetorical effect, given that I routinely believe this only to be told that people were literal and serious.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Okay, that's a very valid point.<br /> <br /> I'll rephrase it then; ordinary peasants did not inherently think it was okay for knights to go and kill a bunch of other peasants somewhere else and take their land (and peasants definitely did not think it was okay for knights to come and take their lands), and even some pillars of establishment (like the Church) weren't cool with it. That's why knights and lords had to come up with justifications to tell their followers (and themselves). Henry V told his soldiers he was fighting to take his rightful crown, not that he just wanted to get more money and power. </div> </div> </div>Enh. Given the fact that the peasant's lot was not going to be improved no matter who actually held sovereignty over their land, I don't think they cared much. (I agree that they obviously wouldn't want to support it.)<br /> <br /> However, I would point out that<i> casus belli</i> are far more important in foreign affairs than the attitudes of peasants. While I do not want to belittle the constituents of a country, it is only in very rare cases historically that justifications were important from the standpoint of the peasantry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A lot of modern historians are not sure there actually was any heresy at all. The Cathars may not have existed. </div> </div> </div>I am happy for modern historians. Given that entire monastic orders were created in response to the Albigensian heresy, at least theologically it did exist. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't know about your country, but in my lifetime my nation has gone to war in Iraq, the Balkans, the Balkans again, Afghanistan and Iraq again. Not to mention all the times when we've sent troops or warplanes to attack enemies, but just not called it a war, like in Libya, Sierra Leone, etc. Currently we're assisting the Iraqi and Afghan governments against rebels. That doesn't involve a Declaration of War, but let's be honest, it's war. </div> </div> </div>Oh, I'm American. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The whole 'needing justification for war' thing is much less of an issue when you're the sole superpower in the world. Again, perhaps I am wrong, but I'm pretty sure that the USA has a very poor image on the world stage precisely <i>because</i> our justifications have not been accepted. (Rather reminds me of the Realm there...)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hmmm... I don't agree with everything there (for one thing, pre-modern attitudes to war covers a vast number of different cultural-political theatres of war), but I do see your point.<br /> <br /> I still think the point stands though, that many cultures who are not the Realm are going to see the Realm invading places as evil. This may at times by hypocritical (they may invade other cultures or groups too), but that's still how they'll see it.<br /> I mean, not always, sure. There may well be places that admire the Realm for it. Until they're the ones who get invaded, of course. </div> </div> </div>Sure, but I don't think it's as monolithic as this thread has presented. If I wanted to be cynical, I think many don't like the Realm's overbearing nature and imperial strides more from a, 'Hey I wanted that!' than, 'Help, help, I'm being repressed.'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ah, sure, but then since Original Sin doesn't affect different groups differently I didn't understand the connection you were making.*<br /> <br /> *Though CS Lewis wrote a rather interesting sci-fi book with pre-Fall aliens on Venus. It wasn't as good a read as the other two books in the trilogy, but I did find it interesting. It was more original than the first in the series, the one on Mars. </div> </div> </div>Perelandra is quite good. I prefer his nonfiction, though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh no. We didn't convert many Irish.<br /> We just filled the north-east with British settlers (mostly Presbyterians, who were much more anti-Catholic than Anglicans were).<br /> They outnumber the descendants of the native Irish, and so comprise a slight majority (it used to be a bigger majority) of Northern Ireland.<br /> We also didn't let most of the natives vote.<br /> (It wasn't racist, honest! We just didn't let poor people vote. Only people who owned property. It was a complete coincidence that most Protestants were rich and most Catholics were poor.)<br /> <br /> The descendants of the native Irish mostly are pretty anti-UK (hence the IRA; it's more peaceful now, but not because the Irish like being part of the UK, they just think it's better than living in a warzone of IRA vs UVF). Because colonised peoples very rarely like their colonisers.<br /> <br /> So when you look at Northern Ireland and think &quot;oh, there's all these patriots who love Britain, clearly the Empire was popular&quot; it's quite misleading. We just kicked out the natives (because they rebelled against Elizabeth I) and sent a bunch of Brits over there. </div> </div> </div>So less 'convert zeal' and more 'almost ghetto pressure' issue. Gotcha.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T17:27:30-08:00","id":1288787,"title":"","content":"There is talk about baby eating and it's not about Raksi. <br /> <br /> She loses a lot of charm by no longer being a literal baby eating monster. Now she is just a creepy sorceress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T18:17:26-08:00","id":1288796,"title":"","content":"She is still literally a baby-eating monster. But it's no longer because she's insane.<br /> <br /> (Ulthwithian, I just got back from a house party and I'm drunk, and I've got to get up for Church in the morning. I'll try and respond tomorrow afternoon.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T18:45:17-08:00","id":1288801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288796#post1288796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She is still literally a baby-eating monster. But it's no longer because she's insane.<br /> <br /> (Ulthwithian, I just got back from a house party and I'm drunk, and I've got to get up for Church in the morning. I'll try and respond tomorrow afternoon.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I must have missed that part. I got the impression she encouraged fictional rumors concerning her monstrosity. Basically, she makes sure that people think she is a baby eating monster even though she isnt.<br /> <br /> Did I miss the part where Ma-Ha-Suchi went insane because he was once one of the most beautiful exalted transformed into a hideous monster by the Wyld. He certainly still has the problematic portions of his character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T18:48:09-08:00","id":1288802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1287486#post1287486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Too bad the same can't be said for Lunar-Dynast engagements. For a superpower, the Realm doesn't really seem to successfully do much of anything.<br /> <br /> Maybe The Realm will be the first book to portray the Realm as something other than Snidely-Whiplash-evil, baby-eating, murder machine of ineffectual incompetence... but I don't hold out much hope for that.<br /> <br /> I'm glad that the Lunar book hypes Lunars; I just wish that any book did the same for Dynasts and the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm so confused.<br /> <br /> I mean, this isn't the thread for it, and maybe it'll never be discussed, but I'm still just... nothing but confused about this thing specifically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T19:05:57-08:00","id":1288805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288802#post1288802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm so confused.<br /> <br /> I mean, this isn't the thread for it, and maybe it'll never be discussed, but I'm still just... nothing but confused about this thing specifically.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is literally an entire splat that tells players in every version of the Lore that they are objectively the bad guys and should feel bad for playing them. It can get frustrating to DB fans that they are always portrayed as bad guys. Yeah, this is Lunars and the wrong place for this discussion because the Lunars book absolutely should be portraying the Realm as bad guys, but the DB book made them bad guys too, so there is some understandable frustration going around.<br /> <br /> I put a lot of effort into planning out a rather epic Realm Civil War campaign and it fell apart before it began because I couldn't get the players to buy into the Realm culture even a little bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T20:27:16-08:00","id":1288825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288775#post1288775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If one state cannot make useful policy without the consent of another state, no matter the reason, the second is imperially dominating the first.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Permit me to issue and control the money of a nation, and I care not who makes its laws!&quot; -- Nathan Rothschild<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, it is very difficult for me at least to understand at times when hyperbole is being used for rhetorical effect, given that I routinely believe this only to be told that people were literal and serious. </div> </div> </div>You can rest assured that I, at least, was being hyperbolic about the baby-eating.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm pretty sure that the USA has a very poor image on the world stage precisely <i>because</i> our justifications have not been accepted. </div> </div> </div>Probably because most of them were lies, and the truth was unacceptable.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Perelandra is quite good. I prefer his nonfiction, though. </div> </div> </div>I love all of his work, but of his Space Trilogy, I found the third book, <i>That Hideous Strength</i>, the most onerous one to read. Of course the ugliest book of the three would take place completely on Earth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T20:38:04-08:00","id":1288828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288805#post1288805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is literally an entire splat that tells players in every version of the Lore that they are objectively the bad guys and should feel bad for playing them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your inability to separate Dragon-Blooded empires from every individual Dragon-Blood, including the unassociated Outcastes and the altruistic Terrestrials trying to reform the system from within, sounds like a personal problem to me.<br /> <br /> Imperialism is evil. The setting needs to have an empire to provide tension and conflict for stories. If the Scarlet Dynasty wasn't trying to conquer the entire world, the Lunar Exalted would have largely given up on fighting them because they could control the Threshold without competition, and the spare Solar Exalted would have reached elderhood by now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, this is Lunars and the wrong place for this discussion </div> </div> </div>That's a good point. If you feel so strongly that the Dragon-Blooded should be the splat largely displaced from power and hunted down by an imperial force, you should make a new thread for that discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T21:21:32-08:00","id":1288838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288801#post1288801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I must have missed that part. I got the impression she encouraged fictional rumors concerning her monstrosity. Basically, she makes sure that people think she is a baby eating monster even though she isnt.<br /> <br /> Did I miss the part where Ma-Ha-Suchi went insane because he was once one of the most beautiful exalted transformed into a hideous monster by the Wyld. He certainly still has the problematic portions of his character.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) You did. One of her adherents only impressed her because she intervened to stop her force-feeding a baby to one of Ma-Ha-Suchi's adherents. That she does it only to piss people off makes her come off as more of a monster, not less.<br /> <br /> 2) We all did, for which we are all glad. He's not only someone you could, hypothetically, work for and not be a total monster, but he's a better antagonist, too. I'm not sure if he lost his face due to Wyld mutation or even if he cares overmuch, but I like &quot;tired, nostalgia-addled old war veteran coming out of depressed haze to rebuild an empire&quot; a lot better than...what we had. If he's sensitive about his face, now it becomes meaningful, because it's become a symbol of how <i>much </i>he lost. He's without his home, his friends, his place in the world-he's even lost his good looks. No wonder he's angry and bitter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T21:34:51-08:00","id":1288841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288733#post1288733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just stopping by to say I am loving the updates so far! Also, I was curious about the moderately numerous references that have been made to Lunar necromancy so far. Does anyone now if we are going to get any mechanics for necromancy in the sorcery chapter of this book?</div> </div> </div> </div>I asked them about it in a couple different topics and the Devs confirmed that Lunars will be able to perform up to second circle necromancy this edition compared to only getting first circle last edition making them incredibly powerful necromancers (which probably made it fairly popular compared to sorcerery for more war minded no moons since sidereals and dragon blooded can't match it directly). Sadly they also confirmed that Lunars isn't going to have necromancy in it and we still have a wait ahead of us for the official release of necromancy so any lunar necromancer is going to need to homebrew it up for awhile. We can only hope they either hurry up with abyssals or decide to release necromancy in some sort of side book first instead of waiting and putting it in the abyssal book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T00:02:39-08:00","id":1288864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288841#post1288841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I asked them about it in a couple different topics and the Devs confirmed that Lunars will be able to perform up to second circle necromancy this edition compared to only getting first circle last edition making them incredibly powerful necromancers (which probably made it fairly popular compared to sorcerery for more war minded no moons since sidereals and dragon blooded can't match it directly). Sadly they also confirmed that Lunars isn't going to have necromancy in it and we still have a wait ahead of us for the official release of necromancy so any lunar necromancer is going to need to homebrew it up for awhile. We can only hope they either hurry up with abyssals or decide to release necromancy in some sort of side book first instead of waiting and putting it in the abyssal book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I figured that was most likely the case, but thanks for answering. I suppose its one of those things thats not too hard to handwave or homebrewing the mean time, but it would be awesome to see some official support. Lunars being able to achieve the second circle is an interesting twist, i find i approve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T02:40:50-08:00","id":1288884,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there's a lot of animals associated with death (crows, vultures, black hounds, etc) that I feel like Lunars should have the option to be decent necromancers. Not Abyssal level, but better than a mortal necromancer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288775#post1288775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that's a very narrow view of influence. If one state cannot make useful policy without the consent of another state, no matter the reason, the second is imperially dominating the first.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that not a very loose view of &quot;imperial&quot; domination?<br /> <br /> I mean, if, say, the Kingdom of X can't ally with the Kingdom of Y because they'll get invaded by the Kingdom of Z... they're being politically dominated. But I wouldn't call it imperial domination.<br /> Similarly, if Democracy X can't pass a law putting up tariffs on a good because Democracy Y will slap a ton of tariffs on X's goods and ruin their economy, this is economic domination, but not imperial domination.<br /> <br /> Essentially, when Obama got the Iranians to put their nuclear program on hold, America was dominating Iran, but I'd hardly say this makes Iran part of an American Empire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The fact that no one has yet successfully achieved a cultural hegemony (except, perhaps in some areas, France through some history) does not make it any less a theoretical possibility. </div> </div> </div>Again, I'm essentially making a semantic argument; an Empire is a political unit, and so purely cultural hegemony may not actually be an Empire. Unless this cultural hegemony leads to political unification.<br /> <br /> Hmmm... I suppose you could argue that the German Empire was a cultural hegemony that became a political unit. Although obviously, it came into existence because Prussia beat up Austria and France, so it's not really entirely cultural. I suppose it depends how you define cultural.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another point is that while Rome <i>obtained</i> its empire through military means, its cultural hegemony was far more important in retaining its Empire than its military.<br /> <br /> I guess. I think that as the use of military force becomes more and more disliked, the competition is increasingly likely to occur in other spheres. </div> </div> </div>Sure. But I'm not arguing about this.<br /> <br /> My point isn't that economic, cultural, religious, etc, domination doesn't exist. My point is that the word &quot;Empire&quot; has a much more specific meaning than simply the power one state has over another. It refers to a specific type of polity.* People on this thread said &quot;Why are Empires presented as the bad guys?&quot; Others said &quot;Empires always invade stuff.&quot; You said &quot;but what about cultural and polticial domination?&quot; My point is not that this is irrelevant, but that your examples of political and cultural domination are not Empires, just like they're not, say, theocracies, or nation-states (Japan is a nation-state. Areas economically dominated by it are not part of that nation-state), or apples, or dogs.<br /> So, if we want to talk about &quot;is it accurate for the Realm's Empire to be presented as military&quot;, and people say &quot;Empires are always military!&quot; I don't think you can respond to that with &quot;well, what about other forms of domination?&quot; Because then you're not answering the question &quot;is it accurate for the Realm's Empire to be presented as military&quot;, you're asking &quot;should the Realm have an Empire, or instead dominate the threshold via other means?&quot;<br /> <br /> As I said, it's a semantic argument.<br /> <br /> *Obviously, all polities are different, and due to translations terms get used imprecisely. But we can still draw a difference between Empires, Kingdoms, Republics, Federations, etc. America is a federal republic, but not an Empire (anymore), despite its high level of hegemony. South Korea is a republic, not an Empire, despite its dominance in Asian pop culture. Egypt is a republic, not an Empire, despite the dominance of its TV in the Arabic world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Historically, yes. </div> </div> </div>When discussing empires vis a vis the Realm, I don't think it's unreasonable for posters on this forum to go by pre-modern empires that have existed, rather than purely theoretical future forms of empire.<br /> <br /> TBH, I expect that if, in the future, one state gains political control over other states and absorbs them under itself into a super-state dominated by the first state, by purely cultural or economic means, I don't think they'll call it an Empire. They'll give it a fancy new name, probably a better sounding one, as they won't want to admit one state dominates the others.<br /> Like &quot;The Kingdom of Great Britain&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, I would point out that<i> casus belli</i> are far more important in foreign affairs than the attitudes of peasants. While I do not want to belittle the constituents of a country, it is only in very rare cases historically that justifications were important from the standpoint of the peasantry. </div> </div> </div>Ah, I assumed, when you said &quot;pre-modern people were much more okay with invasions&quot; you were talking about people generally, rather than governments.<br /> <br /> Because in terms of governments pre-Westphalia (for Europe) and pre-UN (for the world), yes, you are absolutely correct.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am happy for modern historians. Given that entire monastic orders were created in response to the Albigensian heresy, at least theologically it did exist. </div> </div> </div>Well, sure, theologically, but theologically the Pope is infallible (in certain circumstances), yet I don't think that's true.<br /> <br /> The theory now as I understand it, is that, essentially, it was a lot of confirmation bias, fear of heretics, etc, people <i>looking</i> for heretics, then encouraged by people who were looking for an excuse to take military action and so pushed for a Crusade.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure, but I don't think it's as monolithic as this thread has presented. If I wanted to be cynical, I think many don't like the Realm's overbearing nature and imperial strides more from a, 'Hey I wanted that!' than, 'Help, help, I'm being repressed.' </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's probably reasonable.<br /> The Medoans, for example, probably dream more of the conquests of the Touman Prince than of a world of free and independent nations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So less 'convert zeal' and more 'almost ghetto pressure' issue. Gotcha. </div> </div> </div>Kind of, yeah. It's just colonists vs colonised natives, essentially.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I love all of his work, but of his Space Trilogy, I found the third book, <i>That Hideous Strength</i>, the most onerous one to read. Of course the ugliest book of the three would take place completely on Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did too, it was one of those books I tried to read, failed to finish, and came back years later and read again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must have missed that part. I got the impression she encouraged fictional rumors concerning her monstrosity. Basically, she makes sure that people think she is a baby eating monster even though she isnt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, she still eats babies.<br /> The change is that she doesn't eat them because she's insane. She eats them (and makes others eat them) as a power play.<br /> Which arguably makes her more monstrous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Did I miss the part where Ma-Ha-Suchi went insane because he was once one of the most beautiful exalted transformed into a hideous monster by the Wyld. He certainly still has the problematic portions of his character. </div> </div> </div>He's not insane.<br /> He doesn't have rape camps.<br /> He doesn't want to murder all the Dragonblood.<br /> What are the problematic portions of his character he still has? I thought he was fine. But then, I only read his portion once, I might have skimmed stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-17-2019, 05:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T02:59:43-08:00","id":1288885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288828#post1288828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imperialism is evil. The setting needs to have an empire to provide tension and conflict for stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes... but I can see where people are coming from.<br /> <br /> A purely monolithic empire of evil is quite dull, and simplistic. It should be one where you can tell stories with some sympathy for either side, even if you ultimately say &quot;yes, side A are the bad guys.&quot;<br /> <br /> Especially when it's a common theatre of play for groups (in a way that, say, loyal Abyssals of a Deathlord probably isn't).<br /> <br /> One of my friends made the comparison to the Imperium of Man. We used to play Dark Heresy, and of course in that you are the torture-police of a xenophobic, brutal, oppressive empire of evil. The Imperium <i>is</i> bad, no question. But that doesn't mean every member is evil, or that, say, when our PCs were fighting chaos cultists or genestealers or brain-eating aliens on behalf of the Imperium, we weren't doing something good.<br /> <br /> Similarly, even if the game overall says &quot;the Realm is evil&quot;, that doesn't mean you can't have examples of Dragonblood saving peasants from Raksha or the Undead or barbarian hordes led by twisted were-beasts who gain power by eating people's hearts.<br /> <br /> And that's before you get into people believing the propaganda, and, as was mentioned earlier, good people genuinely believing that they must kill Solars, or they should serve the Dragonblood because they're perfected demigods, etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, personally, I didn't actually read WFHW and think &quot;the Realm is a snidely-whiplash villain who loves eeeeevil&quot;, so saying &quot;the Realm needs to be shown more sympathetically&quot; isn't something I'm worried about. But clearly other people got that impression, and I can understand why they'd argue for a more sympathetically presented Realm, for reasons other than Imperial apologism.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T03:10:25-08:00","id":1288886,"title":"","content":"I could see exigents giving both the realm and the silver pact a fairly balanced depiction, when discussing how exigents might interact with other exalted.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T04:01:20-08:00","id":1288890,"title":"","content":"When people say &quot;The Realm is Evil&quot;, they use Evil as a shortcut word. The Realm is not actually Evil, it's a huge nation with policies that adversely effect the world while consolidating power for itself. It has good people in it and bad people in it. Some of the places it touches are likely made better by it, but that's also a simplistic shortcut. &quot;Better&quot; for some people but not for others. The inverse is also true.<br /> <br /> The Realm's huge population lives in relative peace and prosperity. That should count for something. They spread peace and -well...not prosperity- at the point of a spear to other nations. Would the rest of the world be a better place if the Realm ruled over all of it and didn't have to worry about external groups going to war with it? Yeah, probably not, but for some definitions of better, perhaps.<br /> <br /> And just because you're from a place that tends to have a negative impact on the rest of the world, that doesn't mean you can't be a hero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T04:19:05-08:00","id":1288893,"title":"","content":"Stupid mutations with unknown values. Literally all the animal merits in the corebook have no indication how many mutation points it costs to claim them for your spirit shape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T04:37:14-08:00","id":1288895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288884#post1288884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's not insane.<br /> He doesn't have rape camps.<br /> He doesn't want to murder all the Dragonblood.<br /> What are the problematic portions of his character he still has? I thought he was fine. But then, I only read his portion once, I might have skimmed stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless the origin of Beastmen has changed he is definitely running some kind of rape camp or at least a very intense breeding program.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T04:43:35-08:00","id":1288896,"title":"","content":"It has. Lunars can make beastmen via a charm now. I think it's intelligence so we're likely to actually see it next friday. <br /> <br /> Also apparently the old fashioned way is just something that happens in the wyld now. Anyone can do it, in theory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T06:41:29-08:00","id":1288909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288893#post1288893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stupid mutations with unknown values. Literally all the animal merits in the corebook have no indication how many mutation points it costs to claim them for your spirit shape.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got my fingers crossed that the Merits section of the Lunar's book fixes most (if not all) of this.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T06:51:31-08:00","id":1288912,"title":"","content":"Ah, the Chapter Fiction is up for Raksi and her favorite student Weyna. Its amusing to see how they interact, considering what happens later.<br /> <br /> I guess Raksi's reversed hands are a thing of the past then?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T14:32:30-08:00","id":1289000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288893#post1288893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stupid mutations with unknown values. Literally all the animal merits in the corebook have no indication how many mutation points it costs to claim them for your spirit shape.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that's because you're not supposed to be able to do so, because some of those merits would be hella broken if you could buy them with background points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T15:02:31-08:00","id":1289004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288895#post1288895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless the origin of Beastmen has changed he is definitely running some kind of rape camp or at least a very intense breeding program.</div> </div> </div> </div>When a mommy beastwoman and a daddy beastman love each other <i>very much</i>, they get married and make some baby beastmen.<br /> <br /> No effort is required on their great-great-great-great(+30 more greats) grandfather, Ma-Ha-Suchi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T18:42:55-08:00","id":1289053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1289000#post1289000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure that's because you're not supposed to be able to do so, because some of those merits would be hella broken if you could buy them with background points.</div> </div> </div> </div>True but things like the Armour should count as mutations for chimerical soul. Heck, it is not like birds need the wings merit but Birdperson shapes might.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T18:48:14-08:00","id":1289055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288895#post1288895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless the origin of Beastmen has changed he is definitely running some kind of rape camp or at least a very intense breeding program.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's been at least a millennium since the Usurpation. Why would he need breeding camps to have tribes' worth of descendants?<br /> <br /> (also we know already there are other origins of Beastmen - Lunars are going to have charms to turn willing &quot;normal&quot; humans into Beastmen through trials)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T18:59:45-08:00","id":1289058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288805#post1288805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is literally an entire splat that tells players in every version of the Lore that they are objectively the bad guys and should feel bad for playing them. It can get frustrating to DB fans that they are always portrayed as bad guys. Yeah, this is Lunars and the wrong place for this discussion because the Lunars book absolutely should be portraying the Realm as bad guys, but the DB book made them bad guys too, so there is some understandable frustration going around.<br /> <br /> I put a lot of effort into planning out a rather epic Realm Civil War campaign and it fell apart before it began because I couldn't get the players to buy into the Realm culture even a little bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, before typing this response I took the day and re-read the entire section on Great Houses, and the new Lunar setting pieces that we got to compare. I don't think that the DB book necessarily always treats the Dynasts as villains, but it almost never treats them as heroes either, which is something the Lunar book does really well.<br /> <br /> In really oversimplified short, the good parts of the Realm are that they unify areas under their control, build infrastructure, promote trade, defend the people from outside forces and apply a kind of rule of law to protect people from inside forces. The villainous things they do are extract wealth, destroy culture, restrict freedom, and enforce it all with violence and fear. Also they acquire new lands through either invasion or exploitation.<br /> <br /> The good parts of the Silver Pact are that they fight the tyranny of the Realm, promote freedom for the cultures they target, and the societies under their direct rule flourish with their guidance. The villainous things they do are act like violent insurgents or criminals who leverage the suffering of innocent people, and have a callous lack of concern for collateral damage in their war.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Both of those offer a really good setting to be heroes or villains in. As a Lunar hero, the path is obvious, your enemies in the Realm are the soldiers who are lining up frightened civilians for mass execution, or the invading army of the Realm who's decided that an independent border kingdom has been a thorn in their side for too long. You're infiltrating the cruel satrap's palace, assassinating him, and destroying precious Thousand Scale records, or maybe even raising an army yourself and kicking them out once and for all. All of this culminates in a great battle sparked off at a would-be execution, where the tables are turned and it's the executioners blood on the sand. The great liberators, exalted heroes who cast of the chains of slavery, be they literal chains or metaphorical ones. Heroes who might even start on overthrowing the Empire in its entirety.<br /> <br /> As a Dynast hero, you're battling the inhuman march of undead that a Lunar necromancer has unleashed upon your satrapy. Their cold hands grasping for the throats of farmers and children, but your hearth, and your brave soldiers who have sailed here from 1,000 miles away to defend them, won't let that happen. Then once the people can sleep soundly in their beds again, you must decide whether to hunt down that Lunar anathema, or start work on investigating a possible guild ploy to get the entire town addicted to opioid drugs as a means of controlling them. You could even look to the people that your house's harsh taxes are draining dry and think to yourself &quot;There's got to be a better way than this.&quot; and start on actually fixing the Realm.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Lunar book does a super solid job of showing both sides of those stories, the DB book, not so much. There a lot of Lunar heroes in the Lunar book who fit the description of the above kind of PC hero, but very few Dynasts in the DB book who fit the Dynastic one.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the other hand, fuck yeah Lunars: Fangs at the Gate. I fucking <i>like </i>the DB book and this one is shaping up to be even better. All of the characters are really interesting, they're not flawless, and they're not exactly taking up a ton of space that PCs might want to be filling, but at the same time they're acting as great inspiration, and awesome NPC characters to interact with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T20:38:21-08:00","id":1289074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1289053#post1289053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True but things like the Armour should count as mutations for chimerical soul. Heck, it is not like birds need the wings merit but Birdperson shapes might.</div> </div> </div> </div>The core book has merits that give extra soak and wings with costs in merit dots. I'm ...not sure what you're saying here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T20:43:46-08:00","id":1289075,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping Tayan Silver Crowned and her Shadow Fang Vanguard receive more attention, either later in Fangs or at least in Many-Faced Strangers.<br /> <br /> Her school is the most distinct of the Pact, so I would have thought Tayan would get more coverage already, instead of someone like Ruksara-Who-Remembers.<br /> <br /> I appreciate that at least her school gets additional representation through details on her own teacher and advisor.<br /> <br /> Some of Tayan's &quot;Pact Relations&quot; are already covered in the sidebar on her school, but we don't know how much of that is a reflection of her personal feelings as opposed to the collective, aggregate stance of her adherents.<br /> <br /> We also don't know any of her adherents or her relationships with them, though that might come up later in the book, in the same way that Lilith came up in a passing mention.<br /> <br /> The next chapter should cover Dominions, and I can hope that the book will reveal that Vanguard holds an impressive one which will tell us more about the school.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T22:04:01-08:00","id":1289097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1289058#post1289058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> In really oversimplified short, the good parts of the Realm are that they unify areas under their control, build infrastructure, promote trade, defend the people from outside forces and apply a kind of rule of law to protect people from inside forces. The villainous things they do are extract wealth, destroy culture, restrict freedom, and enforce it all with violence and fear. Also they acquire new lands through either invasion or exploitation. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess a thing to me to remember is that while the Realm does those good things, it should be noted it's not altruistically a lot of the time. Think about ancient Rome and Han China there. The roads weren't for the folks in Judea or the former state of Qi. They were for the empire to better extract that wealth.<br /> <br /> To me that's the big thing though that gets lost in tehs ediscussions. Empires are institutions, which people are part of. <i>Individual people</i> are still able to be judged as good or not. <i>Empires</i> by their nature are about controlling other nations for extration of wealth or exertion of power. Folks can be good or bad in that context.<br /> <br /> And I think in this regard, the Realm is actually <i>not</i> an evil empire. Evil empires in fantasy often are evil because it goes out of its way to be sadistic/destructive/etc. Your cliche fantasy empire is either some asshole state ran with assholes, or it is this thing where apparenlty you have super powerful aboslute monarchs who decide its moral character (basically buying into the idea that a state is just its sovereign or something).<br /> <br /> The Realm's issues, though, are not becuase it's full of evil people, but because it's built on exploitive institutions. It doesn't just murder villagers becuase some nobleperson has cart blanch to that. It does it because, much of the time, there's a reason to it. That reason is mind, grand scale theft. But we seem to be able to ahve Rome be something folks find fascinating and a cultural touchstone even though it crucified a lot of people and did outright ethnic cleansing when push came to shove, and often for shit that's actually pretty petty for the Realm (glory and such, like conquering Britainia). The Realm's wrongs are built on <i>real world</i> wrongs, not cartoonish ones. It's what makes it both more interesitng an empire, and more compelling to play in.<br /> <br /> Mind, that I think <i>I live in the Empire</i> right now kind of makes me less willing ot be so judgemental of the people living in that system. Because a lot of the &quot;But folks who live on teh Blessed Isle have it good&quot; kind of can be turned ot the US and arguments I've seen of &quot;Even the poorest in the US is better than in less devleoped palces&quot;. WHich, even if true (it's debatalbe) misses a point that some places are bad <i>because of the US</i>. &quot;Peasants in the Reealm are relatively safe and secure&quot; kind of hits a simlar tune to me.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T00:33:36-08:00","id":1289126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1289097#post1289097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess a thing to me to remember is that while the Realm does those good things, it should be noted it's not altruistically a lot of the time. Think about ancient Rome and Han China there. The roads weren't for the folks in Judea or the former state of Qi. They were for the empire to better extract that wealth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite, quite. I just hope that we don't lose sight of the other good things that groups who are not empires might be doing for their own not exactly altruistic reasons. Or even straight up terrible things. Which is good, because it really seems to me that the developers haven't ignored that at all, and have found a really good balance in Lunars of how to play around that. Lunars, for example, definitely turn Realm barracks into abattoirs while leaving just enough people alive to spread the descriptions of the horrors they witnessed. There are also a few Lunars who would have no problem with the Creation equivalent of bombing an Ariana Grande concert if they were using it to goad House Cathak into an enraged and clumsy attack of retribution.<br /> <br /> So we need the Lunars who do that kind of thing without having the Silver Pact in general just being every bad thing that a rebel group has ever done. If you offer up the idea of running a game as members of the Silver Pact and everyone in your group rolls their eyes and says &quot;The marketplace bombing extremist group? Yeah we'll pass, thanks. How about we play Solars instead?&quot; then the Pact failed as a PC option in the game of Exalted.<br /> <br /> We need the Realm to be a place that players can actually get invested in as well. The Realm book isn't out yet though, so hopefully we get some of that in there. It<i>really really really </i>shouldn't be a big thing in it though. The Realm as it exists should primarily be its Dynasts focused on petty squabbling over power and all that good stuff, which is what the splatbook more focused on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T02:50:22-08:00","id":1289135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288895#post1288895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless the origin of Beastmen has changed he is definitely running some kind of rape camp or at least a very intense breeding program.</div> </div> </div> </div> Camps wouldn't really work as a means of population expansion and are largely a byproduct of simulationist thought ignoring factors that won't come up unless the Storyteller is eyeing the situation critically and throwing in complications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 02-18-2019, 05:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T04:37:03-08:00","id":1289145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1288895#post1288895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless the origin of Beastmen has changed he is definitely running some kind of rape camp or at least a very intense breeding program.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was hoping to see a moratorium on this kind of talk. -_-","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-18-2019, 07:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T07:59:41-08:00","id":1289191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1289126#post1289126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quite, quite. I just hope that we don't lose sight of the other good things that groups who are not empires might be doing for their own not exactly altruistic reasons. Or even straight up terrible things. Which is good, because it really seems to me that the developers haven't ignored that at all, and have found a really good balance in Lunars of how to play around that. Lunars, for example, definitely turn Realm barracks into abattoirs while leaving just enough people alive to spread the descriptions of the horrors they witnessed. There are also a few Lunars who would have no problem with the Creation equivalent of bombing an Ariana Grande concert if they were using it to goad House Cathak into an enraged and clumsy attack of retribution.<br /> <br /> So we need the Lunars who do that kind of thing without having the Silver Pact in general just being every bad thing that a rebel group has ever done. If you offer up the idea of running a game as members of the Silver Pact and everyone in your group rolls their eyes and says &quot;The marketplace bombing extremist group? Yeah we'll pass, thanks. How about we play Solars instead?&quot; then the Pact failed as a PC option in the game of Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would actually peg the typical Lunar Dominion as being pretty more similar to the Realm than a typical &quot;rebel group,&quot; in the sense that what your typical Lunar creates is going to be tributary state with a pseudo-racialized aristocracy emanating from the charismatic court*, with a structural interest in spreading certain kinds of religious practices. We'll see more about how/if this plays out in the preview on Tuesday, but it looks like one of the major ideological splits in the Pact is &quot;We should rule Creation in a Lunar Deliberative&quot;/&quot;Every Lunar Dominion should be ruled by a single absolute god-king&quot; which fits in with state-building being pretty much taken for granted.<br /> <br /> (And of course IRL rebel groups are mostly interested in state-building themselves, but I guess the relevant difference is acting in territory you control vs. that under the more formal control of another state. So I guess there's a degree to which this is a matter of playing offense vs. defense.)<br /> <br /> *This is another reason why rape camps don't make a lot of sense, in addition to all the others and also it just being bad taste OOC: you don't want as many Beastmen as possible. What you want is for beastfolk status to be indicative of closeness and loyalty to the sacred monster-king.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3457-matthias","name":"Matthias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T09:16:10-08:00","id":1289203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1289145#post1289145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was hoping to see a moratorium on this kind of talk. -_-</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm afraid, when discussing games on the internet, that's probably never going to happen.<br /> <br /> (Incidentally, did anyone else notice that Passion-Unbinding Bachanalia is an orgy charm written with no rape? It's better for games, avoids potentially triggering issues, makes it more viable for a non-monster to use, and is actually more realistic.<br /> <br /> At first, I was like &quot;An athletic display? That's kind of stupid,&quot; but then I realised, no, horny men absolutely will make idiots of themselves showing off how they can dive from a roof or do the most push-ups or something like that in order to try and impress girls at a party.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T09:21:09-08:00","id":1289204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1289145#post1289145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was hoping to see a moratorium on this kind of talk. -_-</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider it the death throes of the subject.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1289097#post1289097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess a thing to me to remember is that while the Realm does those good things, it should be noted it's not altruistically a lot of the time. Think about ancient Rome and Han China there. The roads weren't for the folks in Judea or the former state of Qi. They were for the empire to better extract that wealth.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it's not even the most efficient use of those resources. It's all short-term and sinking sand.<br /> <br /> Imperialism, among other things, is the desire to take the resources that others have already produced, without needing to go to the effort of producing those resources themselves, or offering as much in free exchange as the second party would demand.<br /> <br /> &quot;Barbarian raiders&quot; who would rather raid agricultural societies for food and metal tools rather than growing their own crops or mining their own steel are a form of imperialism, especially if they formalize a demand of tribute in exchange for NOT raiding people. For example, the Danes and their practice of &quot;Danegeld&quot; (literally &quot;Dane gold&quot;) appeasement against victim nations.<br /> <br /> This is just one step away from imperialism, as the Danes didn't attempt to occupy or govern the people they stole from, but you can't have full imperialism without this basic level of vampirism.<br /> <br /> Regardless, it's a fool's game.<br /> <br /> The Realm of the Scarlet Dynasty could instead focus on building things for itself. Instead of building roads in foreign countries, they could build more roads in their own country. Instead of training more soldiers than they need for self-defense, they could train only as many soldiers as they need to defend their homeland, and so tax their farmers less to maintain national defense. Or they could hire out the legions to foreign nations as mercenary defenders, which would be an additional source of national revenue without the same costs associated with military occupation, which would still lead to taxing the farmers less.<br /> <br /> If the farmers are taxed less, they seldom suffer from famine or malnutrition. They can produce enough to feed themselves and still have surplus goods to trade with each other and other peasants. The commoner-level economy starts to grow and thrive, creating a middle class, which creates a demand for education. With a more educated commoner class, they discover new techniques and tools for improving agricultural production further, as well as discovering new products to create and exchange with each other. More wealth and assets are generated in an iterative process that produces more wealth and more assets.<br /> <br /> This same process would be repeated in the Threshold if the Scarlet Empire wasn't forcing those countries to tax their farmers to death to pay the Realm's tribute (Danegeld), and forcing its citizens to house the Realm's occupying soldiers.<br /> <br /> This is a long game, but not a fool's game. There are no rebellions, there are fewer wars (since foreign trade is far more profitable for both sides), and no one nation becomes dependent on another nation for its quality of life.<br /> <br /> If the Blessed Isle were, tomorrow, somehow be cut off from the rest of Creation, its economy would collapse in short order because it doesn't produce nearly enough wealth at home to sustain itself. They have the raw resources, but not the infrastructure to process them.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Threshold would shortly experience a renaissance as Satrapies stop taxing their farmers and let them get back to the business of surviving and making the world iteratively better for themselves and their children. No longer forced to pay Realm tributes, countries would stop raiding their neighbors, so those neighbors could also stop devoting so many resources to defense and return to the business of living and making the world iteratively better for themselves and their children.<br /> <br /> Imperialism creates a blackhole of resources and human energy, which ultimately degrades the entire world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T09:52:05-08:00","id":1289215,"title":"","content":"It should be noted that under the Empress the Realm was better at this than most historic analogs (which makes sense, since it\u2019s Imperialists have Bureaucracy Charms). Specifically Empires often end up serving the interests of a few in their homeland at the state\u2019s expense. The Realm is no less exploitative of its satraps, but under the Empress it did benefit the Realm as a whole, not just cram the personal coffers of the House Matriarchs. Realm peasants were some of the lightest taxed people in Creation - that\u2019s what the conquered were for.<br /> <br /> Of course with all the Houses now working at cross purposes, that\u2019s collapsing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T10:02:17-08:00","id":1289220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1289215#post1289215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should be noted that under the Empress the Realm was better at this than most historic analogs (which makes sense, since it\u2019s Imperialists have Bureaucracy Charms). Specifically Empires often end up serving the interests of a few in their homeland at the state\u2019s expense. The Realm is no less exploitative of its satraps, but under the Empress it did benefit the Realm as a whole, not just cram the personal coffers of the House Matriarchs. Realm peasants were some of the lightest taxed people in Creation - that\u2019s what the conquered were for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even so, the Realm experiences a severe drain on manpower and brainpower with all of the Terrestrial Exalted who leave the Blessed Isle to raid and pillage and occupy instead of staying at home to contribute to the improvement of the Blessed Isle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T21:19:19-08:00","id":1290232,"title":"","content":"Art Upgrade Get!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T22:17:00-08:00","id":1290241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1289203#post1289203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm afraid, when discussing games on the internet, that's probably never going to happen.<br /> <br /> (Incidentally, did anyone else notice that Passion-Unbinding Bachanalia is an orgy charm written with no rape? It's better for games, avoids potentially triggering issues, makes it more viable for a non-monster to use, and is actually more realistic.<br /> <br /> At first, I was like &amp;quot;An athletic display? That's kind of stupid,&amp;quot; but then I realised, no, horny men absolutely will make idiots of themselves showing off how they can dive from a roof or do the most push-ups or something like that in order to try and impress girls at a party.)</div> </div> </div> </div>And for a more mythical example, lemme just roll this golden apple marked with &quot;to the prettiest one&quot; into the room...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T22:27:49-08:00","id":1290242,"title":"","content":"Lunars Kickstarter is live, and it is...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://thumbs.gfycat.com/BonySaltyIndochinahogdeer-max-1mb.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Seriously, though, they were my second least favorite Exalt and I cannot get enough of this damn book!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T23:14:22-08:00","id":1290255,"title":"","content":"And we have broken 185K! nice artwork here we come.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T00:12:24-08:00","id":1290263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1290242#post1290242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll