achments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T11:12:17-08:00","id":1290438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1290432#post1290432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She, actually. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You wrote lots of characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T11:28:20-08:00","id":1290447,"title":"","content":"After looking at these charms, I\u2019m pretty confident that you could do Alucard from Hellsing as a Lunar. Granted, I can see him working as a Demon or an Abyssal, but, from the powers he displays, I\u2019ve thought he might make a good Lunar for awhile now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 02-21-2019, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T11:39:20-08:00","id":1290452,"title":"","content":"I agree.<br /> Honestly, Dracula has always been a bit Lunar-esque; the bat associations, the various transformations.<br /> <br /> Hey, I even used a vampire-bat-totem Lunar as an NPC in my game (who was also a reference to a kung-film called Evil Cult. The Evil Cult is, we think, Zorastrians. Or maybe Manicheans).<br /> <br /> Alucard specifically, you can also throw in all the terror stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T12:03:26-08:00","id":1290468,"title":"","content":"Breaking and entering then leaving a message along the lines of &quot;Thats a nice face you have, I think I'll be taking it. But I had a big lunch so I'm not going to eat you, <i>this time</i>. PS-did have room for a snack so I ate your canary&quot; painted on their wall in blood to get someones shape seems hilarious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T12:44:31-08:00","id":1290495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1290447#post1290447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After looking at these charms, I\u2019m pretty confident that you could do Alucard from Hellsing as a Lunar. Granted, I can see him working as a Demon or an Abyssal, but, from the powers he displays, I\u2019ve thought he might make a good Lunar for awhile now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh.<br /> <br /> Dexterity-focused Lunar locked into epic duel against Sidereal wielding Obsidian Shards of Infinity Style: Okay, I know it's filthy rich coming from me, but <i>your powers are <b>bullshit</b></i>!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T13:21:24-08:00","id":1290511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1290495#post1290495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heh.<br /> <br /> Dexterity-focused Lunar locked into epic duel against Sidereal wielding Obsidian Shards of Infinity Style: Okay, I know it's filthy rich coming from me, but <i>your powers are <b>bullshit</b></i>!</div> </div> </div> </div>Hah, brilliant. It\u2019s going to be hard waiting for Obsidian Shards to make this a reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T16:03:33-08:00","id":1290565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1290447#post1290447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After looking at these charms, I\u2019m pretty confident that you could do Alucard from Hellsing as a Lunar. Granted, I can see him working as a Demon or an Abyssal, but, from the powers he displays, I\u2019ve thought he might make a good Lunar for awhile now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't more of Alucard supposed to go in the Abyssal wheelhouse this time around? What with the abandonment of grotesque and slimy powers and their adoption by the Liminals and all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T16:12:27-08:00","id":1290573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1290565#post1290565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wasn't more of Alucard supposed to go in the Abyssal wheelhouse this time around? What with the abandonment of grotesque and slimy powers and their adoption by the Liminals and all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this an expression of being dissatisfied about the direction that the Lunar powers are going, or thinking that Alucard's powers are unsuited to them, or having a particular thing he does in mind or what is it?<br /> <br /> Like, one think I'll say is that I would expect a Lunar shooting out a biting dog head when somebody attacks them is that it would have... fewer eyes than Alucard's Baskerville does. But it's here as a Charm now, I can't really find it to not be fitting, and I find it reminiscent of Alucard's fight with Luke Valentine.<br /> <br /> So is it something specific, or just the general principle of &quot;Alucard was made off limits&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T16:34:49-08:00","id":1290590,"title":"","content":"I tend to read books straight through but do reference work in PDF with search and contents.<br /> <br /> Something that some other games have done amazingly right is the <i>lavish </i>internal linking of their PDFs. If you're browsing a power or something, and can click straight to the rules that use them, to it's prereqs, and so on, I really appreciate that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T17:20:11-08:00","id":1290603,"title":"","content":"The bit where Alucard removes his restrictions and then turns into a dark portal to a black realm full of eyes can just be your No Moon anima going off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T17:51:53-08:00","id":1290612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1290573#post1290573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this an expression of being dissatisfied about the direction that the Lunar powers are going, or thinking that Alucard's powers are unsuited to them, or having a particular thing he does in mind or what is it?<br /> <br /> Like, one think I'll say is that I would expect a Lunar shooting out a biting dog head when somebody attacks them is that it would have... fewer eyes than Alucard's Baskerville does. But it's here as a Charm now, I can't really find it to not be fitting, and I find it reminiscent of Alucard's fight with Luke Valentine.<br /> <br /> So is it something specific, or just the general principle of &quot;Alucard was made off limits&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd imagine that a Lunar in the Luke Valentine fight would probably keep their limbs attached to a trunk rather than having them float in the air or crawl around on their own. The underpinnings of Hellsing vampire powers also feel like that could work better in an edition where non-Sidereals can have as many familiars as they care to pay for, enabling a closer lineup with Alucard's #Lifehack, especially if Abyssals can get ghosts as familiars like Twilights with other spirits.<br /> <br /> This also is riding on my having burnt out hard on Lunar Dracula/Alucard what seems like ages ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T18:46:03-08:00","id":1290623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1290511#post1290511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hah, brilliant. It\u2019s going to be hard waiting for Obsidian Shards to make this a reality.</div> </div> </div> </div> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880953-obsidian-shards-of-infinity-style-ex3-version-peach\">Why wait?</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T06:38:56-08:00","id":1290737,"title":"","content":"Artwork of Charms Part 2 looks more Infernal than Lunar, that's a lot of green.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T07:00:52-08:00","id":1290746,"title":"","content":"An old lady spitting out a swarm of bugs does feel Lunar though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T07:37:14-08:00","id":1290755,"title":"","content":"I know the Thousand Stream River from 2E as a uniting Lunar cause didn\u2019t work because it didn\u2019t actually reflect a shared Lunar experience the way the struggle against the Realm does - but I am thinking it does work as a philosophy within the Silver Pact espoused by some Shahan-ya and opposed by others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T08:33:58-08:00","id":1290781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1290755#post1290755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know the Thousand Stream River from 2E as a uniting Lunar cause didn\u2019t work because it didn\u2019t actually reflect a shared Lunar experience the way the struggle against the Realm does - but I am thinking it does work as a philosophy within the Silver Pact espoused by some Shahan-ya and opposed by others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't the philosophy basically, &quot;Create an impossible mortal-only society that doesn't need Exalted to survive in this hostile magical universe&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T08:51:04-08:00","id":1290785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1290781#post1290781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't the philosophy basically, &quot;Create an impossible mortal-only society that doesn't need Exalted to survive in this hostile magical universe&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn\u2019t need Exalted RULERSHIP. Lunar Stewards protected them from supernatural threats like the Fair Folk, but the goal was societies that were stable and culturally prosperous in their own right. There\u2019s an underlying hypocrisy in that Lunars we\u2019re designing said societies, but that level of hypocrisy strikes me as philosophically realistic.<br /> <br /> In 3E i\u2019d put focus on a divide between those who believe in building up infrastructure and organized societies as bulwarks strong enough to resist the Realm, and those who believe all such infrastructure can be usurped by the Realm, and it should all be ripped out and mortal society pushed back to Hunter-gatherers in wilderness to play to Lunar strengths that the Realm can\u2019t co-opt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 02-22-2019, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T09:51:07-08:00","id":1290807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1290785#post1290785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn\u2019t need Exalted RULERSHIP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said: Impossible. Because if Exalted aren't in charge, then outside Exalted or something else supernatural will take charge. You can't have Exalted protecting the society from other Exalted, because eventually one of those Exalted will decide to take charge or the mortals will come to them begging them to take charge.<br /> <br /> The Exalted are, by definition, the most qualified leaders around. They were made to lead the rest of humanity. This is inescapable.<br /> <br /> If someone finds that horrible, then mine it for horror. I've seen at least one fanfic writer who designed an entire mortal society that lived in terror of any one of them becoming an Exalt and basically existing as a distopian state that constantly screened their best and brightest for signs of Exaltation, with third-strike checks putting them in life-threatening situations to see if they'd manifest an anima banner. Because these people were absolutely terrified that anyone might have supernatural powers of persuasion.<br /> <br /> Well, the people who ran the world, anyway. The unwashed, unenlightened masses were simply told all Exalted were demons who possessed people.<br /> <br /> But the most insidious thing about the story was that the author was actually able to make me look upon Exaltation as a thing of horror, that really did elevate someone above humanity, granting them greater power to dominate the world through force of arms, art of speach, or unreproducible engines of terror and control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T10:22:35-08:00","id":1290822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1290807#post1290807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said: Impossible. Because if Exalted aren't in charge, then outside Exalted or something else supernatural will take charge. You can't have Exalted protecting the society from other Exalted, because eventually one of those Exalted will decide to take charge or the mortals will come to them begging them to take charge.<br /> <br /> The Exalted are, by definition, the most qualified leaders around. They were made to lead the rest of humanity. This is inescapable.<br /> <br /> If someone finds that horrible, then mine it for horror. I've seen at least one fanfic writer who designed an entire mortal society that lived in terror of any one of them becoming an Exalt and basically existing as a distopian state that constantly screened their best and brightest for signs of Exaltation, with third-strike checks putting them in life-threatening situations to see if they'd manifest an anima banner. Because these people were absolutely terrified that anyone might have supernatural powers of persuasion.<br /> <br /> Well, the people who ran the world, anyway. The unwashed, unenlightened masses were simply told all Exalted were demons who possessed people.<br /> <br /> But the most insidious thing about the story was that the author was actually able to make me look upon Exaltation as a thing of horror, that really did elevate someone above humanity, granting them greater power to dominate the world through force of arms, art of speach, or unreproducible engines of terror and control.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Haslanti, Coral, Halta, etc, are doing fine without Exalted rulership. The Thousand Stream River response to \u201ceventually an Exalted will decide they\u2019re in charge\u201d was \u201cand them the Silver Pact will execute that Exalted. Next problem?\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 02-22-2019, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T11:01:49-08:00","id":1290832,"title":"","content":"Every single time in history that someone has tried to create an elite force to safeguard the nation, with unbreakable loyalty to that nation above all, within three or four generations that nation has been ruled by that force, usually via puppet rulers that force choses. Janissaries do not work in the long run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T11:16:16-08:00","id":1290839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1290832#post1290832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every single time in history that someone has tried to create an elite force to safeguard the nation, with unbreakable loyalty to that nation above all, within three or four generations that nation has been ruled by that force, usually via puppet rulers that force choses. Janissaries do not work in the long run.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair. Like I said, there is realistic hypocrisy in this philosophy that I acknowledge and am i\u2019m fine with as something people in-setting would be guilty of.<br /> <br /> That said, I do think the time tables gets extended when your initial safe-guarders have 3,000 year life spans.<br /> <br /> <br /> In any event, as I said in my initial post on the topic, I think in 3E it would play out less as a high minded philosophy, and more as a movement among Lunars who think building complex societies strong enough to resist the Realm is their best tactic, as opposed to rivals who think all such infrastructure is co-optable and humans should be stripped down to Hunter-gatherers to best cripple the Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T11:22:11-08:00","id":1290843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1290832#post1290832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every single time in history that someone has tried to create an elite force to safeguard the nation, with unbreakable loyalty to that nation above all, within three or four generations that nation has been ruled by that force, usually via puppet rulers that force choses. Janissaries do not work in the long run.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because when you have a monopoly on violence, and no one can tell you &quot;no&quot;, why AREN'T you the one making decisions?<br /> <br /> What good is protecting a country when clearly no one else but you knows how to run the country properly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T13:59:46-08:00","id":1290901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1290612#post1290612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd imagine that a Lunar in the Luke Valentine fight would probably keep their limbs attached to a trunk rather than having them float in the air or crawl around on their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>One, reminiscent does not mean identically the same.<br /> <br /> Two, that fight has Alucard straight up shoot a big mutant dog out of his chest while dissolving into a pile of snakes and bugs. The limb doesn't float around in the air, it springs out of the dog's mouth.<br /> <br /> Lunars now, or will in the future, have Charms to turn into swarms of stuff, and we've now been shown a Dexterity Charm in which you can respond to attacks by having stuff like animal heads or insect swarms spring out of you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The underpinnings of Hellsing vampire powers also feel like that could work better in an edition where non-Sidereals can have as many familiars as they care to pay for, enabling a closer lineup with Alucard's #Lifehack, especially if Abyssals can get ghosts as familiars like Twilights with other spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like... just because they're called familiars in the source material doesn't mean they have to be modelled with the game's Familiar rules.<br /> <br /> I don't think Lunars really need ghost powers considering that they can internalize a person's shape by eating them. And their memories and personality traits, with the right Intelligence Charm.<br /> <br /> There are already a few Charms based on the image of evoking your entire Heart's Blood library at once in some kind of terrifying display. Those aren't based on having a command of the dead.<br /> <br /> I've not even started reading the proper Dexterity and Intelligence Charms yet.<br /> <br /> For that matter... can you <b>not</b> have as many Familiars as you care to pay for (which I presume is largely predicated on enhancements through Charms, since Familiar is a Story Merit)?<br /> <br /> Actually, looking back... yeah, explicitly a Merit you can have as many times as you want.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T22:17:30-08:00","id":1291009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1290785#post1290785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... In 3E i\u2019d put focus on a divide between those who believe in building up infrastructure and organized societies as bulwarks strong enough to resist the Realm, and those who believe all such infrastructure can be usurped by the Realm, and it should all be ripped out and mortal society pushed back to Hunter-gatherers in wilderness to play to Lunar strengths that the Realm can\u2019t co-opt.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lunars who make war on the Realm seem less interested in the whole hunter-gathering thing than in previous editions. I'm pretty sure Lunars are not so against going against the Realm with bronze, steel, and crossbows if they have to. A lot of the infrastructure the Realm have broken is magical stuff. They seem just fine co-opting friendly cities and steppe horsemen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T22:23:26-08:00","id":1291011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1291009#post1291009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Lunars who make war on the Realm seem less interested in the whole hunter-gathering thing than in previous editions. I'm pretty sure Lunars are not so against going against the Realm with bronze, steel, and crossbows if they have to. A lot of the infrastructure the Realm have broken is magical stuff. They seem just fine co-opting friendly cities and steppe horsemen.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s why I described opposing philosophies in how to fight the Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T23:12:11-08:00","id":1291017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1291011#post1291011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s why I described opposing philosophies in how to fight the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I don't see what it adds besides pushing a false dichotomy of infrastructure/cities and barbarism, that I think Lunars just kind of drops wholesale thsi edition. The infastructure stuff seems pretty clearly about First Age things, and there's actually a couple Lunars talked about in history who did that. And different philosophies of how to do the war in general at this point are the purview of individual shahan-ya more than anything I would think at this point.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T10:58:39-08:00","id":1291188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1290901#post1290901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One, reminiscent does not mean identically the same.<br /> <br /> Two, that fight has Alucard straight up shoot a big mutant dog out of his chest while dissolving into a pile of snakes and bugs. The limb doesn't float around in the air, it springs out of the dog's mouth.<br /> <br /> Lunars now, or will in the future, have Charms to turn into swarms of stuff, and we've now been shown a Dexterity Charm in which you can respond to attacks by having stuff like animal heads or insect swarms spring out of you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair, but his head and limbs did fall off with fine wounds like a cut to each where the joint meets the trunk, which is probably not very Lunar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like... just because they're called familiars in the source material doesn't mean they have to be modelled with the game's Familiar rules.<br /> <br /> I don't think Lunars really need ghost powers considering that they can internalize a person's shape by eating them. And their memories and personality traits, with the right Intelligence Charm.<br /> <br /> There are already a few Charms based on the image of evoking your entire Heart's Blood library at once in some kind of terrifying display. Those aren't based on having a command of the dead.<br /> <br /> I've not even started reading the proper Dexterity and Intelligence Charms yet.<br /> <br /> For that matter... can you <b>not</b> have as many Familiars as you care to pay for (which I presume is largely predicated on enhancements through Charms, since Familiar is a Story Merit)?<br /> <br /> Actually, looking back... yeah, explicitly a Merit you can have as many times as you want. </div> </div> </div>One giant sticking point is that all of Alucard's #Lifehack is transient. He takes in lives, uses them up as shields or temporary minions, and if they get killed, they're gone. There is no library of forms tied to an inner self, and no duplication or customization of appearances, with the possible exception of Girlycard.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, I think that familiars in both settings is about the right place to go. XP debt may be involved, and they might not actually be ghosts, but they are lives ripped away, and each has only itself to give before dying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T11:13:25-08:00","id":1291198,"title":"","content":"I think Both Alucard and Lunars evoke the whole \u201cI eat part of your spirit when I eat you\u201d motif the same that you see with certain cannibals. So it\u2019s not necessarily necromancy but it can be represented that way, but Lunars can represent it as sort of a primal Blood animus drinking \u201cmagic\u201d. I think it would be interesting to have a way for their Hearts library to be depleted if they can project it and some of those projections are killed. It would be a fun gamble for rare or singularly unique specimens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T11:14:55-08:00","id":1291199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1290832#post1290832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every single time in history that someone has tried to create an elite force to safeguard the nation, with unbreakable loyalty to that nation above all, within three or four generations that nation has been ruled by that force, usually via puppet rulers that force choses. Janissaries do not work in the long run.</div> </div> </div> </div>There hella cool though, and sometimes they lead to insane conquests by the time they take over!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T14:34:24-08:00","id":1291258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1291198#post1291198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Both Alucard and Lunars evoke the whole \u201cI eat part of your spirit when I eat you\u201d motif the same that you see with certain cannibals. So it\u2019s not necessarily necromancy but it can be represented that way, but Lunars can represent it as sort of a primal Blood animus drinking \u201cmagic\u201d. I think it would be interesting to have a way for their Hearts library to be depleted if they can project it and some of those projections are killed. It would be a fun gamble for rare or singularly unique specimens.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't really square with the non-lethal methods of form acquisition, though. Given the description of Luna from Glories, she appears to just feel out the Essence of something and take it in as a part of herself, so that's probably at least similar to what her Chosen are doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T15:05:00-08:00","id":1291264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1291188#post1291188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair, but his head and limbs did fall off with fine wounds like a cut to each where the joint meets the trunk, which is probably not very Lunar.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> One giant sticking point is that all of Alucard's #Lifehack is transient. He takes in lives, uses them up as shields or temporary minions, and if they get killed, they're gone. There is no library of forms tied to an inner self, and no duplication or customization of appearances, with the possible exception of Girlycard.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, I think that familiars in both settings is about the right place to go. XP debt may be involved, and they might not actually be ghosts, but they are lives ripped away, and each has only itself to give before dying.</div> </div> </div> </div>I look forward to the next time that Solars get compared to King Arthur being deconstructed with arguments that Arthur can't shoot golden fire, and Creation does not have Christianity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T18:02:37-08:00","id":1291334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1291258#post1291258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That doesn't really square with the non-lethal methods of form acquisition, though. Given the description of Luna from Glories, she appears to just feel out the Essence of something and take it in as a part of herself, so that's probably at least similar to what her Chosen are doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then limit it to things they killed. But I didn\u2019t say eat their soup either just a taste of Spirit which you can get from porking someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T20:16:21-08:00","id":1291409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1291264#post1291264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I look forward to the next time that Solars get compared to King Arthur being deconstructed with arguments that Arthur can't shoot golden fire, and Creation does not have Christianity.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Revered leader is totally not dead but will return!&quot; is vague and squishy - a concept applied from the top down, on a wide scale, to about 150 characters, with significantly loosened criteria. &quot;I can generate a bunch of extra bodies and take in the spirits of those I've slain!&quot; requires some more exacting structural details for its setup, operating much closer to the ground level as it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T22:19:07-08:00","id":1291429,"title":"","content":"Hey, now that we've got the character creation rules, has anyone tapped Mr. Gone on the shoulder?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11867-caffeine-delusions","name":"Caffeine Delusions","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T05:18:00-08:00","id":1291501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caffeine Delusions</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1291429#post1291429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, now that we've got the character creation rules, has anyone tapped Mr. Gone on the shoulder?</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone ever feel like you're Ma-Ha-Suchi, and someone just mentioned Lilith's name in your hearing for the first time in a century?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T09:05:38-08:00","id":1291544,"title":"","content":"Extra-big thank-you to Vance and Minton for the clarifying sidebar about cultures. Knight Raiton suddenly finds Mastery of Small Manners much more appealing!<br /> <br /> \u200b(Prior to that, he was like, &quot;Okay, sounds good, but I'm <i>from</i> Nexus and I'm operating <i>in</i> Nexus.&quot; <i>Now</i>, though, your weekly Venusday night game of poker is a culture, so Raiton will get a lot more mileage out of it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T09:45:58-08:00","id":1291554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1291544#post1291544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Extra-big thank-you to Vance and Minton for the clarifying sidebar about cultures. Knight Raiton suddenly finds Mastery of Small Manners much more appealing!<br /> <br /> \u200b(Prior to that, he was like, &amp;quot;Okay, sounds good, but I'm <i>from</i> Nexus and I'm operating <i>in</i> Nexus.&amp;quot; <i>Now</i>, though, your weekly Venusday night game of poker is a culture, so Raiton will get a lot more mileage out of it.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow that really is so much better now, I always throught it was kind of meh outside a globe trotting adventure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T10:07:16-08:00","id":1291556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1291409#post1291409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &amp;quot;Revered leader is totally not dead but will return!&amp;quot; is vague and squishy - a concept applied from the top down, on a wide scale, to about 150 characters, with significantly loosened criteria. &amp;quot;I can generate a bunch of extra bodies and take in the spirits of those I've slain!&amp;quot; requires some more exacting structural details for its setup, operating much closer to the ground level as it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, people can draw examples and find inspiration without having to get down to every exacting detail.<br /> <br /> Disregarding the fact that, considering swarm Charms and shit, and presuming a Lunar that has actually acquired at least a few hundred shapes, evoking their library as an army definitely feels like something a Lunar might do at <i>some</i> point. Perhaps not lower than at Essence 5, but some point. They won't look all corpsified and gross, and they won't be disgorged from a damn coffin, and that is about it.<br /> <br /> I mean, is deferring damage to yourself onto little dispersed and semi-independent pieces of yourself, at the cost of losing that shape, very far removed from the Essence 5 Charm to do that to a piece of land that you own?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T15:30:20-08:00","id":1291632,"title":"","content":"This was an accidental quad-post","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":".  Need to get a new mouse 02-24-2019, 06:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T15:30:20-08:00","id":1291633,"title":"","content":"This was an accidental quad-post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":".  Quad-post wtf 02-24-2019, 06:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T02:08:25-08:00","id":1291752,"title":"","content":"So, what do you think we'll get tomorrow? I suppose left there's:<br /> Dominions<br /> Animals<br /> Spells, Evocations and Martial Arts<br /> <br /> Were there any other chapters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T02:16:28-08:00","id":1291754,"title":"","content":"A comment in the second most recent update says it will be martial arts and sorcery.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8217-lukas\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8217\" data-vbnamecard=\"8217\">lukas</a> Buergi: we will celebrate Moonday with Martial Arts and Sorcery! </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T02:36:03-08:00","id":1291757,"title":"","content":"I was hoping it'd be Dominions, but that's cool too.<br /> <br /> TBH, there's been so many native charms, I haven't really thought much about MA and Sorcery. But Falcon and Centipede style sound cool. Our Zenith recently swore loyalty to the Centipede Gods, maybe he can learn Centipede style.<br /> And there's not that many published Celestial Spells, so having more will be useful for both Lunars and Solars.<br /> I had a Lunar who practiced Celestial Sorcery, who I retired (boredom and the fact there were no rules for 3rd ed). I'm tempted to have him return after the current arc, and he could do with more Celestial Spells (he had like 3, I just don't love the ones in the book that much).<br /> <br /> Though I assume it will actually be Martial Arts, Sorcery and Evocations. It'd be nice to see a bunch more Moonsilver artefacts.<br /> <br /> <br /> Presumably the update next week, the last one, will then be Dominions and Animals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-25-2019, 05:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T04:03:38-08:00","id":1291780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1291757#post1291757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Presumably the update next week, the last one, will then be Dominions and Animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>We do still have two Tuesdays before the KS ends, so I'd expect Dominions on one and NPCs &amp; Animals on the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T04:21:39-08:00","id":1291785,"title":"","content":"Is it over 5 weeks? I thought it was four.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T04:58:11-08:00","id":1291788,"title":"","content":"I'm not surprised to see Mishiko back; Vance said one initiation would be a blast from the past, and that's really the only Lunar-specific thing (other than learning it in Sperimin, I guess?).<br /> <br /> I found the story of Mishiko quite boring in 2nd ed, but as gentle and un-grimdark as this initiation is, I quite like it actually.<br /> A ghost of a sorceress makes sense, the merit works, and I like that shaping ritual as one for a sorcerer who quests for knowledge, rather than sitting in their tower. It's kind of the opposite of the Heptagram, which I find fitting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T05:16:23-08:00","id":1291791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1291757#post1291757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was hoping it'd be Dominions, but that's cool too.<br /> <br /> TBH, there's been so many native charms, I haven't really thought much about MA and Sorcery. But Falcon and Centipede style sound cool. Our Zenith recently swore loyalty to the Centipede Gods, maybe he can learn Centipede style.<br /> And there's not that many published Celestial Spells, so having more will be useful for both Lunars and Solars.<br /> I had a Lunar who practiced Celestial Sorcery, who I retired (boredom and the fact there were no rules for 3rd ed). I'm tempted to have him return after the current arc, and he could do with more Celestial Spells (he had like 3, I just don't love the ones in the book that much).<br /> <br /> Though I assume it will actually be Martial Arts, Sorcery and Evocations. It'd be nice to see a bunch more Moonsilver artefacts.<br /> <br /> <br /> Presumably the update next week, the last one, will then be Dominions and Animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't we still missing the last bit of charms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T05:28:29-08:00","id":1291794,"title":"","content":"That'll be this Friday and next Friday (and the next?). Manipulation, Perception, Stamina, Strength, Wits.<br /> <br /> I was talking about tomorrow and next Tuesday (and the next?). Martial Arts+Sorcery (+Evocations?), Dominions, Animals.<br /> <br /> I think that's everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T06:08:04-08:00","id":1291800,"title":"","content":"After thinking about it over the weekend I think I would have preferred for the Lunar Trial charm to not have the mutations breed true without a repurchase. <br /> <br /> It's not necessarily that I view the charm as too powerful, so much as it cuts off a really interesting society and culture basis. <br /> <br /> When I see that charm I think of, as the most recent example I fell in love with, Nicol Bolas' Amonkhet in Magic the Gathering. A world he created entirely based around the passing of one of his five trials, and the way this has changed and modified the culture of the plane.<br /> <br /> I think if the mutations didn't breed true, you could really examine the idea of Lunars making societies entirely around passing their trials to maintain their power, building a culture around passing the trials as a rite to adulthood.<br /> <br /> I think making them breed true removes those types of stories and cultures, which could be fertile grounds not just for Lunars and their beast men, but other sorts of Exalts as well; a Solar who Exalts in desperation to suceed, an Abyssal who fails but tenaciously clings to life rather then dying, etc.<br /> <br /> I would have preferred breeding true to be a repurchase later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T06:10:38-08:00","id":1291802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1291757#post1291757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I assume it will actually be Martial Arts, Sorcery and Evocations. It'd be nice to see a bunch more Moonsilver artefacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Artifacts get their own chapter.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T06:11:14-08:00","id":1291803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1291785#post1291785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it over 5 weeks? I thought it was four.</div> </div> </div> </div>30 days, starting 12th Feb and ending 14th March. That gives us 5 Tuesdays (12th, 19th, 26th, 5th, 12th) and 4 Fridays (15th, 22nd, 1st, 8th).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T07:35:35-08:00","id":1291824,"title":"","content":"I... don't think I've ever even heard of Mishiko. Was that a &quot;Dreams of the First Age / Lords of Creation&quot; character?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T07:41:11-08:00","id":1291827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1291824#post1291824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I... don't think I've ever even heard of Mishiko. Was that a &quot;Dreams of the First Age / Lords of Creation&quot; character?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mishiko's first appearance was in the White and Black Treatises, I believe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T07:46:11-08:00","id":1291832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1291824#post1291824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I... don't think I've ever even heard of Mishiko. Was that a &quot;Dreams of the First Age / Lords of Creation&quot; character?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> She was the daughter of the first Lunar sorcerer, sacrificed as part of his final initiation. At least, she was part of the apocryphal story of how a Bar-Izhad actually discovered sorcery.<br /> <br /> Which, of course, is probably not how it went down in 3e. But Mishiko remains a distinctly Lunar resource for learning sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Elliott | He/him | Exalted Freelancer | Vice Deputy Undersecretary to the Maiden of Secrets </i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2446-gryffon","name":"Gryffon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T08:18:27-08:00","id":1291840,"title":"","content":"Ah. Yeah, I wasn't interested in sorcery before sorcerous workings.<br /> <br /> Though it's telling that I never heard anything about her for... what, 10 or more years?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T08:22:05-08:00","id":1291842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1291802#post1291802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Artifacts get their own chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, thanks.<br /> <br /> Any favourites, Eric?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T09:15:44-08:00","id":1291855,"title":"","content":"Does anyone else think the Spider-Man web mutation is a bit overpowered for three dots, or should be split into multiple mutations with a basic mutation and advanced mutations that build on it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T09:43:40-08:00","id":1291862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1291840#post1291840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah. Yeah, I wasn't interested in sorcery before sorcerous workings.<br /> <br /> Though it's telling that I never heard anything about her for... what, 10 or more years?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's due to Solar propaganda, claiming Brigid was the discoverer of sorcery, when Lunars knew it was Mishiko. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> On a more serious note, it's because she wasn't mentioned in the Lunar book, just in the fluff part of the White and Black Treatise.<br /> <br /> I didn't find it a particularly compelling origin-story for sorcery, but then, I also didn't find Brigid's story particularly compelling.<br /> <br /> Saying this, I do like what I've seen of it in 3rd ed so far. We've had an initiation where you learn sorcery from a demon, and from an elemental, but not one from the ghost of a sorceress.<br /> <br /> And, if the other 1-3 initiations are varied, including more bizarre and perhaps bestial initiations, then it's nice to have a gentle bittersweet initiation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T10:41:43-08:00","id":1291878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1291855#post1291855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone else think the Spider-Man web mutation is a bit overpowered for three dots, or should be split into multiple mutations with a basic mutation and advanced mutations that build on it?</div> </div> </div> </div> I was going to dispute that, but rereading it...<br /> <br /> Yeah, no, I don't see how that's worth three dots, particularly next to the four-dot Serpentine (ignore penalties from being prone, and nothing else) and Hypermobility (add a die to grapple control rolls and other rolls that might benefit from being highly flexible). The ability to substitute Stamina for Strength in feats of strength is straight-up a DB Charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T10:48:54-08:00","id":1291880,"title":"","content":"I think at least part of a merit's cost is determined by how drastically it alters the body. Serpentine is a big change, and so it's worth more dots.<br /> <br /> Plus against dragon blooded it's really useful. They have smashing and prone effects coming out of their ears. If it was cheaper every lunar on Creation would have it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T10:53:26-08:00","id":1291883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1291842#post1291842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, thanks.<br /> <br /> Any favourites, Eric?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a terrible person to ask, because I wrote two of them (Phaessa and Deinon, and Eyebright), and I have an undeniable bias toward my babies.<br /> <br /> Other than that? Maybe the Ichneumon Blades; they have a really tight, flavorful, kinda disturbing design. Very well done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T11:42:03-08:00","id":1291891,"title":"","content":"Ah, on that subject of who wrote what, I generally assumed you wrote most of the fluff and Vance wrote most of the mechanics, but were there any other writers involved?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T12:02:49-08:00","id":1291897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1291891#post1291891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, on that subject of who wrote what, I generally assumed you wrote most of the fluff and Vance wrote most of the mechanics, but were there any other writers involved?</div> </div> </div> </div>We assigned each artifact to a single writer; Vance edited the mechanics and we both edited the nonmechanical material, but we didn't straight-up write all of the artifacts ourselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T12:04:21-08:00","id":1291898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1291802#post1291802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Artifacts get their own chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but we\u2019ve been getting two chapters a week on Tuesdays, so it was reasonable to assume Artifacts would be folded together with MA and Sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T12:37:36-08:00","id":1291905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1291898#post1291898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, but we\u2019ve been getting two chapters a week on Tuesdays, so it was reasonable to assume Artifacts would be folded together with MA and Sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>We do have three more Tuesdays though.<br /> <br /> But if we\u2019re getting everything in 2 more chunks, + the charm previews, it would make sense for them to pair one mechanics chapter with one setting chapter. So Martial Arts/Sorcery + NPCs tomorrow, and Artifacts + Domains next week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T13:19:41-08:00","id":1291916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1291840#post1291840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah. Yeah, I wasn't interested in sorcery before sorcerous workings.<br /> <br /> Though it's telling that I never heard anything about her for... what, 10 or more years?</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything is <i>somebody's</i> favorite, but some things don't get widely admired. I mean, I think Jadeborn are frickin' awesome, other people deeply resent the whole &quot;Obi-Wan Truth&quot; thing that birthed them. Mishiko is a pretty deep cut, lore-wise, so it's not too surprising. I mean, Brigid got an artifact at least.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T14:11:12-08:00","id":1291939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1291897#post1291897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We assigned each artifact to a single writer; Vance edited the mechanics and we both edited the nonmechanical material, but we didn't straight-up write all of the artifacts ourselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I meant the book as a whole. Though that's interesting too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T14:34:57-08:00","id":1291956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div