=\"message\">I was hoping it would be.<br /> <br /> It's also a whip Style!</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it was the Raksha Staff Shaping Style back in the day, so it should allow them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T20:54:46-08:00","id":1292363,"title":"","content":"I like all the MA styles, but when I read Falcon Style I was hit by a major urge to make a character based around the style. I LOVE it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T21:07:20-08:00","id":1292366,"title":"","content":"So, I made a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1T0A2jFMYt_LWe8ll9WKnXNWHUIkGzgbqoXMHCr7hWgU/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">list of the various mutations and their prices</a>, both in the Core and the Lunars book. For reference purposes when building various hybrid forms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T21:27:21-08:00","id":1292369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1292193#post1292193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's the intention.<br /> <br /> Notice how chairs are a form weapon?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like there's a huge flaw here: you can't train actual falcons in this style and have them then flock together to suplex your enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/563-roadie","name":"Roadie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T22:06:35-08:00","id":1292380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1292369#post1292369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like there's a huge flaw here: you can't train actual falcons in this style and have them then flock together to suplex your enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, no, but with Horses-Like-Dragons Stampede you actually COULD do that with giant riding falcons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T07:57:00-08:00","id":1292484,"title":"","content":"Splashing into Falcon, if only for Swift Talon Strike, is something every Crane stylist should consider. That Charm plus Wings Spread to Sky gives you a very easily set-up dive attack that rerolls 1s and 2s, gives the attack an auto-success, AND doubles 10s on the damage roll. Very nice for boosting Crane's actual hitting power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T18:27:25-08:00","id":1294555,"title":"","content":"Not enthused about the Caul pilgrimage. Or at least not the Water and Wood parts of it.<br /> <br /> The Water part is the lesser concern, especially if I'm misinterpreting what it says (and it certainly isn't written very clearly). I don't care for the idea of losing your reflection forever as part of this journey. As a sorcerous initiation, okay, but a journey for a Terrestrial to ensure that his or her next child will Exalted as a Dragonblood, it doesn't feel like an appropriate sacrifice, especially given the sacrifices suffered already.<br /> <br /> But at least it IS a sacrifice, which is what really bothers me about the Wood Shrine.<br /> <br /> To make a complete pilgrimage, a Dragonblood will end up murdering no less than five random people; potentially six, if the thing the Wood Shrine chooses for her to kill happens to be a local person. That's may be a ritual sacrifice to the Wood Shrine, but it is NOT a personal sacrifice on the part of the pilgrim. Saint or sinner, this pilgrimage should be an equal hardship to a Dragonblood, and murdering mortals for personal gain isn't exactly a sacrifice for many Dragonblooded.<br /> <br /> In contrast to that, I think the Earth, Fire, and Air Shrines and trials are pretty cool.<br /> <br /> The Air Shrine is the weirdest, because it's the only one that seems to function BECAUSE it was destroyed. Like, the text doesn't give me this sense at all, but I'm getting idea that whoever made the Air City specifically built it and then had people live in it for a time before deliberately destroying it so that its intended form of &quot;a city of merely memories&quot; would be fully realized.<br /> <br /> Of course the Fire City is the most EXTREME, and it's great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T03:11:35-08:00","id":1294655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1294555#post1294555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But at least it IS a sacrifice, which is what really bothers me about the Wood Shrine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess my take on the shrines isn't that they desire sacrifices from the pilgrim, they desire <i>understanding</i>.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T07:40:31-08:00","id":1294735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1294655#post1294655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess my take on the shrines isn't that they desire sacrifices from the pilgrim, they desire <i>understanding</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s more ways to understand Wood Essence than \u201cnature red in tooth and claw\u201d.<br /> <br /> And it\u2019s easily the weakest trial for being so. Either you\u2019re killing a small animal like people do every day just to eat (and nothing prevents you from eating the animal to make the most of its death) or you\u2019re murdering a person that you may not even consider a person (depending on how distanced you become from humanity or commoners outside of your Scarlet Dynasty).<br /> <br /> The only way this could be considered hard is if you\u2019re one of those absolute pacisifists who based their self-righteous on never harming another creature, or the Shrine is the one to decide what a pilgrim hunts and chooses to demand a human life of someone who would consider that murder.<br /> <br /> This trial is either no hardship at all or only a hardship at all because of arbitrary storyteller decision.<br /> <br /> At least the Earth Shrine is always a risk because no one really KNOWS what its criteria are or how badly it might choose to punish you... or how much time it takes from you even if you pass. So it is just as risky and dangerous for everyone, not just saints or just murderers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T07:51:57-08:00","id":1294740,"title":"","content":"The wood shrine's final thing once the pilgrimage is done definitely does feel silly, it's one of those 'why do you live in this otherwise totally normal city that you can find in other palaces with the understanding that sometimes you might just die for no reason.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T08:17:32-08:00","id":1294748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1294740#post1294740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The wood shrine's final thing once the pilgrimage is done definitely does feel silly, it's one of those 'why do you live in this otherwise totally normal city that you can find in other palaces with the understanding that sometimes you might just die for no reason.'</div> </div> </div> </div>That's definitely another complaint. At least with the Fire Shrine, you're safe as long as you leave the city each night, and the people who live there obviously don't actually live in the part that burns, but the city around it, and only go into the Fire City during the day to conduct business.<br /> <br /> Sure, the Wood City is currently abandoned except for its monks, but what makes ALL of those monks so devoted to the shrine that they're willing to die at random at any time? I suppose it was easier when other people lived there and might die instead, but that just raises the question of why anyone was ever willing to live there.<br /> <br /> Sure, they could all just up and leave the city for their own protection every time a pilgrim manages to pass the Earth Shrine, but then they would all need to stay out of their city until the pilgrim finishes or fails her journey, and that could take days if not weeks or longer. That's a lot more inconvenient than the Fire City.<br /> <br /> The Earth, Fire, Water, and Air cities and shrines are all great, but Wood is just dumb. It's dumb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T08:49:33-08:00","id":1294757,"title":"","content":"Well, actually no one's been on the pilgrimage for five years, so no one's died from it in five years, ie since lots of people lived there.<br /> <br /> Still, it doesn't seem very enlightened to condemn five innocents to death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T09:21:43-08:00","id":1294766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1294757#post1294757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, actually no one's been on the pilgrimage for five years, so no one's died from it in five years, ie since lots of people lived there.<br /> <br /> Still, it doesn't seem very enlightened to condemn five innocents to death.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it doesn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> But the cities are all older than the Usurpation, right? There was a point during the First Age where people lived on the Caul and Lunars or Dragon-Blooded would take the pilgrimage.<br /> <br /> The Wood City alone would need to post-date this period because no one would dare live there. Living near the Air City or Fire City is much safer.<br /> <br /> I suppose you could live NEAR the Wood City, too, and maybe that surrounding city has been reclaimed by the jungle since the Lunars drove out the people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T09:47:50-08:00","id":1294773,"title":"","content":"Eh... in the First Age, if, say, 20,000 people lived there, that 5 people dropped dead every year or two wouldn't have much significance statistically. I mean, 70-80 people in my city die in accidents every year, but it seems pretty safe to me. I still cycle to work. 96 people die of drugs every year in my city... but, obviously, people still take drugs.<br /> Actually, my city has a much higher death rate for the non-elderly than most cities in the UK, but house prices are insane because so many people want to live here.<br /> <br /> When the population is 100, 5 deaths is a lot, when it's 100,000, it's not.<br /> <br /> Hmmm... has any mention been made of how often people can do the pilgrimage? I know many simply fail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-07-2019, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T10:38:35-08:00","id":1294791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1294773#post1294773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh... in the First Age, if, say, 20,000 people lived there, that 5 people dropped dead every year or two wouldn't have much significance statistically. I mean, 70-80 people in my city die in accidents every year, but it seems pretty safe to me. I still cycle to work. 96 people die of drugs every year in my city... but, obviously, people still take drugs.<br /> Actually, my city has a much higher death rate for the non-elderly than most cities in the UK, but house prices are insane because so many people want to live here.<br /> <br /> When the population is 100, 5 deaths is a lot, when it's 100,000, it's not.<br /> <br /> Hmmm... has any mention been made of how often people can do the pilgrimage? I know many simply fail.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a difference between 'people die to drugs' and 'every time we have a municipal election 5 rocks fall from the sky only in this city and hit 5 people on the head, instantly killing them.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T10:46:53-08:00","id":1294792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1294757#post1294757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, actually no one's been on the pilgrimage for five years, so no one's died from it in five years, ie since lots of people lived there.<br /> <br /> Still, it doesn't seem very enlightened to condemn five innocents to death.</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019re conflating understanding of the elements with moral enlightenment. Adorjan is \u201cenlightened\u201d. There is no moral code built into the universe that \u201cthe enlightened\u201d are more adherent to in Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T10:47:32-08:00","id":1294795,"title":"","content":"Yes. That's going to make you want to not have elections. But an election every 2 years where 5 people die isn't going to stop you living in a city.<br /> (And, actually, in countries where elections are regularly marred by violence, it doesn't even stop always stop elections.)<br /> <br /> But the fact I know that way more than 5 people get hit by cars and die in my city every year, doesn't make me want to leave the city and go live somewhere safer, more boring, where I don't know anyone, and don't have as good a job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-07-2019, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T10:54:33-08:00","id":1294798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1294795#post1294795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. That's going to make you want to not have elections. But an election every 2 years where 5 people die isn't going to stop you living in a city.<br /> (And, actually, in countries where elections are regularly marred by violence, it doesn't even stop always stop elections.)<br /> <br /> But the fact I know that way more than 5 people get hit by cars and die in my city every year, doesn't make me want to leave the city and go live somewhere safer, more boring, where I don't know anyone, and don't have as good a job.</div> </div> </div> </div>But what if you and everyone else in the city could stop people by getting hit by cars by packing up everyone and moving a mile down the road? Then no more car wrecks and no one dies. It in no other way affects your life other then changing your address. Everything you own is still yours, all your friends are still there, and you have the same job<br /> <br /> Is it still impossible to imagine doing that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T10:57:27-08:00","id":1294799,"title":"","content":"Because down the road is full of monsters and toadmen and stuff. It's a literal jungle.<br /> <br /> (Also... my house is here. Can't move my house. I worked for years to get this house, I ain't leaving it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T11:00:30-08:00","id":1294800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1294792#post1294792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You\u2019re conflating understanding of the elements with moral enlightenment. Adorjan is \u201cenlightened\u201d. There is no moral code built into the universe that \u201cthe enlightened\u201d are more adherent to in Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, sure, but...<br /> <br /> Your PCs manage to drive the last of the evil Empire from the Caul, after a long and dramatic campaign. They've fought for the rights of the locals against the evil oppressors. Yes, you could argue some innocent Caulborn in Faxai died, slaves and so on, but that wasn't deliberate, it was a hard choice that had to be made for the greater good.<br /> <br /> So now it's time for your reward. The ST says you can do the pilgrimage. You'll get some amazing reward at the end... but also, five random, innocent people will die.<br /> <br /> It's one thing for your PC to kill Realm soldiers to free the Caul. It's another for you to kill five random locals just so you can get the reward.<br /> <br /> And the same applies for the Dragonblood, tbh.<br /> <br /> My point is that defeating the other side isn't rewarded with a numinous prize. It's rewarded for the option to get a numinous prize by killing 5 random people.<br /> <br /> Which many Dragonblood, of course, will take. But a large number, the better ones, will not. Including a fair few PCs.<br /> <br /> Weirdly, this also means that the Dragonblood who have gained the Caul's enlightenment are, for the most part, pretty awful examples of Dynasts.<br /> <br /> Unless of course, the Dragonblood don't actually realise it has this effect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-07-2019, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T11:06:22-08:00","id":1294801,"title":"","content":"I've got to admit, as things currently stand I see the appeal of driving the Realm from Faxai then immediately turning on the Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T11:11:17-08:00","id":1294802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1294799#post1294799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because down the road is full of monsters and toadmen and stuff. It's a literal jungle.<br /> <br /> (Also... my house is here. Can't move my house. I worked for years to get this house, I ain't leaving it.)</div> </div> </div> </div>What kind of monsters do you have that respect cities?<br /> <br /> I admittedly recognize most animals naturally come to fear cities and the magical nature of a demanse or shrine might heighten such actions, but any sort of 'monsters avoid it because of people' stuff would still exist when everyone moved.<br /> <br /> As for your house, at least for me, I'd rather have a house that is 100% safe from meteors destroying my skull.<br /> <br /> The car and animal analogs don't work super well because this isn't like those. This isn't someone getting run over by a cart, it's in addition to the people getting run over by carts","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T11:27:36-08:00","id":1294803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1294791#post1294791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a difference between 'people die to drugs' and 'every time we have a municipal election 5 rocks fall from the sky only in this city and hit 5 people on the head, instantly killing them.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially when it's not &quot;five rocks fall on their own&quot; but &quot;this Dragon-Blood who threw five rocks at random people to murder them&quot;.<br /> <br /> Either no one would have wanted to live in the city back when pilgrims were frequent, or they would have actively opposed letting any pilgrim into their city to protect themselves from random murders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T11:41:03-08:00","id":1294805,"title":"","content":"This is driving me crazy. I just read the Caul section of the Dominions chapter and I'm not seeing any of this info about killing random people at the Wood shrine. Did I miss an update somewhere?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T11:44:49-08:00","id":1294806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1294805#post1294805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is driving me crazy. I just read the Caul section of the Dominions chapter and I'm not seeing any of this info about killing random people at the Wood shrine. Did I miss an update somewhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Realm section on the Caul describes the pilgrimage, which is where I read it.<br /> <br /> To pass the Wood Shrine the first time you go into a dream and murder something the Shrine tells you to, either person or animal. When the pilgrimage finishes, an additional five people disappear forever, and 5 white stags appear in the shrine, dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T11:46:55-08:00","id":1294809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1294801#post1294801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got to admit, as things currently stand I see the appeal of driving the Realm from Faxai then immediately turning on the Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's kind of the idea.<br /> <br /> It's a Middle Eastern nation, and the Lunars are all those foreign fundamentalists who've turned up to fight jihad against your oppressors. Except they don't really care about you; your country is just another arena for their war, and you sure don't want them in charge at the end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T12:06:50-08:00","id":1294814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1294802#post1294802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What kind of monsters do you have that respect cities?<br /> <br /> I admittedly recognize most animals naturally come to fear cities and the magical nature of a demanse or shrine might heighten such actions, but any sort of 'monsters avoid it because of people' stuff would still exist when everyone moved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not if it's because of the magic of the wood shrine.<br /> <br /> Which on top of may well, being a wood shrine, generate healing energy or something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for your house, at least for me, I'd rather have a house that is 100% safe from meteors destroying my skull. </div> </div> </div>And do you? How much money have you spent on it? I haven't spent a penny on protecting my house from meteors. I don't think my insurance covers it, and I certainly haven't considered paying extra trying to get it added.<br /> <br /> Come on, people live near nuclear power stations despite the increased risk of cancer. They go on holiday to countries with high accident or murder rates. They do skydiving. They drive too fast. They smoke. I lived for 3 years in a city so polluted you sometimes couldn't see the buildings in the next block.<br /> People are very good at convincing themselves that something unlikely to kill you, won't kill you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The car and animal analogs don't work super well because this isn't like those. This isn't someone getting run over by a cart, it's in addition to the people getting run over by carts </div> </div> </div>Stabbings in London have risen 50% in the last two years. People aren't leaving London because of it. Hey, there was an actual terrorist attack while I lived there, which is definitely &quot;on top of&quot; regular crimes. A Jihadist drove into a crowd, then jumped out and started stabbing people. He killed five people.<br /> <br /> Didn't make me leave London.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that if five people die every couple of years from magic in a village of 200, people won't leave.<br /> <br /> And I'm not saying there doesn't need to be something to keep them there (perhaps, for example, the presence of the Wood shrine reduces deaths by disease).<br /> <br /> But if there was a huge city there in the First Age, 5 deaths every couple of years wouldn't make people leave.<br /> <br /> Medieval and industrial-era cities were death traps, with more deaths than birth... but people still moved there. (Generally. Though that's why in places like Zimbabwe and North America, cities got abandoned and people just went back to the countryside.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But Sunder is right... it would make pilgrims very, very unpopular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T12:20:08-08:00","id":1294819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1294805#post1294805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is driving me crazy. I just read the Caul section of the Dominions chapter and I'm not seeing any of this info about killing random people at the Wood shrine. Did I miss an update somewhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s in the Realm excerpt that got posted before the actual Dominions chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T12:20:47-08:00","id":1294821,"title":"","content":"Maybe the locals are religious fanatics? Dying to the shrine might be seen as the greatest and most honourable ascension to the afterlife. I\u2019m not sure if this is clairified I haven\u2019t had the chance to read it myself yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T12:23:21-08:00","id":1294823,"title":"","content":"None of those things are stopped by leaving, which is the crux of my point. I can continue to try and explain this but I want to be sure you're making an honest effort to understand what I'm saying rather then just repeating the same point over and over again as I explain how it's not related .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T12:25:18-08:00","id":1294824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1294821#post1294821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the locals are religious fanatics? Dying to the shrine might be seen as the greatest and most honourable ascension to the afterlife. I\u2019m not sure if this is clairified I haven\u2019t had the chance to read it myself yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>There could have been a culture like Shirley Jackson\u2019s The Lottery, where the occasional sacrifice of 5 random people was seen as a public good that assured all the prosperous benefits of living in the city (include quite possibly a lower rate of death than most comparable metropoli even accounting for the 5 stag deaths).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T12:25:46-08:00","id":1294825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1294821#post1294821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the locals are religious fanatics? Dying to the shrine might be seen as the greatest and most honourable ascension to the afterlife. I\u2019m not sure if this is clairified I haven\u2019t had the chance to read it myself yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not clarified, but that's certainly a plausible explanation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T12:26:22-08:00","id":1294826,"title":"","content":"Wizard, the city didn't need to be built around the Wood Shrine. The founders could have built it a safe distance away.<br /> <br /> At some point, someone had to go to the effort and risk of clearing out a part of the jungle and building a dwelling there. There was a point before the city was complete, where construction could have been halted, or could have wandered in a different direction so that it strayed away from the shrine instead of gathering around it.<br /> <br /> But no one did that, even though the pressure of avoiding murder or disappearance would have created a natural demand for housing as FAR away from the Shrine as possible, leading to city planning favoring distance from the shrine, until any buildings around the shrine are abandoned or inhabited only by those who cannot afford safer housing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T12:30:49-08:00","id":1294828,"title":"","content":"That could make for some really weird and intense scenes, once your players push out the Realm/Pact and finally decide to try and attain enlightenment, they find out 5 people have to die. So of course they don\u2019t want to, but then they find out that the locals are actually excited at a chance to become one with the Wood Dragon and you\u2019re left thinking these guys are insane, and maybe wondering how much you can justify with \u201cwell they do WANT it to happen...\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T12:32:54-08:00","id":1294829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1294823#post1294823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of those things are stopped by leaving, which is the crux of my point. I can continue to try and explain this but I want to be sure you're making an honest effort to understand what I'm saying rather then just repeating the same point over and over again as I explain how it's not related .</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I do understand. Your point is there's a cause of death that people can avoid by just moving out of the city.<br /> <br /> My point is there might be advantages to living there that outweigh the increased chance of death, which can't be moved, such as reduced chance of death living by a wood manse, or religious enlightenment, or, in the First Age, economic dependence on rich Lunar and Dragonblood pilgrims. And of course, the bigger the city, the lower the chance of death.<br /> <br /> I mean, it is something worth thinking about. And perhaps the book should address it. But there are possible explanations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-07-2019, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T12:36:54-08:00","id":1294833,"title":"","content":"So, with 6 days to go you guys think Lunars are going to manage to match the Dragon Bloodeds 331K after the last minute sprint of backers or will they end up losing out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T12:39:56-08:00","id":1294834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1294828#post1294828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That could make for some really weird and intense scenes, once your players push out the Realm/Pact and finally decide to try and attain enlightenment, they find out 5 people have to die. So of course they don\u2019t want to, but then they find out that the locals are actually excited at a chance to become one with the Wood Dragon and you\u2019re left thinking these guys are insane, and maybe wondering how much you can justify with \u201cwell they do WANT it to happen...\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>We had a similar conundrum recently.<br /> <br /> 2 sessions ago, there was a funeral for my previous character. Two guys volunteered to have their hearts cut out by the Zenith NPC who was raised by Dragon Kings.<br /> <br /> And you know, we don't want to make the stab-happy Zenith, who is an important ally, angry... and they volunteered to be sacrificed. I asked them why, turned out they were both pirates and wanted redemption.<br /> <br /> So... we let her. But it was super dubious.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T12:42:04-08:00","id":1294835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1294748#post1294748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's definitely another complaint. At least with the Fire Shrine, you're safe as long as you leave the city each night, and the people who live there obviously don't actually live in the part that burns, but the city around it, and only go into the Fire City during the day to conduct business.<br /> <br /> Sure, the Wood City is currently abandoned except for its monks, but what makes ALL of those monks so devoted to the shrine that they're willing to die at random at any time? I suppose it was easier when other people lived there and might die instead, but that just raises the question of why anyone was ever willing to live there.<br /> <br /> Sure, they could all just up and leave the city for their own protection every time a pilgrim manages to pass the Earth Shrine, but then they would all need to stay out of their city until the pilgrim finishes or fails her journey, and that could take days if not weeks or longer. That's a lot more inconvenient than the Fire City.<br /> <br /> The Earth, Fire, Water, and Air cities and shrines are all great, but Wood is just dumb. It's dumb.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Real life people have killed themselves for religious reasons, I therefore don't see whats hard to believe about the monks being cool with dying for religious reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T12:46:19-08:00","id":1294838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1294835#post1294835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Real life people have killed themselves for religious reasons, I therefore don't see whats hard to believe about the monks being cool with dying for religious reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>The monks are the people who remain. But the city was built and inhabited by the people the Lunars drove from the land after the Imperial Legions left.<br /> <br /> Monks don't need a whole city. Which is why the whole city is overgrown. There aren't enough of them to inhabit it all. Because it was built for a larger, general population of people NOT devoted enough to become monks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T12:47:51-08:00","id":1294839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1294833#post1294833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, with 6 days to go you guys think Lunars are going to manage to match the Dragon Bloodeds 331K after the last minute sprint of backers or will they end up losing out?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to make a thread about the sorts of characters Thousand Blade Style might allow you to play, and see if that helps us achieve the goal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T12:48:13-08:00","id":1294840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1294838#post1294838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The monks are the people who remain. But the city was built and inhabited by the people the Lunars drove from the land after the Imperial Legions left.<br /> <br /> Monks don't need a whole city. Which is why the whole city is overgrown. There aren't enough of them to inhabit it all. Because it was built for a larger, general population of people NOT devoted enough to become monks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where the people of Jonestown monks? Or the people that blow themselves up because they think it will get them a bunch of virgins in heaven? One doesn't have to make a career out of their religion to be devoted enough to die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T13:13:01-08:00","id":1294851,"title":"","content":"To be clear, I do think it is creepy as well just not that it is unrealistic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T13:17:17-08:00","id":1294854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1294834#post1294834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We had a similar conundrum recently.<br /> <br /> 2 sessions ago, there was a funeral for my previous character. Two guys volunteered to have their hearts cut out by the Zenith NPC who was raised by Dragon Kings.<br /> <br /> And you know, we don't want to make the stab-happy Zenith, who is an important ally, angry... and they volunteered to be sacrificed. I asked them why, turned out they were both pirates and wanted redemption.<br /> <br /> So... we let her. But it was super dubious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah that\u2019s cool. Does the book elaborate on the manner of enlightenment that Lunars/DBs get out of the whole thing? Does it give tempting power, or more like sage wisdom?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T13:32:17-08:00","id":1294860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1294840#post1294840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where the people of Jonestown monks?</div> </div> </div> </div>Did Jonestown communally commit suicide all at once? Seems easier to have one moment of suicidal fervor than living for generations in a city where you could die at random at any time. The more you plan for and invest in your future, the less accepting you are of a sudden and random death. It's only in being convinced to give up your future that a sudden death seems acceptable.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or the people that blow themselves up because they think it will get them a bunch of virgins in heaven? One doesn't have to make a career out of their religion to be devoted enough to die. </div> </div> </div>But as I said, if you live and pursue a career unrelated to dying, you're not keen to give it up with a random death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T13:49:38-08:00","id":1294869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1294860#post1294860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did Jonestown communally commit suicide all at once? Seems easier to have one moment of suicidal fervor than living for generations in a city where you could die at random at any time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone who lives in a city could die at random at any time. That's life. I had a boss who died in a car crash. Death is random.<br /> <br /> I mean, I get the point that there's an incentive to move, if there's somewhere safer that's easy to get too, but there's plenty of reasons people don't move from dangerous places. Maybe the Dragonblood who controlled the city paid well. Maybe the wilderness was more dangerous than the city. Maybe the population was too big for 5 people to be significant. Maybe, as DrLoveMonkey said, they see it as Ascension, rather than death. Maybe living near the wood shrine makes you less likely to die of disease.<br /> <br /> I don't know, and agree it ought to be addressed, but there are possible explanations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T14:31:35-08:00","id":1294884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1294833#post1294833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, with 6 days to go you guys think Lunars are going to manage to match the Dragon Bloodeds 331K after the last minute sprint of backers or will they end up losing out?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not reach that dollar amount, but significantly better in Backer count. It\u2019s just less per-Backer without the Realm Add-On.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T19:40:15-08:00","id":1294955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1294740#post1294740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The wood shrine's final thing once the pilgrimage is done definitely does feel silly, it's one of those 'why do you live in this otherwise totally normal city that you can find in other palaces with the understanding that sometimes you might just die for no reason.'</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't write this section, but it makes sense to me. What greater honor could there be for a mortal than to serve a crucial role in a holy pilgrimage that directly enhances the Dragon-Blooded Host? What more sacred duty could a peasant have? What sacrifice could more fully earn the respect of the community for one's surviving family members?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T19:57:15-08:00","id":1294956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1294955#post1294955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't write this section, but it makes sense to me. What greater honor could there be for a mortal than to serve a crucial role in a holy pilgrimage that directly enhances the Dragon-Blooded Host? What more sacred duty could a peasant have? What sacrifice could more fully earn the respect of the community for one's surviving family members?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would work if the people were immaculate believers but they are supposedly not by default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T20:01:57-08:00","id":1294957,"title":"","content":"Query Re:Wood Shrine.<br /> <br /> The events being described are in the past yes? In the so-called Bad Old Days of Dragonblooded occupation? The current status quo is that the Wood Shrine is under new glorious Argent leadership, and the Caulborn can heave a sigh of relief?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T20:34:35-08:00","id":1294960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1294957#post1294957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Query Re:Wood Shrine.<br /> <br /> The events being described are in the past yes? In the so-called Bad Old Days of Dragonblooded occupation? The current status quo is that the Wood Shrine is under new glorious Argent leadership, and the Caulborn can heave a sigh of relief?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, the caulborn seem to dislike the lunars just as much if not more than the dragonblooded. If the lunars do take faxai then you can expect them to start doing the pilgrimage themselves to open the mystery box, in which case more will die.<br /> <br /> Though honestly I do not see any particular issue with the Wood shrine. The caul born are said to be extremely weird so to assume they have any issue with the end of the pilgrimage is silly. Also five people do not die they disappear, while we as readers can make a possible connection that does not mean people in setting can. As far as the native population is concerned they could be fulfilling a sacred duty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T20:56:21-08:00","id":1294966,"title":"","content":"Yeah. At worst you have something of an Omelas situation where, sure, there's those who walk away from Omelas but given the weirdness of the Caul you can go so far to say that pilgramages don't even get a chance to complete unless there's five people fated to die soon. Every other time, something interferes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T23:14:30-08:00","id":1294979,"title":"","content":"These are people who get to live by the Wood Shrine! It's a religious relic with power over dreams. Of course people want to live there. It's an important location for the entire living continent.<br /> <br /> Then the people who aren't religious in that way live there because that's where everyone else is living and passing through. It's a huge place for pilgrims. Commerce and all that. If you moved five miles away, pilgrims and their bodyguards wouldn't come to you and bring their wealth. There's a legitimate reason why people would want to live there.<br /> <br /> Yeah sometimes people die and you can get sad about it. But it always happens to someone else, never to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T04:20:27-08:00","id":1295013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1294957#post1294957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Query Re:Wood Shrine.<br /> <br /> The events being described are in the past yes? In the so-called Bad Old Days of Dragonblooded occupation? The current status quo is that the Wood Shrine is under new glorious Argent leadership, and the Caulborn can heave a sigh of relief?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if being driven out of the city by beastfolk with everyone who couldn't escape being slaughtered is relief then Third Daughter of the Leaves provided.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T12:41:03-08:00","id":1295111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1294956#post1294956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would work if the people were immaculate believers but they are supposedly not by default.</div> </div> </div> </div>The caulborn also find the cities sacred, and they generally approve of pilgrims, even if they normally dislike the realm, without caring about immaculate dogma.<br /> <br /> Why do we have the assumption that people are dying all the time at the Wood Shrine? Presumably most of the kills are animals. Also, are we assuming that the rate of casual violence in this premodern setting is low enough that this city is particularly unusual with its murder rate?<br /> <br /> I'm comfortable with Garianghis being an underpopulated city of wacky religious zealots who kill and are killed occasionally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24366,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","user":"Slarn!","date":". 03-08-2019, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","name":"Slarn!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T12:45:24-08:00","id":1295112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1294803#post1294803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially when it's not &quot;five rocks fall on their own&quot; but &quot;this Dragon-Blood who threw five rocks at random people to murder them&quot;.<br /> <br /> Either no one would have wanted to live in the city back when pilgrims were frequent, or they would have actively opposed letting any pilgrim into their city to protect themselves from random murders.</div> </div> </div> </div>What makes you think that the monks who lived in the city weren't also doing the murdering? They probably engage in similar rituals as the pilgrims.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24366,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","user":"Slarn!","date":". 03-08-2019, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","name":"Slarn!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T13:44:43-08:00","id":1295118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slarn!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1295111#post1295111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The caulborn also find the cities sacred, and they generally approve of pilgrims, even if they normally dislike the realm, without caring about immaculate dogma.<br /> <br /> Why do we have the assumption that people are dying all the time at the Wood Shrine? Presumably most of the kills are animals. Also, are we assuming that the rate of casual violence in this premodern setting is low enough that this city is particularly unusual with its murder rate?<br /> <br /> I'm comfortable with Garianghis being an underpopulated city of wacky religious zealots who kill and are killed occasionally.</div> </div> </div> </div>even if the first kill is not an animal the specific thing says that when the pilgrimige is finished, five more people are killed.<br /> <br /> Because apparently there's no interesting thing about Wood as an Element besides animals killing things, which is one of the reasons it feels so lame.<br /> <br /> For all the many ways to discuss growth, death, and stuff like that in Wood, they chose killing an animal or person, then killing 5 more of them.<br /> <br /> How boring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T14:40:48-08:00","id":1295127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1295118#post1295118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> even if the first kill is not an animal the specific thing says that when the pilgrimige is finished, five more people are killed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just reread both the Lunar and the Dragon-blood versions, and I couldn't find anything that says this. Perhaps my brain fell out. What am I missing?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1295118#post1295118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because apparently there's no interesting thing about Wood as an Element besides animals killing things, which is one of the reasons it feels so lame.<br /> <br /> For all the many ways to discuss growth, death, and stuff like that in Wood, they chose killing an animal or person, then killing 5 more of them.<br /> <br /> How boring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I hope they include some other cool wood manses that are more to your taste in The Realm. My personal understanding/headcanon is that these shrines are essentially N/A Manses that are dedicated to a particular elemental dragon AND luna, and I love the irony that Realm pilgrims are fighting against Lunars so they can do a ritual that resembles a Lunar's sacred hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24366,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","user":"Slarn!","date":". 03-08-2019, 05:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","name":"Slarn!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T14:52:40-08:00","id":1295128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slarn!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1295127#post1295127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just reread both the Lunar and the Dragon-blood versions, and I couldn't find anything that says this. Perhaps my brain fell out. What am I missing?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Well, I hope they include some other cool wood manses that are more to your taste in The Realm. My personal understanding is that these shrines are essentially N/A Manses that are dedicated to a particular elemental dragon AND luna, and I love the irony that Realm pilgrims are fighting against Lunars so they can do a ritual that resembles a Lunar's sacred hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Garianghis, all residents fall into a deep sleep that lasts for a full hour, during which they<br /> dream of being hunted. When they awaken, five sleepers have vanished without a trace, and five<br /> stags lie dead before the Wood Shrine, arranged in a circle and without a mark on their bodies.<br /> <br /> Dragonblooded Preview, explaining what happens when the pilgrim finishes her quest.<br /> <br /> And unlike every other Shrine, which does something completely different from when the Pilgrim finishes her prayers there; with the Earth Shrine causing an earthquake, the Fire Shine raining Fire that does not burn, the Water Shrine draining of Water and the Air Shrine rebuilding the city for an instant, the Wood Shrine is just 'What happened before, but more so'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T14:54:22-08:00","id":1295130,"title":"","content":"Hey there! Just want y'all know that Vance and I are aware of the situation.<br /> <br /> We do appreciate this sort of feedback! We don't always agree with everything we hear, but we do listen, and we're especially happy when it spurs us on to better ideas and approaches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T14:58:48-08:00","id":1295132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1295128#post1295128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Garianghis, all residents fall into a deep sleep that lasts for a full hour, during which they<br /> dream of being hunted. When they awaken, five sleepers have vanished without a trace, and five<br /> stags lie dead before the Wood Shrine, arranged in a circle and without a mark on their bodies.<br /> <br /> Dragonblooded Preview, explaining what happens when the pilgrim finishes her quest.<br /> <br /> And unlike every other Shrine, which does something completely different from when the Pilgrim finishes her prayers there; with the Earth Shrine causing an earthquake, the Fire Shine raining Fire that does not burn, the Water Shrine draining of Water and the Air Shrine rebuilding the city for an instant, the Wood Shrine is just 'What happened before, but more so'</div> </div> </div> </div>My brain DID fall out. Thanks for the reply.<br /> That's... a shade too gruesome for my tastes as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","name":"Slarn!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T15:48:00-08:00","id":1295141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1295130#post1295130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey there! Just want y'all know that Vance and I are aware of the situation.<br /> <br /> We do appreciate this sort of feedback! We don't always agree with everything we hear, but we do listen, and we're especially happy when it spurs us on to better ideas and approaches.</div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciate that, whatever the final result is.<br /> <br /> But can you clarify whether you're suppose to lose your reflection forever or not? Or is it referring only to the alternative version of yourself?<br /> <br /> None of the other trials involve cutting off pieces of yourself, permanently or otherwise, so losing your reflection permanently seems out of place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T16:54:20-08:00","id":1295151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1295141#post1295141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of the other trials involve cutting off pieces of yourself, permanently or otherwise, so losing your reflection permanently seems out of place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Losing your reflection makes it much harder for Lunars to impersonate you, something very valuable for paranoid Dynasts, as well as protecting you from some malevolent magic like the spell Shadow Summons back from 2e. This is a boon as much as a cost.<br /> <br /> It'd also be an undeniable mark of prestige in realm society, since it proves you completed the pilgrimage. Just think of how that changes the life (&amp; marriage prospects) of a peasant who does that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","name":"Slarn!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T19:45:05-08:00","id":1295187,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, it also makes it hard to see if you have something stuck in your teeth and are probably going to forget what your face looks like in a few years unless you get a hyper-realistic painting made or something (and that wont let you keep track of any changes that happen). So definitely something of a trade off there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T23:08:24-08:00","id":1295221,"title":"","content":"I think if the final version of the Wood Shrine is as-printed, my house rule is that those who vanish are always among the most devout or those seeking a (small-i) immaculate rebirth - it doesn't kill random people, there is some degree of spiritual consent involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T23:38:05-08:00","id":1295229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1295130#post1295130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey there! Just want y'all know that Vance and I are aware of the situation.<br /> <br /> We do appreciate this sort of feedback! We don't always agree with everything we hear, but we do listen, and we're especially happy when it spurs us on to better ideas and approaches.</div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciate the way you guys listen. Sometimes, you know, people just are whining on the internet, which can mean game developers just ignore the whole thing, but other times a few small tweaks can improve things. And crowd-storming can work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T00:55:24-08:00","id":1295258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1295187#post1295187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, it also makes it hard to see if you have something stuck in your teeth and are probably going to forget what your face looks like in a few years unless you get a hyper-realistic painting made or something (and that wont let you keep track of any changes that happen). So definitely something of a trade off there.</div> </div> </div> </div>What suffering it is to be a Prince of the Earth! To think you'd have to sit for your portrait every other decade!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","name":"Slarn!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T01:11:51-08:00","id":1295260,"title":"","content":"I just have to say... Lunar Strength is everything I wanted from Lunar Strength.<br /> <br /> Simple, straightforward, and <b>brutal. </b>I'm definitely gonna make a Full Moon this weekend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T02:02:43-08:00","id":1295266,"title":"","content":"There's a Strength 2 charm with no prereqs for throwing scenery at people. <br /> And in fact loads of stuff for wrecking scenery, throwing people around, etc. Should make for really fun fights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T06:22:00-08:00","id":1295295,"title":"","content":"The problem I see with the Wood Shrine is that <b>everyone</b> collapses and dreams of being hunted then at the end five people are gone forever. So the comparison to random deaths in city living doesn't hold water for me, it's like throwing lots to see who gets fed to the minotaur.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T08:25:21-08:00","id":1295320,"title":"","content":"And here I was thinking of Xuthal of the Dusk, where the vile amorphous god of titular Xuthal slithered about its city, devouring people when the mood struck it\u2026 so the people there turned to the black lotus for escapism, instead of just fleeing the city.<br /> <br /> People are weird animals, and even knowing that something could arbitrarily kill someone isn't always enough to get them to leave. My grandpa lives pretty much directly where the wildfires are blazing through California, and no one in my family's been able to persuade him to leave his home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T09:28:16-08:00","id":1295329,"title":"","content":"on a different track, I think there's only two charms in the new set I think are a bit weird.<br /> <br /> I think Chain-Breaking Fury is a bit iffy towards the idea that if someone has socially influenced you, you've been hypnotized and brainwashed. I don't think the actual power is that powerful or broken; the idea that when you've been persuaded to do something you reconsider when you see it's against something else you care about isn't too bad, but the idea that the fluff describes it as becoming furious at the idea that you were 'used' or 'deceived' and that you immediately get a Major intimacy of Rage feels, to me, like it's pushing the envelope on what the social system means, which feels like a step back from the Psyche keyword, which is clearly used to differentiate between simply being good at persuading someone and magically debilitating their ability to resist. <br /> <br /> The second charm is Wound-Mastering Body Evolution. For a charm that makes you immune to Withering Damage, it feels like the cost of the continuing effect is pretty meaningless. It's meant to be a reflection of Aegis of Invincible Might, but it's probably way better. Both essentially make you immune to Withering Damage (the effects are slightly different, but both roughly give you 10 soak and then a way to ignore Overwhelming. The major benefit of Aegis here is that it also helps you against Post-Soak Damage, but Lunars have other charms to help prevent that), and 20 Hardness.<br /> <br /> Their activation requirements are somewhat similar, enough I don't think there's one that's easier then the other. It activates when the Exalt takes a Decisive Attack; for Lunars, they take the damage, for a Solar, they activate Adamant Skin Technique. Neither character can be crashed (as both are Perilous), so they both, realistically, can be activated multiple times per combat without too much issue, since Adamant Skin Technique doesn't actually have a reset condition, while Lunars are excellent at taking some Decisive Damage but making sure it's only a small amount. The only major thing to look at, to me, is the cost; Since Aegis is Permanent, it doesn't have a cost, but Adamant Skin has a cost of 8m, meaning you need to pay 8m to activate Aegis. Wound Mastering Body Evolution is only 6m, 1wp. However, since Adamant Skin is it's own charm, it's not really that different.<br /> <br /> However, Aegis of Invincible Might has far more requirements; you have to Decisively attack every turn, or pay 8 motes on combat charms, and if you stop making Combat Actions at all, the charm immediately ends. This means the Exalt is either spending a massive amount of Motes per round- surpassing normal mote regen-, or having to make a bunch of Decisive attacks at 3 Initiative. This means they may not be able to penetrate Hardness, or the damage they're doing is very minuscule (we're ignoring the powerful combos with Brawl here, because then we would need to get into how Wound Mastering combines with other Stamina and Strength Charms and the like, and those combos are, I would argue, pretty potent themselves), and that they're at risk of Crash themselves if someone has post-soak damage adders or similar. Meanwhile, the requirement for Wound-Mastering Body Evolution is...you pay 1 Initiative per turn. It just doesn't feel like a fair payment for a charm clearly supposed to be the same style of effect; there's far fewer requirements on the Exalt's actions, and the drip is minuscule, not even costing motes at all. So long as a Lunar can effectively hit a foe, or gain Initiative through dodging or repelling their attacks through their Stamina or Dexterity trees, Wound Mastering Body Evolution puts no requirements on the Lunar to play any differently then they did before, a decision I feel is questionable for an incredibly powerful charm, even if the Solar version is more broad in applying to every attack, while the Lunars only have this effect against a single person.<br /> <br /> However, I may not be looking at this in the correct way, and I'm curious what others thing about these two charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T10:03:17-08:00","id":1295338,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">&quot;As the Lunar realizes how she\u2019s been deceived or used, a terrible wrath fills her heart.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> This description doesn't look like hypnotism to me. I think Chain-Breaking Fury just models an exalted extension of a natural emotional reaction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","name":"Slarn!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T10:03:32-08:00","id":1295339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slarn!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1295258#post1295258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What suffering it is to be a Prince of the Earth! To think you'd have to sit for your portrait every other decade!</div> </div> </div> </div>Its probably hard to find retainers trustworthy enough that you allow them constant access to your neck with a sharp blade to shave for you because you can't see yourself in the mirror to do it well yourself. Or if you get slashed across the face by a lunar you need someone else around to tell you what color it is turning to see what kind of poison the vile anathema hit you with. Its a serious sacrifice in terms of a bunch of really helpful small utilities that add up quick. Granted a lot of them can be mitigated by having trustworthy servants you trust not to gank you or put clown makeup on you and humiliate you when you show up to the latest Cynis party.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T10:04:09-08:00","id":1295340,"title":"","content":"While reading Sha'a Oka entry on the Manuscript preview 1, I find difficult to reconciliate the first and third paragraphes as he is supposed to be &quot;Born into the many wars of the Shogunate&quot; but also being &quot;one of the many on the Caul when it vanished shortly after the Usurpation&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25116-daiklave","name":"Daiklave","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T10:04:46-08:00","id":1295341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slarn!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1295338#post1295338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">&quot;As the Lunar realizes how she\u2019s been deceived or used, a terrible wrath fills her heart.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> This description doesn't look like hypnotism to me. I think Chain-Breaking Fury just models an exalted extension of a natural emotional reaction.</div> </div> </div> </div>it's within the description and how it's read or can be read as 'the Lunar realizes someone convinced them to do something, and is now incredibly angry at them for it'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T10:06:24-08:00","id":1295342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1295320#post1295320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And here I was thinking of Xuthal of the Dusk, where the vile amorphous god of titular Xuthal slithered about its city, devouring people when the mood struck it\u2026 so the people there turned to the black lotus for escapism, instead of just fleeing the city.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Conan stories, while a solid foundation for a lot of fantasy work indulge in a lot of racial profiling to justify why people behave the way they do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T10:22:18-08:00","id":1295345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1295320#post1295320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And here I was thinking of Xuthal of the Dusk, where the vile amorphous god of titular Xuthal slithered about its city, devouring people when the mood struck it\u2026 so the people there turned to the black lotus for escapism, instead of just fleeing the city.<br /> <br /> People are weird animals, and even knowing that something could arbitrarily kill someone isn't always enough to get them to leave. My grandpa lives pretty much directly where the wildfires are blazing through California, and no one in my family's been able to persuade him to leave his home.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is gonna be my last post on this because at this point this thread has been talking about this for the better part of a week, two new previews have come out, and we're still arguing about the Wood Shrine. There's people who think it's dumb and there's people who think it's not, and no one is gonna budge an inch. So I'm just gonna highlight why I think it's dumb one last time and then not talk about it again.<br /> <br /> 1: One person dying to a person in a dream isn't beyond the pale. The Lottery is a good example of this; it's a singular act for an instant that informs a community. It becomes dumb when it's not 1 person once, but rather 2 times for one person; once 1 person, then again with 5 more. At that point it just comes off as silly and too grim; it's not someone refuisng to move because 'hey, everyone dies in car crashes all the time, whatcha gonna do?', it's 'if we took our city and moved it 5 feet to the left, no one would ever die to a lightning strike ever again. But that's too much effort.'<br /> <br /> 2: It's easy to ignore or rationalize one person dying to a person hunting them down and ripping their throat out. It's less so when everyone falls into a dream, dreams of being hunted down, then 5 people die. in your fire analogies or whatever else, it's 'well, it sucks for them but at least it didn't happen to me'. in this sequence, it's more like everyone sees their home burn down and you have to hope you're one of the lucky ones whose Insurance policy kicks in and pays out for it.<br /> <br /> 3: It's boring. All the other shrines have two distinct effects; the challenge and what occurs during it, and the after effect when the pilgrim completes their journey. These are, for every other shrine, completely distinct effects that are totally different and have entirely different reactions. The Wood Shrine does not have this. Instead, the same thing happens again, but it kills more people. This isn't very interesting, and seems to speak of an idea that for a Wood based action, there was difficulty thinking of something interesting happening, and instead they just went 'Blood and Claw!' then paused and went 'BLOOD AND CLAW!', but louder. Why not, instead, when the pilgrim finishes their journey, millions of fantastical flowers bloom across the city, filling it with beautiful sights and smells, before they wither away at the day's end. Or perhaps the nearby animals enter the city without fear, and rather then hunting down humans, celebrate festivities with them, with wolves letting children ride on their backs or boars dancing in the street, and then at the day's end, they return to the wilds and the 'natural' order of the world resumes? These both highlight Wood ideas; the cycle of life, the interaction between Man and Nature, but do so in ways that isn't just 'predator and prey' and then 'predator and prey, but more so'.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T11:03:33-08:00","id":1295351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daiklave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1295340#post1295340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While reading Sha'a Oka entry on the Manuscript preview 1, I find difficult to reconciliate the first and third paragraphes as he is supposed to be &quot;Born into the many wars of the Shogunate&quot; but also being &quot;one of the many on the Caul when it vanished shortly after the Usurpation&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wondered this too, so I asked about it.<br /> <br /> They said, basically, he was born in the wars of the very early Shogunate, while the Dragonblood were fighting over what to do now the Solars were gone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T13:18:34-08:00","id":1295379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daiklave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1295340#post1295340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While reading Sha'a Oka entry on the Manuscript preview 1, I find difficult to reconciliate the first and third paragraphes as he is supposed to be &amp;quot;Born into the many wars of the Shogunate&amp;quot; but also being &amp;quot;one of the many on the Caul when it vanished shortly after the Usurpation&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>While i\u2019m not a fan of that timeline decision, it isn\u2019t a contradiction. You could have a century there between his Exaltation and disappearance and still be accurate.<br /> <br /> That said, I\u2019m inclined to make Sha\u2019a Ok\u2019a have been a thorn in the Shogunate\u2019s side for almost its entire history, and the Caul to have vanished when the Wyld crashed in in the Balorian Crusade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T19:32:31-08:00","id":1295444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1295341#post1295341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's within the description and how it's read or can be read as 'the Lunar realizes someone convinced them to do something, and is now incredibly angry at them for it'</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, if you want to talk references to 2e memes Dragon-Blooded literally have a \u201cJoin Battle to not get Psyched\u201d Charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T10:33:16-07:00","id":1295581,"title":"","content":"Is there any kind of break in the shipping costs when ordering multiple books? If so I'm willing to pick up an additional book or two for people in the UK and possibly Europe who are otherwise wincing at the thought of paying an exta $50.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T11:36:17-07:00","id":1295594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1295444#post1295444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, if you want to talk references to 2e memes Dragon-Blooded literally have a \u201cJoin Battle to not get Psyched\u201d Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I specifically pointed out that the reason I brought this charm up was because it reacted to all influence like this, not Psyche effects only.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T13:11:54-07:00","id":1295615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1295581#post1295581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any kind of break in the shipping costs when ordering multiple books? If so I'm willing to pick up an additional book or two for people in the UK and possibly Europe who are otherwise wincing at the thought of paying an exta $50.</div> </div> </div> </div>That might be something to ask James Bell or Rich Thomas about via the Kickstarter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T19:03:45-07:00","id":1296299,"title":"","content":"I am pretty excited about all the new animals, my current character (wood aspect) actually has a Elk mount (we were using horse stats) so that is pretty fun! Also we are only a little about 2,000$ before we hit Sublime danger which is exciting.<br /> <br /> I find it strange that some of the custom charms/QC characters/animal/artifact slots are still open. I really wanted to buy a Charm during DB but I was buying a car at the time and now this time around I am having a patio installed. That and I can't really think of any charms for Lunars that really are 'wham-pow-awesome' to add. <br /> <br /> I have to say in the past, I have not been a Lunars fan. However this Kickstarter really turned me around on them. In 3e they seem 100 kinds of awesome. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T19:14:24-07:00","id":1296302,"title":"","content":"Hopefully we are able to make it to 300K and get them that bonus, but I think it would need to further pick up the pace to make it in the time we have left.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T19:22:06-07:00","id":1296306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1296302#post1296302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hopefully we are able to make it to 300K and get them that bonus, but I think it would need to further pick up the pace to make it in the time we have left.</div> </div> </div> </div>I sadly have to agree, I think we will make the 270,000 mark but not much more than that. Which is sad because this is a excellent book and I think the devs &amp; writers deserve a nice bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T19:26:25-07:00","id":1296311,"title":"","content":"Nah, we are only a little over a thousand away from that right now so we are definitely hitting 270K. I think at the current rate we might just barely manage to scrape in 290K. But thats assuming it doesn't further speed up in the very final hour. We might maybe hit 300K.<br /> <br /> For the record, right now we are at $268,971","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T20:17:13-07:00","id":1296318,"title":"","content":"Uh...<br /> <br /> Reading the previews, I get to Raksi, and, uh, I'm looking at her Intimacies, and I see a highly narcissistic woman who is utterly dedicated to the destruction of an archrival that humiliated and scarred her (emotionally), leading her to becoming a near-faceless dictator, sorceress, and scholar-queen who is beloved and feared by her people, absolutely loathed outside of her circle of intimates, and prone to histrionics both to intimidate and for the sheer grandeur of it all, and who both calls herself a villain and beyond mere simplistic morality, and cares more for having a personal dominion than ruling it.<br /> <br /> It's weird. I swear I've seen this before somewhere...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1