forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T19:49:22-07:00","id":1297128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1296318#post1296318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh...<br /> <br /> Reading the previews, I get to Raksi, and, uh, I'm looking at her Intimacies, and I see a highly narcissistic woman who is utterly dedicated to the destruction of an archrival that humiliated and scarred her (emotionally), leading her to becoming a near-faceless dictator, sorceress, and scholar-queen who is beloved and feared by her people, absolutely loathed outside of her circle of intimates, and prone to histrionics both to intimidate and for the sheer grandeur of it all, and who both calls herself a villain and beyond mere simplistic morality, and cares more for having a personal dominion than ruling it.<br /> <br /> It's weird. I swear I've seen this before somewhere...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>... and now Rakshi needs to exclusively refer to herself in the third person.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T20:48:24-07:00","id":1297136,"title":"","content":"The one thing in the assessment I'd disagree with is the emotional scarring; I don't read Raksi's response to the Usurpation as traumatised so much as pragmatically considerate of the fact that she's faced with a world-spanning enemy who wants to kill her. She otherwise seems super into the kind of person that fighting that made her into.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1297128#post1297128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... and now Rakshi needs to exclusively refer to herself in the third person.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been thinking that her general style of address in the Total Control Zone would be some Eastern word that translates out to Queen of Fangs, but find the idea that Raksi expects to be identified by her Tell and general demeanour means that she foregoes any self-reference that would give her away.<br /> <br /> But maybe that would just be something before somebody addressing her makes the correct propitiation and address.<br /> <br /> The references to her as erudite and frustrated by lack of people to converse with recalls to me my notion that Raksi insistently speaks in Old Realm as it was during the during the end of the First Age, within which I'd model her as basically having a personal pronoun exclusively for her own use, ala the Japanese emperor.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T21:31:59-07:00","id":1297150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1297136#post1297136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one thing in the assessment I'd disagree with is the emotional scarring; I don't read Raksi's response to the Usurpation as traumatised so much as pragmatically considerate of the fact that she's faced with a world-spanning enemy who wants to kill her. She otherwise seems super into the kind of person that fighting that made her into.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I've been thinking that her general style of address in the Total Control Zone would be some Eastern word that translates out to Queen of Fangs, but find the idea that Raksi expects to be identified by her Tell and general demeanour means that she foregoes any self-reference that would give her away.<br /> <br /> But maybe that would just be something before somebody addressing her makes the correct propitiation and address.<br /> <br /> The references to her as erudite and frustrated by lack of people to converse with recalls to me my notion that Raksi insistently speaks in Old Realm as it was during the during the end of the First Age, within which I'd model her as basically having a personal pronoun exclusively for her own use, ala the Japanese emperor.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, the Queen of Fangs would have, say, a one or two syllable word that basically translates to &quot;She who is the Queen of Fangs&quot; and might be represented in gameplay by people calling her the Queen of Fangs all the time? Or, if Queen of Fangs is too long, I suppose one could use an English word(s) with an appropriate meaning, such as Feared One or Dread or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T22:43:44-07:00","id":1297160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287120-lunars-kickstarter-is-live?p=1297150#post1297150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, the Queen of Fangs would have, say, a one or two syllable word that basically translates to &quot;She who is the Queen of Fangs&quot; and might be represented in gameplay by people calling her the Queen of Fangs all the time? Or, if Queen of Fangs is too long, I suppose one could use an English word(s) with an appropriate meaning, such as Feared One or Dread or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I was in a position to do so, my inclination would be to decide on an appropriate language and try to find an approximation of how the term might translate into that, and try to come up with a word that sounds like a compound or evolved form of it.<br /> <br /> Something that might capture the feel of how the Roman name Caesar (a word of uncertain etymology even by the time of the most famous Gaius Julius) eventually evolves into the Russian title czar, modified by time and the language conventions of the people adopting it.<br /> <br /> In this conception, &quot;Queen of Fangs&quot; would still be the general term for referring to Raksi from a distance, invoking her reputation and what she's been known to do, and referencing her adopted moniker as it translates into their own languages, much as titles for different polities might get revised to be familiar to a given speaker. She gets called that rather than just something more prosaic like the queen of Mahalanka, both because that implies a legitimacy that most competing powers don't want to give to her, and from the general perspective that a Lunar who has actually managed to build up and maintain a sizable sovereign territory in open defiance of the Realm warrants something more distinct and fearsome. I'm imagining that in the minds of most speakers, a comprehensible approximation of Raksi's own fearsome moniker conveys the impression that she's openly displaying herself as an evil monster. Whereas the inhabitants of Mahalanka and its surroundings would refer to her by her formal title, and doing so if ever addressing her (with the possible exception of members of the Silver Pact who can get away with calling her shahan-ya) is a good idea.<br /> <br /> It's like how you don't style yourself as Dark Lord if you don't have a particular message to send.<br /> <br /> But that's just me. I'm sure that in most cases, the point that people under her authority use the title Queen of Fangs all the time would convey the necessary gravitas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}